,500 -4,200)= 300,000 +9,300 =309,300 -189 =309,111. Yep, same result.\n\nTherefore, all methods converge to 309,111. So I think that's correct. I don't see any errors in my calculations now. Initially, I was worried when I thought there might be a discrepancy, but upon checking, everything lines up. So the product of 493 and 627 is 309,111.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 493 and 627 is \\boxed{309111}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 493 and 627, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify using the difference of squares method.\n\n### Step-by-Step Multiplication:\n1. **Multiply 493 by 7 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   493 \\times 7 = 3451\n   \\]\n2. **Multiply 493 by 20 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   493 \\times 2 = 986 \\quad \\text{(then add a zero)} \\quad 9860\n   \\]\n3. **Multiply 493 by 600 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   493 \\times 6 = 2958 \\quad \\text{(then add two zeros)} \\quad 295800\n   \\]\n4. **Add the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   3451 + 9860 + 295800\n   \\]\n   - First, add \\(3451 + 9860\\):\n     \\[\n     3451 + 9860 = 13311\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to \\(295800\\):\n     \\[\n     13311 + 295800 = 309111\n     \\]\n\n### Verification Using Difference of Squares:\n1. Recognize that \\(493\\) and \\(627\\) are equidistant from 560:\n   \\[\n   493 = 560 - 67 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 627 = 560 + 67\n   \\]\n2. Apply the identity \\((a - b)(a + b) = a^2 - b^2\\):\n   \\[\n   (560 - 67)(560 + 67) = 560^2 - 67^2\n   \\]\n3. Calculate each term:\n   - \\(560^2 = 313600\\)\n   - \\(67^2 = 4489\\)\n4. Subtract the squares:\n   \\[\n   313600 - 4489 = 309111\n   \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 493 and 627 is \\(\\boxed{309111}\\).",
