ultiply (1000 - 22)(400 + 35) = 1000\u00d7400 + 1000\u00d735 -22\u00d7400 -22\u00d735.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n1000\u00d7400 = 400,000.\n\n1000\u00d735 = 35,000.\n\n-22\u00d7400 = -8,800.\n\n-22\u00d735 = -770.\n\nAdding them all up:\n\n400,000 + 35,000 = 435,000.\n\n435,000 - 8,800 = 426,200.\n\n426,200 - 770 = 425,430. So that matches the previous result. Good, that's a good check.\n\nTherefore, the product of 978 and 435 is indeed 425,430.\n\nWait, just to be thorough, let me do the multiplication in another way. Let me try using the standard algorithm again but more carefully.\n\nMultiplying 978 \u00d7 435.\n\nStart with 5 (units place):\n\n978 \u00d75:\n\n8\u00d75=40, write 0 carryover 4.\n\n7\u00d75=35 +4=39, write 9 carryover 3.\n\n9\u00d75=45 +3=48, write 48.\n\nSo partial product is 4890. Correct.\n\nNext, 3 (tens place):\n\n978 \u00d73. Since it's the tens place, we'll shift one position left.\n\n8\u00d73=24, write 4 carryover 2.\n\n7\u00d73=21 +2=23, write 3 carryover 2.\n\n9\u00d73=27 +2=29, write 29.\n\nSo partial product is 2934, but shifted left one becomes 29340. Correct.\n\nThen 4 (hundreds place):\n\n978 \u00d74, shifted two left.\n\n8\u00d74=32, write 2 carryover 3.\n\n7\u00d74=28 +3=31, write 1 carryover 3.\n\n9\u00d74=36 +3=39, write 39.\n\nPartial product is 3912, shifted two left becomes 391200. Correct.\n\nAdding them all up:\n\n4890\n\n29340\n\n391200\n\nAdding the first two gives 4890 +29340 = 34230.\n\nThen 34230 +391200 = 425,430. Yep, same as before.\n\nTherefore, confident that the answer is 425,430.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using calculator verification, but since I can't use a calculator, the cross-check with different methods gives me confidence. So the final answer should be 425,430.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 978 and 435 is \\boxed{425430}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 978 and 435, we use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here are the key steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 978 by 5 (units place of 435):**\n   \\[\n   978 \\times 5 = 4890\n   \\]\n   Partial product: 4890\n\n2. **Multiply 978 by 30 (tens place of 435):**\n   \\[\n   978 \\times 3 = 2934 \\quad \\text{(then shift one position left)}\n   \\]\n   Partial product: 29340\n\n3. **Multiply 978 by 400 (hundreds place of 435):**\n   \\[\n   978 \\times 4 = 3912 \\quad \\text{(then shift two positions left)}\n   \\]\n   Partial product: 391200\n\n4. **Add all partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   4890 + 29340 + 391200\n   \\]\n   - First, add 4890 and 29340:\n     \\[\n     4890 + 29340 = 34230\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to 391200:\n     \\[\n     34230 + 391200 = 425430\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 978 and 435 is \\(\\boxed{425430}\\).",
