al Answer**\nThe product of 731 and 962 is \\boxed{703222}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 731 and 962, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm by breaking down the multiplication into partial products and then summing them up.\n\nFirst, we calculate the partial products:\n\n1. **Multiplying by 2 (units place of 962):**\n   \\[\n   731 \\times 2 = 1462\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiplying by 60 (tens place of 962):**\n   \\[\n   731 \\times 6 = 4386 \\quad \\text{(then add a zero)} \\quad 43860\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiplying by 900 (hundreds place of 962):**\n   \\[\n   731 \\times 9 = 6579 \\quad \\text{(then add two zeros)} \\quad 657900\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the partial products:\n\n1. **Adding the first two partial products:**\n   \\[\n   1462 + 43860 = 45322\n   \\]\n\n2. **Adding the result to the third partial product:**\n   \\[\n   45322 + 657900 = 703222\n   \\]\n\nTo verify, we can use another method by breaking down the numbers:\n- \\(731 = 700 + 31\\)\n- \\(731 \\times 962 = (700 + 31) \\times 962\\)\n- Calculating separately:\n  - \\(700 \\times 962 = 673400\\)\n  - \\(31 \\times 962 = 29822\\)\n- Summing these results:\n  \\[\n  673400 + 29822 = 703222\n  \\]\n\nAdditionally, verifying through division confirms the result:\n- \\(703222 \\div 731 = 962\\)\n\nThus, the product of 731 and 962 is \\(\\boxed{703222}\\).",
