he results together.\n\nFirst, we express the numbers as:\n\\[\n403 = 400 + 3\n\\]\n\\[\n616 = 600 + 16\n\\]\n\nUsing the distributive property:\n\\[\n(400 + 3)(600 + 16) = 400 \\times 600 + 400 \\times 16 + 3 \\times 600 + 3 \\times 16\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term separately:\n1. \\(400 \\times 600 = 240000\\)\n2. \\(400 \\times 16 = 6400\\)\n3. \\(3 \\times 600 = 1800\\)\n4. \\(3 \\times 16 = 48\\)\n\nAdding all these results together:\n\\[\n240000 + 6400 + 1800 + 48\n\\]\n\nStep-by-step addition:\n1. \\(240000 + 6400 = 246400\\)\n2. \\(246400 + 1800 = 248200\\)\n3. \\(248200 + 48 = 248248\\)\n\nTo verify, we can also use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n    403 \\\\\n  \\times 616 \\\\\n  \\hline\n    2418 & \\text{(403 \u00d7 6)} \\\\\n   4030  & \\text{(403 \u00d7 10)} \\\\\n+241800 & \\text{(403 \u00d7 600)} \\\\\n\\hline\n  248248 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 403 and 616 is \\(\\boxed{248248}\\).",
