ent.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I can compute 742 \u00d7 131 as follows:\n\nFirst compute 742 \u00d7 100 = 74,200,\n\nThen 742 \u00d7 30 = 22,260,\n\nThen 742 \u00d7 1 = 742,\n\nAdd them all: same as before. So that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe compute 742 \u00d7 131 by breaking 131 into 130 +1,\n\nSo 742\u00d7130 +742\u00d71,\n\n742\u00d7130 = 742\u00d710\u00d713 = 7,420 \u00d713,\n\nHmm, maybe that complicates more. Let me see:\n\n7,420 \u00d710 is 74,200, so 7,420 \u00d713:\n\n7,420 \u00d710 =74,200,\n\n7,420 \u00d73 =22,260,\n\nAdding those gives 74,200 +22,260 =96,460,\n\nThen add the 742\u00d71=742,\n\nTotal: 96,460 +742 = 97,202. Yep, same answer.\n\nSo that's the same as before. So that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, using another method, perhaps cross-multiplication?\n\nWait, let me try multiplying 742 \u00d7131 directly:\n\nFirst, 742 \u00d71 (units place): 742,\n\nThen 742 \u00d73 (tens place, so shifted one): 2,226 shifted one is 22,260,\n\nThen 742 \u00d71 (hundreds place, shifted two): 742 shifted two is 74,200,\n\nAdding those gives the same.\n\nAlternatively, I can also do 131 \u00d7 742, which is the same thing.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps to check with a calculator? Wait, since I can't use a calculator, but maybe approximate the answer to see if it's reasonable.\n\n131 is about 130, 742 is about 740.\n\n130 \u00d7740 = 130\u00d7700 +130\u00d740 = 91,000 + 5,200 = 96,200. Our answer was 97,202, which is a bit higher, which makes sense because we rounded down both numbers. Since 131 is 1 more than 130 and 742 is 2 more than 740, so the difference would be (1\u00d7740)+(2\u00d7130) + (1\u00d72) = 740 +260 +2= 1,002. So 96,200 +1,002= 97,202. Exactly. So that approximation checks out perfectly. Therefore, this gives me more confidence.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 97,202. Wait, but let me check once again step-by-step the addition of the partial products.\n\nFirst partial product: 742,\n\nSecond: 22,260,\n\nThird: 74,200.\n\nAdding first and second: 742 +22,260.\n\nLet me do 742 +22,260:\n\n22,260 +700 =22,960,\n\n22,960 +42 =23,002. Yes.\n\n23,002 +74,200:\n\n23,002 +70,000 =93,002,\n\n93,002 +4,200 =97,202. Correct.\n\nTherefore, the product is indeed 97,202.\n\nBut just to ensure I didn't make a mistake in the initial multiplication steps:\n\nCalculating 742 \u00d730:\n\n742 \u00d73=2,226, so times 10 is 22,260. Correct.\n\n742 \u00d7100 =74,200. Correct.\n\nSo all steps check out. Therefore, I think the answer is correct.\n\nAnother way: Let me try multiplying 742 \u00d7131 directly step by step.\n\nMultiplying 742 by 1 (units digit of 131):\n\n742 \u00d71 = 742.\n\nThen multiplying 742 by 3 (tens digit, so it's 30), so 742 \u00d73 =2,226, and since it's the tens place, we write it shifted one position to the left: 22,260.\n\nThen multiplying 742 by 1 (hundreds digit, so 100), giving 74,200, shifted two positions left.\n\nAdding all three gives 742 +22,260 =23,002; then 23,002 +74,200 =97,202. Yep.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I can compute using another multiplication technique, like the Russian peasant method? Let's see, but that might be more time-consuming.\n\nAlternatively, let me try using the standard algorithm again but writing it out step by step.\n\nMultiplying 742 \u00d7131:\n\nFirst, write 742,\n\n\u00d7131,\n\n------------.\n\nStart with the 1 (units place of 131):\n\nMultiply 1 \u00d7742: 742.\n\nWrite that down.\n\nNext, the 3 (tens place, so 30), multiply 3 \u00d7742:\n\n3\u00d72=6,\n\n3\u00d74=12,\n\n3\u00d77=21,\n\nSo starting from the right:\n\n3\u00d72 is 6,\n\n3\u00d74=12, write down 2, carryover 1,\n\n3\u00d77=21 plus the 1 is 22. So the result is 2226. Since it's the tens place, shift one to the left, so 22260.\n\nThird, the 1 (hundreds place, so 100), multiply 1 \u00d7742 =742, shifted two places left, so 74200.\n\nAdding all three: 742 +22260 +74200 =97,202. Same result.\n\nTherefore, after multiple checks, I believe the answer is correct. So the product of 131 and 742 is 97,202. I'll double-check once more.\n\nWait, just to ensure I didn't make any arithmetic errors in multiplying 742 by 3:\n\n700\u00d73=2100,\n\n40\u00d73=120,\n\n2\u00d73=6,\n\nAdding those: 2100+120=2220,\n\n2220+6=2226. Correct. So 3\u00d7742 is indeed 2226, so shifted becomes 22,260. Yes.\n\n100\u00d7742 is 74,200. Correct.\n\nAdding all three partial products gives 97,202. So I think that's solid.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 97,202. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 131 and 742 is \\boxed{97202}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 131 and 742, we use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 742 by 1 (units place of 131):**\n   \\[\n   742 \\times 1 = 742\n   \\]\n   This is the first partial product.\n\n2. **Multiply 742 by 3 (tens place of 131, which represents 30):**\n   \\[\n   742 \\times 3 = 2226\n   \\]\n   Since this is the tens place, we shift the result one position to the left:\n   \\[\n   2226 \\times 10 = 22260\n   \\]\n   This is the second partial product.\n\n3. **Multiply 742 by 1 (hundreds place of 131, which represents 100):**\n   \\[\n   742 \\times 1 = 742\n   \\]\n   Since this is the hundreds place, we shift the result two positions to the left:\n   \\[\n   742 \\times 100 = 74200\n   \\]\n   This is the third partial product.\n\n4. **Add all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n      \\quad 742 \\\\\n    + 22260 \\\\\n    +74200 \\\\\n    \\hline\n     97202 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\n   - Adding the first two partial products:\n     \\[\n     742 + 22260 = 23002\n     \\]\n   - Adding the result to the third partial product:\n     \\[\n     23002 + 74200 = 97202\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 131 and 742 is \\(\\boxed{97202}\\).",
