50 = 100 (Wait, maybe this isn't the best way). Alternatively, adding digit by digit:.\n\n8280.\n\n+1656.\n\n=?.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\n0 + 6 = 6.\n\n8 + 5 = 13, write down 3, carryover 1.\n\n2 + 6 + 1 = 9.\n\n8 + 1 = 9.\n\nSo that gives 9936. Okay, so 1656 + 8280 is indeed 9936.\n\nNow, add that to 496,800. So 9936 + 496,800. Let's see:.\n\n496,800 + 9,936.\n\nAdding the thousands: 496,800 + 9,000 = 505,800. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
