\n183,200 + 10,000 = 193,200.\n\n193,200 + 992 = 194,192. Yep, same answer.\n\nHmm, so all methods are leading me to 194,192. Maybe that is correct. Let me see if I can find any mistake in my initial steps.\n\nWait, perhaps I should check with a calculator? Since I can't use a calculator, but maybe do another verification.\n\nLet me compute 212 \u00d7 916.\n\nLet me compute 212 \u00d7 900 = 190,800. Then 212 \u00d7 16 = ?\n\n212 \u00d710=2120, 212 \u00d76=1272. Adding those gives 2120+1272=3392.\n\nSo total is 190,800 + 3,392 = 194,192. Yep, same.\n\nAlternatively, let me try multiplying 916 \u00d7200 = 183,200.\n\n916 \u00d712 = ?\n\n916 \u00d710 = 9,160.\n\n916 \u00d72 = 1,832.\n\nSo 9,160 + 1,832 = 10,992.\n\nAdding to 183,200 gives 183,200 +10,992 = 194,192.\n\nSame result again.\n\nHmm, so all the different ways I try, I get 194,192. Therefore, I think that is correct. Wait, but I want to make sure that perhaps in my first step, when I multiplied 212 by 9, I didn't make an error.\n\nLet me recalculate 212 \u00d79:\n\n2\u00d79=18, so units digit 8, carryover 1.\n\n1\u00d79=9 +1=10, so write 0 and carryover 1.\n\n2\u00d79=18 +1=19, so digits 19. So total is 1908. Correct. So 212 \u00d79 is indeed 1908, so \u00d7100 is 190,800.\n\nOkay, so that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can compute 212 \u00d7916 by adding 212\u00d7900 and 212\u00d716 as before, but let me check 212\u00d716 again.\n\n212 \u00d716:\n\nBreak it down as 212\u00d710=2120, and 212\u00d76=1272. Adding them gives 2120+1272.\n\n2120+1200=3320, then +72=3392. Correct.\n\nSo, adding to 190,800 gives 194,192. So yes, seems correct.\n\nTherefore, I think the product of 212 and 916 is 194,192.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 212 and 916 is \\boxed{194192}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 212 and 916, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm by breaking it down into partial products:\n\n1. **Multiply 212 by 6 (units place of 916):**\n   \\[\n   212 \\times 6 = 1272\n   \\]\n\n2. **Mult