ation step by step again:\n\nMultiplying 419 by 495.\n\nLet me write it out as:\n\n       419\n     x495\n     -------\n       2095   (419 x 5)\n      37710   (419 x 90)\n    +167600   (419 x 400)\n     -------\n     207405\n\nYes, adding those three numbers:\n\nFirst, 2095 + 37710: \n\n2095 + 37710. Let's add 2000 + 37000 = 39000. Then 95 + 710 = 805. So total is 39805. Then adding 167600: 39805 + 167600.\n\n39805 + 167600: Let's add 39805 + 160000 = 199805, then add 7600 more: 199805 + 7600 = 207,405. Yep, same as before.\n\nHmm, seems like that's correct. So I think 207,405 is the right answer.\n\nAlternatively, if I use a calculator to verify, but since I can't, but given that two different methods give me the same result, I can be confident.\n\nAlternatively, let me try multiplying 419 * 500 first, which would be 209,500, and then subtract 419*5, which is 2,095. So 209,500 - 2,095 = 207,405. That's another way to think of it, which is similar to the distributive approach. Yep, that works too. So that's three different methods all leading to the same answer. I think that's solid.\n\nTherefore, the product of 419 and 495 is 207,405.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 419 and 495 is \\boxed{207405}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 419 and 495, we can use the standard multiplication method and verify using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, we break down the multiplication into partial products:\n\n1. Multiply 419 by 5 (units place of 495):\n   \\[\n   419 \\times 5 = 2095\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 419 by 90 (tens place of 495, which is 9 \\times 10):\n   \\[\n   419 \\times 90 = 419 \\times 9 \\times 10 = 3771 \\times 10 = 37710\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 419 by 400 (hundreds place of 495, which is 4 \\times 100):\n   \\[\n   419 \\times 400 = 419 \\times 4 \\times 100 = 1676 \\times 100 = 167600\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum these partial products:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n2095 + 37710 &= 39805, \\\\\n39805 + 167600 &= 207405.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this using the distributive property by expressing 495 as \\(500 - 5\\) and 419 as \\(400 + 19\\):\n\\[\n(400 + 19)(500 - 5) = 400 \\times 500 - 400 \\times 5 + 19 \\times 500 - 19 \\times 5\n\\]\n\\[\n= 200000 - 2000 + 9500 - 95\n\\]\n\\[\n= 200000 - 2000 = 198000, \\\\\n198000 + 9500 = 207500, \\\\\n207500 - 95 = 207405\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 419 and 495 is \\(\\boxed{207405}\\).",
