herefore, 313 \u00d7 684 = 214,092.\n\nWait, but let me verify this with another method to be sure. Maybe using the distributive property: (300 +13)(600 +84) = ?\n\nAlternatively, perhaps breaking it down into smaller parts. Let me try 313 \u00d7 684.\n\nAlternatively, 313 \u00d7 684 = 313 \u00d7 (700 -16) = 313\u00d7700 - 313\u00d716.\n\nCompute 313 \u00d7700: 313 \u00d77 =2191, so \u00d7100 is 219,100.\n\nThen 313\u00d716: 313\u00d710=3,130; 313\u00d76=1,878. So total is 3,130 +1,878=5,008.\n\nTherefore, 219,100 -5,008 = 214,092. Okay, same result.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps do 313 \u00d7684 using another method to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, let me compute 313 \u00d7 600 = 187,800\n\n313\u00d780 = 25,040\n\n313\u00d74 =1,252\n\nAdding those together: 187,800 +25,040 =212,840; then +1,252 =214,092. Yes, same.\n\nTherefore, I think the product is 214,092.\n\nWait, but just to be thorough, perhaps do the multiplication step by step again.\n\nMultiplying 313 \u00d7684:\n\nFirst, write 313 \u00d7 684.\n\nMultiply 313 by 4 (units digit):\n\n3\u00d74=12, write 2, carryover1.\n\n1\u00d74=4 +1=5.\n\n3\u00d74=12. So first partial product: 1252.\n\nMultiply 313 by 8 (tens digit, so shifted one left):\n\n3\u00d78=24, write 4, carryover2.\n\n1\u00d78=8 +2=10, write 0 carryover1.\n\n3\u00d78=24 +1=25. So 2504, shifted left one: 25040.\n\nMultiply 313 by 6 (hundreds digit, shifted two left):\n\n3\u00d76=18, write 8 carryover1.\n\n1\u00d76=6 +1=7.\n\n3\u00d76=18. So 1878, shifted two left: 187800.\n\nAdding them all:\n\n1252\n\n+25040\n\n=26292; then +187,800:\n\n26292 +187,800 = 214,092. Yep, same answer.\n\nAlternatively, use calculator verification? Well, since I can't use a calculator, but let me do another cross-check.\n\nLet me compute 300\u00d7684 = 205,200.\n\nThen 13\u00d7684: 10\u00d7684=6,840; 3\u00d7684=2,052. So 6,840 +2,052=8,892.\n\nAdding 205,200 +8,892 =214,092. Yep, same result.\n\nTherefore, I'm confident that the product is 214,092.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 313 and 684 is \\boxed{214092}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 313 and 684, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 313 by 4 (units place of 684):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   313 \\times 4 &= 1252 \\\\\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n   The first partial product is 1252.\n\n2. **Multiply 313 by 8 (tens place of 684) and shift one position to the left:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   313 \\times 8 &= 2504 \\\\\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n   Shifting one position to the left gives 25040.\n\n3. **Multiply 313 by 6 (hundreds place of 684) and shift two positions to the left:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   313 \\times 6 &= 1878 \\\\\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n   Shifting two positions to the left gives 187800.\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   1252 + 25040 + 187800 &= 1252 + 25040 \\\\\n   &= 26292 \\\\\n   26292 + 187800 &= 214092 \\\\\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 313 and 684 is \\(\\boxed{214092}\\).",
