 663 is 186,303. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, and the cross-verification steps all lead to the same result. So I'm confident this is correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 281 and 663 is \\boxed{186303}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 281 and 663, we use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 281 by 3 (units place of 663):**\n   \\[\n   281 \\times 3 = 843\n   \\]\n   Partial product: 843\n\n2. **Multiply 281 by 60 (tens place of 663):**\n   \\[\n   281 \\times 60 = 16860\n   \\]\n   Partial product: 16860 (shifted one position to the left)\n\n3. **Multiply 281 by 600 (hundreds place of 663):**\n   \\[\n   281 \\times 600 = 168600\n   \\]\n   Partial product: 168600 (shifted two positions to the left)\n\n4. **Add all partial products:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     843 \\\\\n   + 16860 \\\\\n   + 168600 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     186303 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\n   - Adding 843 and 16860:\n     \\[\n     843 + 16860 = 17703\n     \\]\n   - Adding the result to 168600:\n     \\[\n     17703 + 168600 = 186303\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 281 and 663 is \\(\\boxed{186303}\\).",
