r of 1000, so 391\u00d7250 = 391\u00d7(1000/4) = (391\u00d71000)/4 = 391000 /4 = 97,750.\n\nThen 391\u00d71 =391. Adding them together: 97,750 +391 = 98,141. Perfect, same result. So that's another way to confirm.\n\nHmm, all methods lead to 98,141. Therefore, I can be confident that the product is 98,141.\n\nBut just to ensure I didn't make any arithmetic errors in my head, let me go through the initial standard algorithm step-by-step again.\n\nFirst partial product: 391\u00d71 =391.\n\nSecond partial product: 391\u00d75 (tens place, so actually 50). Let me compute 391\u00d75:\n\n3\u00d75=15, write down 5, carryover 1.\n\n9\u00d75=45 +1=46, write 6, carryover4.\n\nWait, wait, 391\u00d75:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits digit:1\u00d75=5.\n\nTens digit:9\u00d75=45. Write down 5, carryover 4.\n\nHundreds digit:3\u00d75=15 +4=19. So the result is 1955. Then adding the zero for the tens place gives 19550. Correct.\n\nThird partial product:391\u00d72 (hundreds place, so 200). 391\u00d72:\n\nUnits:1\u00d72=2.\n\nTens:9\u00d72=18, write 8, carryover1.\n\nHundreds:3\u00d72=6 +1=7. So 782. Adding two zeros gives 78200. Correct.\n\nAdding them up:\n\nFirst, 391 +19550:\n\n391 +19550. Let me add 19550 + 391.\n\n19550 + 300 =19850.\n\n19850 +91 =19941. Correct.\n\nThen 19941 +78200.\n\n19941 +78200. Let me do 20000 +78200 =98200. But subtract the difference: 20000 -19941 =59. So 98200 -59 =98141. Yes, that's another way. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, I can confirm that 391 multiplied by 251 is indeed 98,141. I think that's the correct answer. I've checked it using multiple methods: standard algorithm, breaking down into distributive property, and also using the (a+b)(c+d) approach. All methods led me to the same result, so I'm pretty confident.\n\nWait, just one last check: perhaps approximate the result to see if it's in the ballpark.\n\n391 is approximately 400, 251 is approximately 250. 400\u00d7250 is 100,000. Our answer is 98,141, which is slightly less, which makes sense because we subtracted a bit (since 391 is less than 400 and 251 is a bit more than 250). The difference would be (400 -391)=9 less in one factor and (251-250)=1 more in the other. The net effect would be roughly (400\u00d7250) - (9\u00d7250) + (400\u00d71) - (9\u00d71) as before, which is 100,000 -2,250 +400 -9= 98,141. So the approximation matches, so that's good.\n\nTherefore, I think that's solid. The answer is 98,141.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 391 and 251 is \\boxed{98141}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 391 and 251, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 391 by 1 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   391 \\times 1 = 391\n   \\]\n   This gives the first partial product: \\(391\\).\n\n2. **Multiply 391 by 5 (tens place, representing 50):**\n   \\[\n   391 \\times 5 = 1955\n   \\]\n   Adding a zero for the tens place, we get the second partial product: \\(19550\\).\n\n3. **Multiply 391 by 2 (hundreds place, representing 200):**\n   \\[\n   391 \\times 2 = 782\n   \\]\n   Adding two zeros for the hundreds place, we get the third partial product: \\(78200\\).\n\n4. **Add all partial products:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     391 \\\\\n   + 19550 \\\\\n   + 78200 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     98141 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   - Adding the first two partial products: \\(391 + 19550 = 19941\\)\n   - Adding the result to the third partial product: \\(19941 + 78200 = 98141\\)\n\nTo verify, we can use the distributive property:\n\\[\n(400 - 9)(250 + 1) = 400 \\times 250 + 400 \\times 1 - 9 \\times 250 - 9 \\times 1\n\\]\n\\[\n= 100000 + 400 - 2250 - 9 = 100000 + 400 = 100400\n\\]\n\\[\n100400 - 2250 = 98150\n\\]\n\\[\n98150 - 9 = 98141\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 391 and 251 is \\(\\boxed{98141}\\).",
