      "text": "133,860?\n\nWait, hold on, let me check again. Maybe I made an addition mistake. Let's do it step by step.\n\nFirst, 7,760 + 29,100. Let's add the thousands: 7,000 + 29,000 = 36,000. Then the hundreds and tens: 760 + 100 = 860. So total is 36,000 +860 = 36,860. That's correct. Then adding 36,860 +97,000. Let's break that down: 36,860 + 97,000. 36,000 +97,000 =133,000, then plus 860 is 133,860. Okay, so that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe there's another way to verify. Let me try multiplying 970 x138 using another method to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps using the distributive property as (900 +70) x (100 +38). Wait, but that might complicate. Alternatively, 138 can be expressed as 140 -2. So 970 x (140 -2) = 970x140 -970x2. Let's see.\n\n970x140. 140 is 14x10, so 970x14x10. Let's compute 970x14 first. 970x10 is 9,700. 970x4 is 3,880. So adding those: 9,700 +3,880 =13,580. Then multiply by 10 gives 135,800. Wait no, hold on. Wait, 140 is 14x10, so 970x140 is 970x14x10. Wait, actually, perhaps better to compute 970x14 first: 970x10 is 9,700, plus 970x4 is 3,880, so total 9,700+3,880=13,580. Then multiply by 10? Wait, no, that would be 970 x 140 = 13,580 x10? Wait, no. Wait, 140 is 14 x10, so 970 multiplied by 14 first gives 13,580, then multiplied by 10 would be 135,800? Wait, no, actually, that's overcomplicating.\n\nWait, maybe I messed up here. Let me recast this. If 970 x140 is 970 x14 x10? Not exactly. Actually, 140 is 100 +40. So 970x140 =970x100 +970x40 =97,000 +38,800 =135,800. Yes, that's better. So 97,000 +38,800 is indeed 135,800. Then subtract 970x2 which is 1,940. So total is 135,800 -1,940 =133,860. That matches the previous result. Okay, so that's a good check.\n\nAlternatively, another way: 970 x138. Let me do it in straight multiplication.\n\n970\nx138\n--------\nFirst, multiply 970 x8 =7,760.\n\nThen, multiply 970 x3 (tens place, so actually 30). 970x3=2,910. But since it's the tens place, shift one position to the left, so