      "text": "169,744 minus 49. Hmm, 169,744 minus 40 would be 169,704, then minus 9 more is 169,695. Wait, but let me check again to be sure.\n\nWait, 169,744 minus 49. Let's do it step by step. 169,744 minus 50 would be 169,694, but since it's only minus 49, add 1 back: 169,695. So that's the result?\n\nWait, but I thought maybe I made a mistake in the calculation of 412 squared? Let me re-calculate that part. Let's do 412 squared again.\n\nAlternatively, maybe compute 412 times 412 directly. Let me try that.\n\n412 \u00d7 412:\n\nFirst, multiply 412 \u00d7 400 = 164,800.\n\nThen, 412 \u00d7 12 = 4,944.\n\nAdding them together: 164,800 + 4,944 = 169,744. Okay, that's the same as before. So that part is correct. Then subtracting 49 gives 169,744 - 49 = 169,695. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I should just do the multiplication the standard way to confirm. Let me try multiplying 419 \u00d7 405 the traditional way.\n\nLet me write it out:\n\n    419\n\u00d7 405\n--------\n\nFirst, multiply 419 by 5: 419 \u00d7 5 = 2,095.\n\nThen, multiply 419 by 0 (the tens place, since it's the second digit from the right in 405, which is 0). So that would be 0, but shifted one position to the left: 0000.\n\nThen multiply 419 by 4 (the hundreds place, since 405 is 4 hundreds, 0 tens, 5 ones). But since it's the hundreds place, it's actually 400. So 419 \u00d7 400 = 167,600.\n\nNow add all three results together:\n\n2,095 (from the units place)\n+ 0 (from the tens place, shifted left once)\n+167,600 (from the hundreds place, shifted left two places)\n\nWait, actually, let me make sure of the positions. When multiplying by the hundreds digit (the 4 in 405), it's actually 400, so the partial products should be:\n\nFirst partial product: 419 \u00d7 5 = 2,095\n\nSecond partial product: 419 \u00d7 0 (tens place) = 0, but shifted one position to the left: 0000 with a zero at the end? Wait, no. Wait, actually, when multiplying by the tens digit (which is 0 here), you write a zero shifted one