ns place, resulting in 0):\n  \\[\n  846 \\times 0 = 0\n  \\]\n- Multiply 846 by 1 (hundreds place, shifted two positions left):\n  \\[\n  846 \\times 100 = 84600\n  \\]\n- Sum the partial products:\n  \\[\n  4230 + 0 + 84600 = 88830\n  \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 846 and 105 is \\(\\boxed{88830}\\).",
