t me write them vertically aligned by place:.\n\n          967.\n        87030.\n      +580200.\n      -----------.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nThe units column: 7 (from 967) + 0 (from 87030's units place) + 0 (from 580200's units place) = 7.\n\nTens column: 6 + 3 (from 87030's tens place) + 0 = 9.\n\nHundreds column: 9 (from 967's hundreds) + 0 (from 87030's hundreds place? Wait, 87030 is 8 7 0 3 0, so hundreds place is the third digit from the right, which is 0. Wait, let's see:.\n\nWait, 87030: the digits are 8 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 0 (units). Wait no, that can't be. Wait 87030 is 8 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 0 (units). Wait, so the hundreds place in 87030 is the third digit from the right, which is 0.\n\nWait, but 967 is only three digits, so in the hundreds place for 967 it's 9, then the thousands place is 0, etc. Hmm, maybe I need to write them all out with commas to see:.\n\nFirst partial product: 967 (units:7, tens:6, hundreds:9).\n\nSecond partial product: 87,030 (units:0, tens:3, hundreds:0, thousands:7, ten thousands:8).\n\nThird partial product: 580,200 (units:0, tens:0, hundreds:2, thousands:0, ten thousands:8, hundred thousands:5).\n\nSo when adding:.\n\nLet me write each number with their digits separated by place:.\n\nFor units:.\n\n- 967: 7.\n\n- 87030: 0.\n\n- 580200: 0.\n\nTotal units: 7.\n\nTens place:.\n\n- 967: 6.\n\n- 87030: 3.\n\n- 580200: 0.\n\nTotal tens: 6 + 3 = 9.\n\nHundreds place:.\n\n- 967: 9.\n\n- 87030: 0.\n\n- 580200: 2.\n\nTotal hundreds: 9 + 0 + 2 = 11. So write down 1, carry over 1.\n\nThousands place:.\n\n- 967: 0 (since it's a 3-digit number, thousands place is 0).\n\n- 87030: 7.\n\n- 580200: 0 (wait, 580,200 has thousands place as 0? Wait, 580,200 is 5 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 0 (units). Wait no, 580,200 is:.\n\nBreaking down 580,200:.\n\n- Hundred thousands: 5.\n\n- Ten thousands: 8.\n\n- Thousands: 0.\n\n-