Wait, perhaps the estimation method is:\n\nThe exact numbers are 654 and 549. So approximating 654 as 650 and 549 as 550 gives an overestimation for 549 (since we rounded up by 1) and underestimation for 654 (rounded down by 4). The difference from the actual numbers would be:\n\n(654 -650) = +4 and (549 -550)= -1. So the actual product is (650 +4)*(550 -1). Let me compute that:\n\n(650 +4)*(550 -1) =650\u00d7550 +650\u00d7(-1) +4\u00d7550 +4\u00d7(-1).\n\n= 357,500 -650 + 2,200 -4.\n\n= 357,500 -650 = 356,850; 356,850 +2,200 =359,050; 359,050 -4 =359,046. Exactly the result we had earlier. So that checks out. Therefore, the exact answer is indeed 359,046. Okay, so that must be correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do the multiplication in another way:\n\n654 \u00d7549 can be written as 654\u00d7(500 +40 +9) which is the same as 654\u00d7500 +654\u00d740 +654\u00d79, which is exactly what I did before, so that gives the same partial products, so adding up gives the same result. So that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps do 549 \u00d7654, which should give the same result. Let me try that quickly.\n\nLet me compute 549 \u00d7654.\n\nStarting with 549 \u00d74 (units place):\n\n549 \u00d74:.\n\n9\u00d74=36 \u21926, carryover3.\n\n4\u00d74=16 +3=19 \u21929, carryover1.\n\n5\u00d74=20 +1=21 \u219221. So 2196. That's the first partial product.\n\nSecond partial product: 549 \u00d750 (tens place, so 5\u00d710, so multiply by 5 and shift left one).\n\n549 \u00d75:.\n\n9\u00d75=45 \u21925, carryover4.\n\n4\u00d75=20 +4=24 \u21924, carryover2.\n\n5\u00d75=25 +2=27 \u219227. So 2745. Shift left one \u219227450.\n\nThird partial product: 549 \u00d7600 (hundreds place, 6\u00d7100).\n\n549 \u00d76 = 549\u00d76: 9\u00d76=54 \u21924, carryover5.\n\n4\u00d76=24 +5=29 \u21929, carryover2.\n\n5\u00d76=30 +2=32 \u219232. So 3294. Multiply by 100 \u2192329400.\n\nNow add all three partial products: 2196 +27450 +329400.\n\nFirst, 2196 +27450:.\n\n2196 +27450 = 29646.\n\nThen, 29646 +329400 = 359,046. Same result. Okay, that's reassuring.\n\nTherefore, I can be confident that the product of 654 and 549 is 359,046.\n\nWait, just to make absolutely sure, perhaps do a calculator check?\n\nSince I can't use an actual calculator, but let me try another method, like prime factorization? Though that might take longer.\n\nAlternatively, compute 654 \u00d7 549 as (600 +54)(500 +49).\n\nMultiply using the distributive property:\n\nFirst, 600\u00d7500 = 300,000.\n\n600\u00d749 = 600\u00d740 +600\u00d79 =24,000 +5,400 =29,400.\n\n54\u00d7500 =27,000.\n\n54\u00d749: Let's compute 54\u00d750 =2,700 minus 54\u00d71 =54 \u21922,700 -54 =2,646.\n\nNow add all these together:.\n\n300,000 +29,400 =329,400.\n\n329,400 +27,000 =356,400.\n\n356,400 +2,646 =359,046. Exactly the same result. Perfect, that's another confirmation.\n\nSo all methods lead to 359,046. I think that's solid. Therefore, the answer should be 359,046.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 654 and 549 is \\boxed{359046}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 654 and 549, we use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 654 by 9 (units place of 549):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   654 \\times 9 &= 5886 \\\\\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 654 by 4 (tens place of 549, which is 40):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   654 \\times 4 &= 2616 \\\\\n   \\text{Shift left by one position:} \\quad 26160 \\\\\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 654 by 5 (hundreds place of 549, which is 500):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   654 \\times 5 &= 3270 \\\\\n   \\text{Shift left by two positions:} \\quad 327000 \\\\\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all partial products:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   5886 + 26160 + 327000 &= 5886 + 26160 \\\\\n   &= 32046 \\\\\n   32046 + 327000 &= 359046 \\\\\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n\\[\n\\begin{align}\n654 \\times 549 &= (600 + 54) \\times (500 + 49) \\\\\n&= 600 \\times 500 + 600 \\times 49 + 54 \\times 500 + 54 \\times 49 \\\\\n&= 300000 + 29400 + 27000 + 2646 \\\\\n&= 300000 + 29400 = 329400 \\\\\n&= 329400 + 27000 = 356400 \\\\\n&= 356400 + 2646 = 359046 \\\\\n\\end{align}\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 654 and 549 is \\boxed{359046}.",
