e higher. 613,735 is indeed higher, so that makes sense. The difference is about 28,735, which seems reasonable given the rounding.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using calculator-like step-by-step multiplication again. Let me try writing it out vertically again to ensure I didn't make an arithmetic mistake in the initial steps.\n\nMultiplying 655 by 937:\n\nFirst, 655 \u00d7 7:\n\n7\u00d75 =35, write 5 carry 3.\n\n7\u00d75 =35 +3 =38, write 8 carry 3.\n\n7\u00d76 =42 +3 =45, so write 45. So 4585. Correct.\n\nThen 655 \u00d730 (the 3 in tens place):\n\n3\u00d75=15, write 5 carry1.\n\n3\u00d75=15+1=16, write6 carry1.\n\n3\u00d76=18 +1=19. So 1965, then add a zero: 19650. Correct.\n\nThen 655 \u00d7900:\n\n9\u00d75=45, write5 carry4.\n\n9\u00d75=45+4=49, write9 carry4.\n\n9\u00d76=54+4=58. So 5895, then add two zeros: 589500. Correct.\n\nAdding them up:\n\n4585 +19650:\n\n4585 +19650: Let's see:\n\n4585 + 19650.\n\n4585 + 19000 =23585.\n\n23585 + 650 =24235. Correct.\n\n24235 +589500:\n\n24,235 +589,500 =613,735. Correct.\n\nYes, so all steps check out. Therefore, I can be confident the product is 613,735.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 655 and 937 is \\boxed{613735}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 655 and 937, we use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 655 by 7 (ones place):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   655 \\times 7 &= 4585 \\\\\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 655 by 30 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   655 \\times 30 &= 19650 \\\\\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 655 by 900 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   655 \\times 900 &= 589500 \\\\\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   4585 + 19650 + 589500 &= 4585 + 19650 + 589500 \\\\\n   &= 24235 + 589500 \\\\\n   &= 613735 \\\\\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n\nTo verify, we use the distributive property:\n\\[\n(600 + 55) \\times (900 + 37) = 600 \\times 900 + 600 \\times 37 + 55 \\times 900 + 55 \\times 37\n\\]\n\\[\n= 540000 + 22200 + 49500 + 2035 = 613735\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the result. The product of 655 and 937 is \\(\\boxed{613735}\\).",
