gorithm.\n\nFirst, we decompose 176 into 100, 70, and 6:\n\\[\n239 \\times 176 = 239 \\times (100 + 70 + 6)\n\\]\n\nCalculating each part separately:\n1. \\(239 \\times 100 = 23900\\)\n2. \\(239 \\times 70 = 239 \\times 7 \\times 10\\)\n   - \\(239 \\times 7 = 1673\\)\n   - \\(1673 \\times 10 = 16730\\)\n3. \\(239 \\times 6 = 1434\\)\n\nAdding the results together:\n\\[\n23900 + 16730 + 1434\n\\]\n\nStep-by-step addition:\n1. \\(23900 + 16730 = 40630\\)\n2. \\(40630 + 1434 = 42064\\)\n\nVerification using the standard algorithm:\n- Multiply 239 by 6: \\(239 \\times 6 = 1434\\)\n- Multiply 239 by 70 (shifted one position left): \\(239 \\times 70 = 16730\\)\n- Multiply 239 by 100 (shifted two positions left): \\(239 \\times 100 = 23900\\)\n- Sum the partial products: \\(1434 + 16730 + 23900 = 42064\\)\n\nAnother verification method using approximation:\n- \\(240 \\times 180 = 43200\\) (rounded values), confirming the result is reasonable.\n\nThus, the product of 239 and 176 is \\(\\boxed{42064}\\).",
