ltiplication in another way, perhaps using the lattice method, but that might take longer. Alternatively, check with approximate estimation.\n\nEstimate: 160 \u00d7800 =128,000. The actual numbers are slightly higher: 163\u00d7808. 163 is 3 more than 160, and 808 is 8 more than 800. So the difference would be (160\u00d78)+(3\u00d7800)+(3\u00d78) =1,280 +2,400 +24=3,704. So 128,000 +3,704=131,704. Exactly the same. So that checks out.\n\nTherefore, I'm confident the product of 163 and 808 is 131,704.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 163 and 808 is \\boxed{131704}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 163 and 808, we can use the distributive property and break down the multiplication into smaller parts:\n\n1. **Multiply 163 by 8 (units place of 808):**\n   \\[\n   163 \\times 8 = 1304\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 163 by 0 (tens place of 808):**\n   \\[\n   163 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n   This result is shifted one position to the left, resulting in 000.\n\n3. **Multiply 163 by 8 (hundreds place of 808):**\n   \\[\n   163 \\times 8 = 1304\n   \\]\n   This result is shifted two positions to the left, resulting in 130400.\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   1304 + 0 + 130400 = 131704\n   \\]\n\nVerification using alternative methods (breaking down numbers and distributive property) confirms the result. \n\nThe product of 163 and 808 is \\(\\boxed{131704}\\).",
