s, the first one was 13,885. The second partial product from the 7 (tens place) should be 7 × 277, but shifted left by one. Let me compute 7 × 277 first:.\n\n7 × 200 = 1400.\n\n7 × 70 = 490.\n\n7 × 7 = 49.\n\nAdding those: 1400 + 490 = 1890, plus 49 is 1939. But since it's the tens place, we need to multiply by 10, so 1939 × 10 = 19,390. Okay, that makes sense.\n\nNow moving to the next digit in 475, which is 4 (the hundreds place). This should be shifted two places to the left. So 4 × 277. Let me compute that:.\n\n4 × 200 = 800.\n\n4 × 70 = 280.\n\n4 × 7 = 28.\n\nAdding those together: 800 + 280 = 1080, plus 28 is 1108. Then, since it's the hundreds place, multiply by 100, so 1108 × 100 = 110,800.\n\nNow, adding up all three partial products:.\n\nFirst partial product: 13,885.\n\nSecond partial product: 19,390.\n\nThird partial product: 110,800.\n\nAdding them together step by step. Let's start with 13,885 + 19,390.\n\n13,885 + 19,390:.\n\nAdding the thousands: 13,000 + 19,000 = 32,000.\n\nAdding the hundreds: 800 + 300 = 1,100.\n\nAdding the tens and ones: 85 + 90 = 175.\n\nWait, maybe breaking it down differently. Alternatively, 13,885 + 19,390:.\n\n13,885.\n\n+19,390.\n\n= ?.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\n5 + 0 =5.\n\n8 +9 =17, write 7, carryover 1.\n\n8 +3 +1=12, write 2, carryover 1.\n\n3 +9 +1=13, write 3, carryover 1.\n\n1 +1 +1=3. Wait, maybe let me do it properly:.\n\nUnits place: 5 +0=5.\n\nTens place:8 +9=17, so 7, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place:8 +3=11, plus the carried over 1 is 12. So write 2, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place:3 (from 13,885) +9 (from 19,390) =12, plus the carried over 1 is 13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 1 (from 13,885) +1 (from 19,390) =2, plus the carried over 1 is 3.\n\nSo total is 33,275?.\n\nWait, let me check with another method:.\n\n13,885 +19,390:.\n\n13,885 +10,000 =23,885.\n\n23,885 +9,000 =32,885.\n\n32,885 +390 =33,275. Yes, that's correct.\n\nNow add the third partial product: 33,275 +110,800.\n\n33,275