77=35. Adding those: 5,600 +280=5,880 +35=5,915. So that is correct. So 845\u00d7700 is 5,915 \u00d7100 = 591,500. Okay, so my previous calculation was wrong when I did 845\u00d77 as 5,215. I must have miscalculated that step earlier. So that was an error.\n\nThen, moving on, 845\u00d725. Let me compute that again:\n\n845\u00d725. Let's break it into 800\u00d725 +45\u00d725.\n\n800\u00d725 = 20,000 (since 8\u00d725=200, \u00d7100 is 20,000).\n\n45\u00d725: 40\u00d725=1,000, 5\u00d725=125. So total 1,000 +125=1,125. So total 20,000 +1,125=21,125.\n\nTherefore, adding to the 591,500 from before: 591,500 +21,125 =612,625. Ah! That matches the previous results. So I must have miscalculated the first part when I thought I got 521,500. That was my mistake. So that's why it's important to double-check. So this method also gives 612,625. So that's consistent.\n\nTherefore, after verifying through multiple methods and catching an arithmetic error in one of the steps, I can be confident the correct product is 612,625.\n\nAlternatively, let me try another check using estimation. Let's see:\n\n725 is approximately 700, 845 is approximately 800. 700\u00d7800=560,000. The actual numbers are a bit higher, so the product should be higher. 612,625 is 52,625 more than 560,000, which seems reasonable given that we added 25 and 45 to the original approximations.\n\nAlternatively, let me compute 700\u00d7845 first, then add 25\u00d7845.\n\n700\u00d7845: 700\u00d7800=560,000; 700\u00d745=31,500. So total 560,000+31,500=591,500.\n\n25\u00d7845: 25\u00d7800=20,000; 25\u00d745=1,125. So total 21,125.\n\nAdding those two parts: 591,500 +21,125 = 612,625. Yep, same answer.\n\nAlright, I think that's thorough enough. All methods lead to the same result, so I'm confident the answer is correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 725 and 845 is \\boxed{612625}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 725 and 845, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into smaller parts:\n\n\\[\n(700 + 25)(800 + 45)\n\\]\n\nExpanding this using the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n700 \\times 800 + 700 \\times 45 + 25 \\times 800 + 25 \\times 45\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term separately:\n\n1. \\(700 \\times 800 = 560,000\\)\n2. \\(700 \\times 45 = 31,500\\)\n3. \\(25 \\times 800 = 20,000\\)\n4. \\(25 \\times 45 = 1,125\\)\n\nAdding these results together:\n\n\\[\n560,000 + 31,500 = 591,500\n\\]\n\\[\n591,500 + 20,000 = 611,500\n\\]\n\\[\n611,500 + 1,125 = 612,625\n\\]\n\nWe can also verify this using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 725 by 5: \\(725 \\times 5 = 3,625\\)\n2. Multiply 725 by 40: \\(725 \\times 40 = 29,000\\)\n3. Multiply 725 by 800: \\(725 \\times 800 = 580,000\\)\n\nAdding these results together:\n\n\\[\n3,625 + 29,000 = 32,625\n\\]\n\\[\n32,625 + 580,000 = 612,625\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 725 and 845 is \\(\\boxed{612625}\\).",
