      "text": "89,980 plus 44? Wait, no. Wait, 744 is 700 + 44. So adding 700 to 89,280 gives 89,980, then add the remaining 44. So 89,980 + 44 = 90,024. .\n\nWait, let me check that again. 89,280 + 744. Let's line them up:\n\n89,280\n+   744\n--------\nStarting from the right:\n0 + 4 = 4\n8 + 4 = 12, write 2, carryover 1\n2 + 7 = 9 plus the 1 is 10, write 0, carryover 1\n9 + 0 = 9 plus the 1 is 10, write 0, carryover 1\n8 + 0 = 8 plus the 1 is 9.\n\nWait, that gives 89,280 + 744 as 90,024. Hmm. Wait, that doesn't seem right. Let me do it again step by step:\n\n89,280 + 744:\n\nFirst, 89,280 + 700 = 89,980\n\nThen, 89,980 + 44 = 90,024. Yes, that's correct. So total is 90,024. .\n\nBut wait, let me confirm this with another method to be sure. Maybe multiplying directly? Let's try the standard multiplication algorithm for 744 \u00d7 121.\n\nFirst, write 744  \n\u00d7121  \n------------\n\nMultiply 744 by 1 (units place): 744  \nMultiply 744 by 20 (tens place: since the 2 is in the tens place, it's 20): 744\u00d720 = 14,880  \nMultiply 744 by 100 (hundreds place: the 1 is in the hundreds place, so 100): 744\u00d7100 = 74,400  \n\nNow add them all together:\n\n744  \n14,880  \n74,400  \nTotal: ?\n\nAdding 744 +14,880 first. 744 +14,880 = 15,624. Then add 74,400:\n\n15,624 +74,400. Let's see, 15,000 +74,000 = 89,000. 624 + 400 = 1,024. So total is 89,000 +1,024 = 90,024. Okay, same result. That matches. .\n\nHmm, so that seems correct. Wait, but I want to check again using another method, maybe breaking down 121 into 100 + 20 +1? Let's see:\n\n744 \u00d7 100 = 74,400  \n744 \u00d7 20 = 14,880  \n744 \u00d7 1 = 744  \nAdding those together: 74,400 +14,880 = 89,280; then +744 = 90,024. Yep, same answer. .\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the standard vertical multiplication:\n\n       744  \n     \u00d7121  \n     ------  \n       744   (744 \u00d7 1)  \n      1488    (744 \u00d7 20, shifted one position to the left)  \n     74400    (744 \u00d7 100, shifted two positions)  \n     -------  \n     90,024  \n\nYes, adding those rows: 744 +14,880 is 15,624; plus 74,400 gives 90,024. .\n\nTherefore, I think the correct product is 90,024. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, and cross-verified with different methods. So I'm confident that's the right answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 744 and 121 is \\boxed{90024}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 744 and 121, we can use the distributive property and break down the multiplication into smaller parts:\n\n1. Break down 121 into 100 + 20 + 1:\n   \\[\n   744 \\times 121 = 744 \\times (100 + 20 + 1)\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate each part separately:\n   - \\( 744 \\times 100 = 74400 \\)\n   - \\( 744 \\times 20 = 14880 \\)\n   - \\( 744 \\times 1 = 744 \\)\n\n3. Add the results of these multiplications together:\n   \\[\n   74400 + 14880 + 744\n   \\]\n\n4. Perform the addition step-by-step:\n   - First, add \\( 74400 \\) and \\( 14880 \\):\n     \\[\n     74400 + 14880 = 89280\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to \\( 744 \\):\n     \\[\n     89280 + 744 = 90024\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 744 and 121 is \\(\\boxed{90024}\\).",
