*24 = 384\n\nAdding them up:\n\n20,000 + 4,800 = 24,800\n\n24,800 + 1,600 = 26,400\n\n26,400 + 384 = 26,784. \n\nSame result again. So that's three different methods all leading to 26,784. I think that's solid. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check using a calculator if I have one, but since this is a thought process, I can't. But since all manual methods give the same answer, that's reassuring.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps estimate to see if the answer makes sense. 200*100 = 20,000, and 200*120 would be 24,000, so 216 is a bit more than 200 and 124 is a bit more than 120, so the product should be a bit more than 200*120 =24,000. Wait, but 216*124 is 26,784 which is significantly higher. Hmm, actually 216 is 16 over 200, and 124 is 4 over 120. Let me see, maybe my estimation is too rough. Alternatively, 200*124 is 24,800, and then adding 16*124 to that. 16*124 is 1,984. So 24,800 + 1,984 = 26,784. Yep, that works. So that's another way to break it down. \n\nAlternatively, breaking down 216 into 200 + 16 and multiplying by 124:\n\n(200 +16)*124 = 200*124 + 16*124.\n\n200*124 is straightforward: 200*100=20,000; 200*24=4,800; so total 24,800.\n\n16*124: Let's compute that. 10*124=1,240; 6*124=744; so total 1,240 + 744 = 1,984. Adding to 24,800 gives 24,800 + 1,984 = 26,784. Yep, same number again.\n\nAlright, so after multiple methods and checks, I can be confident that the product of 216 and 124 is 26,784.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 216 and 124 is \\boxed{26784}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 216 and 124, we can use the distributive property and break down the numbers into smaller parts for easier calculation.\n\nFirst, we break down 124 into 120 and 4:\n\\[\n216 \\times 124 = 216 \\times (120 + 4)\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate each part separately:\n1. Calculate \\(216 \\times 4\\):\n   \\[\n   216 \\times 4 = 864\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\(216 \\times 120\\). We can further break this down:\n   \\[\n   216 \\times 120 = 216 \\times (100 + 20)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   216 \\times 100 = 21600\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   216 \\times 20 = 4320\n   \\]\n   Adding these results:\n   \\[\n   21600 + 4320 = 25920\n   \\]\n\nNow, add the results of the two parts:\n\\[\n25920 + 864 = 26784\n\\]\n\nWe can also verify this using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n- Multiply 216 by 4 (units place): \\(216 \\times 4 = 864\\)\n- Multiply 216 by 20 (tens place): \\(216 \\times 20 = 4320\\)\n- Multiply 216 by 100 (hundreds place): \\(216 \\times 100 = 21600\\)\n\nAdding these results:\n\\[\n864 + 4320 + 21600 = 26784\n\\]\n\nAnother verification using the distributive property with different breakdowns:\n- Break down 216 into 200 and 16:\n  \\[\n  (200 + 16) \\times 124 = 200 \\times 124 + 16 \\times 124\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  200 \\times 124 = 24800\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  16 \\times 124 = 1984\n  \\]\n  Adding these results:\n  \\[\n  24800 + 1984 = 26784\n  \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 216 and 124 is \\(\\boxed{26784}\\).",
