bably the simplest way.\n\nAlternatively, let me compute 317*1000 = 317,000. Then subtract 317*4=1,268. 317,000 - 1,268 is indeed 315,732.\n\nHmm. So all methods lead to the same result, so I think that's correct.\n\nWait, but just to be thorough, maybe I can check using a calculator-like approach, but since I can't use a calculator, perhaps an approximate estimation to see if it's in the ballpark.\n\n317 is approximately 300, and 996 is approximately 1000. So 300*1000 = 300,000. The actual answer should be a bit less than that because both numbers are slightly higher than their approximations? Wait, 317 is higher than 300, but 996 is lower than 1000. So the effect might be a bit complex.\n\nAlternatively, 300*1000 = 300,000. The actual numbers are 17 more and 4 less. The difference would be (300+17)*(1000-4) = 300*1000 - 300*4 +17*1000 -17*4. Which is 300,000 -1,200 + 17,000 -68 = 300,000 +17,000 = 317,000; minus (1,200 +68)=1,268. So same as before. So 317,000 -1,268 = 315,732. So that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, if I estimate 317*1000 = 317,000. Then subtract 4*317 = 1,268. So yeah, 315,732. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, after multiple methods and checks, I believe the correct product is 315,732.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 317 and 996 is \\boxed{315732}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 317 and 996, we can simplify the calculation by breaking down 996 into \\(1000 - 4\\). Using the distributive property, we have:\n\n\\[\n317 \\times 996 = 317 \\times (1000 - 4)\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(317 \\times 1000\\):\n\n\\[\n317 \\times 1000 = 317000\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(317 \\times 4\\):\n\n\\[\n317 \\times 4 = 1268\n\\]\n\nSubtract the second result from the first:\n\n\\[\n317000 - 1268 = 315732\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can also use standard multiplication:\n\n1. Multiply 317 by 6:\n   \\[\n   317 \\times 6 = 1902\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 317 by 90 (since the 9 is in the tens place):\n   \\[\n   317 \\times 9 = 2853 \\quad \\text{then} \\quad 2853 \