, we can use the distributive property and break down the multiplication into smaller parts:\n\n1. **Multiply 304 by 2 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   304 \\times 2 = 608\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 304 by 50 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   304 \\times 50 = 304 \\times 5 \\times 10 = 1520 \\times 10 = 15200\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 304 by 600 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   304 \\times 600 = 304 \\times 6 \\times 100 = 1824 \\times 100 = 182400\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the results of the three multiplications:**\n   \\[\n   608 + 15200 + 182400\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add 608 and 15200:\n     \\[\n     608 + 15200 = 15808\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to 182400:\n     \\[\n     15808 + 182400 = 198208\n     \\]\n\nTo verify, we can use another method by expanding the numbers:\n\\[\n(300 + 4) \\times (600 + 50 + 2)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 300 \\times 600 + 300 \\times 50 + 300 \\times 2 + 4 \\times 600 + 4 \\times 50 + 4 \\times 2\n\\]\n\\[\n= 180000 + 15000 + 600 + 2400 + 200 + 8\n\\]\n\\[\n= 180000 + 15000 = 195000\n\\]\n\\[\n195000 + 600 = 195600\n\\]\n\\[\n195600 + 2400 = 198000\n\\]\n\\[\n198000 + 200 = 198200\n\\]\n\\[\n198200 + 8 = 198208\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 304 and 652 is \\(\\boxed{198208}\\).",
