\u00d7100):\n\n790\u00d78: 8\u00d70=0, 8\u00d79=72 (write 2, carryover7), 8\u00d77=56 +7=63. So 6320. Then \u00d7100 is 632,000.\n\nAdding them all:\n\nFirst partial product:    7,110\n\nSecond partial product: 55,300\n\nThird partial product: 632,000\n\nAdding first two: 7,110 +55,300 =62,410\n\nAdding to third: 62,410 +632,000 =694,410.\n\nYes, same result. So I think that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, let me try multiplying 879 \u00d7 790 instead, to see if commutative property holds.\n\n879 \u00d7790. Let's do that:\n\n879 \u00d7700 = 615,300\n\n879 \u00d790 = 79,110\n\nAdding those together: 615,300 +79,110 =694,410. Yep, same answer. So that confirms it.\n\nTherefore, the product of 790 and 879 is 694,410.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 790 and 879 is \\boxed{694410}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 790 and 879, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here are the key steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 790 by 9 (units place of 879):**\n   \\[\n   790 \\times 9 = 7110\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 790 by 70 (tens place of 879, which is 7 followed by a zero):**\n   \\[\n   790 \\times 70 = 55300\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 790 by 800 (hundreds place of 879, which is 8 followed by two zeros):**\n   \\[\n   790 \\times 800 = 632000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   7110 + 55300 + 632000\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add \\(7110\\) and \\(55300\\):\n     \\[\n     7110 + 55300 = 62410\n     \\]\n\n   - Then add the result to \\(632000\\):\n     \\[\n     62410 + 632000 = 694410\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 790 and 879 is \\(\\boxed{694410}\\).",
