lace, so 300) times 292: 292*3=876, so 87600.\n\nAdding them: 1460 + 11680 = 13140, then 13140 +87600 = 100,740. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I can compute 292 * 345 using another method. Let's try the box method (area model) to cross-verify.\n\nBreaking down 292 into 200 +90 +2, and 345 into 300 +40 +5.\n\nThen the product is:\n\n(200 +90 +2)*(300 +40 +5).\n\nMultiplying each term:\n\nFirst, 200*300 = 60,000\n\n200*40 = 8,000\n\n200*5 = 1,000\n\n90*300 = 27,000\n\n90*40 = 3,600\n\n90*5 = 450\n\n2*300 = 600\n\n2*40 = 80\n\n2*5 =10\n\nNow add all these up:\n\n60,000\n\n+8,000 =68,000\n\n+1,000 =69,000\n\n+27,000 =96,000\n\n+3,600 =99,600\n\n+450 =100,050\n\n+600 =100,650\n\n+80 =100,730\n\n+10 =100,740.\n\nYes! That gives the same total of 100,740. So that confirms it. Therefore, the product should be 100,740.\n\nWait, but let me check once more using another approach, perhaps calculator-style step-by-step.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do 292 multiplied by 345 as follows:\n\nFirst, multiply 292 by 345.\n\nCompute 292 * 300 = 87,600\n\n292 *40 =11,680\n\n292 *5 =1,460\n\nAdding those three: 87,600 +11,680 = 99,280. Then 99,280 +1,460 = 100,740. Yep, same result.\n\nTherefore, I can be confident that the product is 100,740.\n\nBut just to be absolutely sure, let me try another way: using the difference of squares or some other algebraic identity? Hmm, not sure if applicable here.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps approximate to check if it's in the ballpark. 292 is close to 300, and 345 is close to 300. 300*300 is 90,000, but since both numbers are a bit higher, the actual product should be higher. 300*350 would be 105,000, so 100,740 is between those, which makes sense. So that approximation seems plausible.\n\nAlternatively, 292*345. Let me compute 292*300 =87,600, and 292*45.\n\nWait, 292 *45: 292*(40 +5)=292*40 +292*5=11,680 +1,460=13,140. Then adding to 87,600 gives 100,740. Correct.\n\nThus, after multiple methods, I keep getting 100,740. So I think that's the right answer. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. Probably correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 292 and 345 is \\boxed{100740}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 292 and 345, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm by breaking it down into partial products:\n\n1. **Multiply 292 by 5 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   292 \\times 5 = 1460\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 292 by 40 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   292 \\times 40 = 11680\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 292 by 300 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   292 \\times 300 = 87600\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum these partial products:\n\n1. **Add the first two partial products:**\n   \\[\n   1460 + 11680 = 13140\n   \\]\n\n2. **Add the result to the third partial product:**\n   \\[\n   13140 + 87600 = 100740\n   \\]\n\nTo verify, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into hundreds, tens, and units:\n\n\\[\n(200 + 90 + 2) \\times (300 + 40 + 5)\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term and summing them up:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&200 \\times 300 = 60000, \\\\\n&200 \\times 40 = 8000, \\\\\n&200 \\times 5 = 1000, \\\\\n&90 \\times 300 = 27000, \\\\\n&90 \\times 40 = 3600, \\\\\n&90 \\times 5 = 450, \\\\\n&2 \\times 300 = 600, \\\\\n&2 \\times 40 = 80, \\\\\n&2 \\times 5 = 10.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nSumming these results:\n\\[\n60000 + 8000 + 1000 + 27000 + 3600 + 450 + 600 + 80 + 10 = 100740\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 292 and 345 is \\(\\boxed{100740}\\).",
