adding all three results together:.\n\nFirst partial product: 5236.\nSecond partial product: 67320.\nThird partial product: 598400.\n\nLet me stack them up:.\n\n\u2003\u20035236.\n\u200367320.\n+598400.\n----------.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nAdding the units place: 6 + 0 + 0 = 6.\n\nTens place: 3 + 2 + 0 = 5.\n\nHundreds place: 2 + 3 + 4 = 9.\n\nThousands place: 5 (from 5236) + 7 (from 67320) + 8 (from 598400) = 5 +7 is 12, plus 8 is 20. So write down 0 and carry over 2.\n\nTen-thousands place: 0 (since 5236 has no digit here) + 6 (from 67320) + 9 (from 598400) plus the carried 2. Wait, let me check again. Wait, the numbers are:.\n\n5236 is four digits, so:.\n\nUnits: 6.\n\nTens: 3.\n\nHundreds: 2.\n\nThousands: 5.\n\nTen-thousands: 0.\n\n67320 is five digits:.\n\nUnits:0.\n\nTens:2.\n\nHundreds:3.\n\nThousands:7.\n\nTen-thousands:6.\n\n598400 is six digits:.\n\nUnits:0.\n\nTens:0.\n\nHundreds:4.\n\nThousands:8.\n\nTen-thousands:9.\n\nHundred-thousands:5.\n\nWait, maybe I need to align them properly. Let me write each number with commas for clarity.\n\n5236 is 5,236.\n\n67,320.\n\n598,400.\n\nAdding them:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:.\n\nUnits: 6 + 0 + 0 = 6.\n\nTens: 3 + 2 + 0 = 5.\n\nHundreds: 2 + 3 + 4 = 9.\n\nThousands: 5 (from 5,236) + 7 (from 67,320) + 8 (from 598,400) = 5+7=12, 12+8=20. So write 0 and carry over 2.\n\nTen-thousands place: 0 (from 5,236) + 6 (from 67,320) +9 (from 598,400) + 2 (carry) = 6+9=15 +2=17. So write 7 and carry over 1.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 0 (from the first two numbers) +5 (from 598,400) + 1 (carry) = 6.\n\nSo putting it all together: 673,636? Wait, let me check again.\n\nWait, perhaps I miscalculated the ten-thousands place. Let's see:.\n\nBreaking down each number:.\n\n5,236 is:.\n\nDigit places (from right):.\n\n1: 6.\n\n2: 3 (tens).\n\n3: 2 (hundreds).\n\n4: 5 (thousands).\n\n5: 0 (ten thousands).\n\n6: 0 (hundred thousands).\n\n67,320 is:.\n\nDigit places:.\n\n1:0.\n\n2:2 (tens).\n\n3:3 (hundreds).\n\n4:7 (thousands).\n\n5:6 (ten thousands).\n\n6:0 (hundred thousands).\n\n598,400 is:.\n\n1:0.\n\n2:0 (tens).\n\n3:4 (hundreds).\n\n4:8 (thousands).\n\n5:9 (ten thousands).\n\n6:5 (hundred thousands).\n\nNow adding each column:.\n\nUnits (1st digit from right):.\n\n6 + 0 +0=6.\n\nTens (2nd):.\n\n3 +2 +0=5.\n\nHundreds (3rd):.\n\n2 +3 +4=9.\n\nThousands (4th):.\n\n5 +7 +8 = 20. So 0 with carryover 2.\n\nTen thousands (5th):.\n\n0 +6 +9 +2 (carry) =17. So 7 with carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands (6th):.\n\n0 +0 +5 +1 (carry)=6.\n\nSo the total is 6 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 6 (units). Wait, but the thousands place was 20, so we had 0 there with carryover. Then the ten thousands place is 17, so 7 with carryover. So putting it together:.\n\n6 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 6 (units). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
