      "text": "584,320 + 5,312. Let me do that addition carefully.\n\n584,320 plus 5,000 is 589,320. Then add 312 more: 589,320 + 312 = 589,632. So is that the total? Wait, let me check again to make sure I didn't make any mistakes in the steps.\n\nAlternatively, maybe there's another way to cross-verify. Let me try multiplying 664 \u00d7 888 using another method, like the standard algorithm. Let me set it up:\n\n       664\n    \u00d7 888\n    -------\nFirst, multiply 664 by 8 (units place): 664 \u00d7 8 = 5,312.\n\nThen, multiply 664 by 80 (tens place): 664 \u00d7 80 = 53,120. So that's shifting one position to the left.\n\nNext, multiply 664 by 800 (hundreds place): 664 \u00d7 800 = 531,200. Shifting two positions to the left.\n\nAdding them up:\n\n    5,312\n  53,120\n+531,200\n----------\nTotal?\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n5,312\n+53,120 = 58,432\n\n58,432 + 531,200 = 589,632. Okay, same result as before. So that seems to check out.\n\nWait, but let me confirm once more with another approach, perhaps using some other decomposition. Maybe breaking down 664 instead?\n\nAlternatively, perhaps using the fact that 888 is 900 - 12? Let's see:\n\nSo 664 \u00d7 (900 - 12) = 664 \u00d7 900 - 664 \u00d7 12.\n\nCalculating 664 \u00d7 900: 664 \u00d7 9 = 5,976 (since 600\u00d79=5,400; 64\u00d79=576; 5,400+576=5,976). Then \u00d7100 gives 597,600.\n\nThen 664 \u00d712: Let's compute that. 664 \u00d710 = 6,640 and 664 \u00d72 = 1,328. Adding those gives 6,640 +1,328 = 7,968.\n\nSo subtracting: 597,600 - 7,968. Let's compute that.\n\n597,600 minus 7,000 is 590,600. Then subtract 968 more: 590,600 - 968 = 589,632. Same result again. Okay, so that's a third method and still the same answer, so I think that must be correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use calculator verification? But since I can't use a calculator, but let me see another way.\n\nAnother way is to compute 664 \u00d7 888 = 664 \u00d7 (800 + 80 +8) as done earlier, which also gives the same result.\n\nAlternatively,