ite 18. So partial product is 1820 shifted twice: 182000.\n\nNow add the three partial products:\n\n2548\n\n+32760 = 35308\n\nThen 35308 +182000 = 217,308. Yep, same as before.\n\nTherefore, after multiple methods and cross-verifying, I can confidently say the product of 364 and 597 is 217,308.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 364 and 597 is \\boxed{217308}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 364 and 597, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy. Here are the key steps from the thought process:\n\n1. **Standard Multiplication Method:**\n   - Multiply 364 by 7 (units place): \\(364 \\times 7 = 2548\\)\n   - Multiply 364 by 9 (tens place, shifted left once): \\(364 \\times 9 = 3276\\), resulting in 32760\n   - Multiply 364 by 5 (hundreds place, shifted left twice): \\(364 \\times 5 = 1820\\), resulting in 182000\n   - Sum the partial products:\n     \\[\n     2548 + 32760 + 182000 = 217308\n     \\]\n\n2. **Distributive Property (597 as 600 - 3):**\n   - Calculate \\(364 \\times 600 = 218400\\)\n   - Subtract \\(364 \\times 3 = 1092\\)\n   - Result: \\(218400 - 1092 = 217308\\)\n\n3. **Expanding Both Numbers:**\n   - Break down \\(364\\) into \\(300 + 60 + 4\\) and \\(597\\) into \\(500 + 90 + 7\\)\n   - Multiply each term and sum the results:\n     \\[\n     (300 \\times 500) + (300 \\times 90) + (300 \\times 7) + (60 \\times 500) + (60 \\times 90) + (60 \\times 7) + (4 \\times 500) + (4 \\times 90) + (4 \\times 7)\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     = 150000 + 27000 + 2100 + 30000 + 5400 + 420 + 2000 + 360 + 28 = 217308\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm the product of 364 and 597 is \\(\\boxed{217308}\\).",
