,800.\n\n947 \u00d7 2 = 1,894.\n\nAdding them together: 378,800 + 1,894 = 380,694. Yep, same result again.\n\nHmm, so I think that's correct then. Maybe I was just second-guessing myself unnecessarily, but better safe than sorry. Let me try one more time using a different approach, perhaps the lattice method or something else?\n\nAlternatively, maybe using estimation to check if 380,694 is reasonable.\n\nEstimate 947 is about 950 and 402 is about 400. 950 \u00d7 400 = 380,000. Since 947 is 3 less than 950 and 402 is 2 more than 400, the actual product should be a bit less than 380,000 minus some amount? Wait, no, actually, let's see:\n\nThe exact difference would be (950 - 3)*(400 + 2) = 950\u00d7400 + 950\u00d72 -3\u00d7400 -3\u00d72. Which is 380,000 + 1,900 - 1,200 -6 = 380,000 + 700 -6 = 380,694. Wait, that actually gives the exact value. So that's another way to see it.\n\nSo, the estimation approach actually gives the exact answer here because the numbers worked out nicely. So that confirms it again.\n\nTherefore, I think the correct product is 380,694. All methods are converging to that number, so I'm confident that's the right answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 947 and 402 is \\boxed{380694}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 947 and 402, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into smaller parts:\n\n1. Break down the numbers:\n   - \\(947 = 900 + 40 + 7\\)\n   - \\(402 = 400 + 2\\)\n\n2. Multiply each term in the first parentheses by each term in the second parentheses:\n   - \\(900 \\times 400 = 360,000\\)\n   - \\(900 \\times 2 = 1,800\\)\n   - \\(40 \\times 400 = 16,000\\)\n   - \\(40 \\times 2 = 80\\)\n   - \\(7 \\times 400 = 2,800\\)\n   - \\(7 \\times 2 = 14\\)\n\n3. Sum all the products:\n   \\[\n   360,000 + 1,800 + 16,000 + 80 + 2,800 + 14\n   \\]\n\n4. Perform the addition step-by-step:\n   - \\(360,000 + 1,800 = 361,800\\)\n   - \\(361,800 + 16,000 = 377,800\\)\n   - \\(377,800 + 80 = 377,880\\)\n   - \\(377,880 + 2,800 = 380,680\\)\n   - \\(380,680 + 14 = 380,694\\)\n\n5. Verification using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n   - Multiply \\(947\\) by \\(2\\) (units place): \\(947 \\times 2 = 1,894\\)\n   - Multiply \\(947\\) by \\(0\\) (tens place): \\(0\\) (shifted one position left)\n   - Multiply \\(947\\) by \\(4\\) (hundreds place): \\(947 \\times 4 = 3,788\\) (shifted two positions left, resulting in \\(378,800\\))\n   - Sum the results: \\(1,894 + 0 + 378,800 = 380,694\\)\n\nThus, the product of 947 and 402 is \\(\\boxed{380694}\\).",
