\n\nWait, just to be thorough, maybe I can check with a calculator. But since I can't use a calculator, perhaps I can approximate to see if it's reasonable.\n\n325 is approximately 300, 745 is approximately 700. 300\u00d7700=210,000. The actual numbers are a bit higher, so 325 is 25 more, and 745 is 45 more. So the approximate increase would be 25\u00d7700 + 300\u00d745 + 25\u00d745. Let's see:\n\n25\u00d7700 = 17,500\n\n300\u00d745 = 13,500\n\n25\u00d745 = 1,125\n\nAdding those up: 17,500 +13,500 = 31,000 +1,125=32,125. Adding to the original approximation 210,000 gives 242,125. Exactly the same. So that seems consistent.\n\nTherefore, I think the correct product is 242,125. I don't see any errors in my calculations, and both methods gave me the same result. So I'm confident that's the right answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 325 and 745 is \\boxed{242125}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 325 and 745, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into smaller parts and then adding the results together.\n\nFirst, we break down the numbers:\n- \\(325 = 300 + 25\\)\n- \\(745 = 700 + 45\\)\n\nUsing the distributive property:\n\\[\n(300 + 25) \\times (700 + 45) = 300 \\times 700 + 300 \\times 45 + 25 \\times 700 + 25 \\times 45\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term separately:\n1. \\(300 \\times 700 = 210000\\)\n2. \\(300 \\times 45 = 13500\\)\n3. \\(25 \\times 700 = 17500\\)\n4. \\(25 \\times 45 = 1125\\)\n\nAdding all the results together:\n\\[\n210000 + 13500 + 17500 + 1125\n\\]\n\nStep-by-step addition:\n1. \\(210000 + 13500 = 223500\\)\n2. \\(223500 + 17500 = 241000\\)\n3. \\(241000 + 1125 = 242125\\)\n\nTo verify, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n- Multiply 325 by 5: \\(325 \\times 5 = 1625\\)\n- Multiply 325 by 40 (since 4 is in the tens place): \\(325 \\times 40 = 13000\\)\n- Multiply 325 by 700 (since 7 is in the hundreds place): \\(325 \\times 700 = 227500\\)\n\nAdding these partial products:\n\\[\n1625 + 13000 + 227500 = 242125\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 325 and 745 is \\(\\boxed{242125}\\).",
