,208 is close to 153,000, so that seems plausible.\n\nAlternatively, let me compute 453 \u00d7 336 using another method. Let's see, maybe breaking down 336 as 300 + 36.\n\nSo 453\u00d7300 = 135,900, and 453\u00d736. Let's compute 453\u00d736.\n\n453\u00d736 can be broken into 453\u00d730 + 453\u00d76. Wait, that's similar to before. 453\u00d730 is 13,590 and 453\u00d76 is 2,718. Adding those gives 13,590 + 2,718 = 16,308. Then adding to the 135,900 gives again 152,208.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps compute 336\u00d7400, subtract 336\u00d747? Wait, maybe that's more complicated. 453 is 400 +53. Hmm. Alternatively, 336\u00d7453. Let me try multiplying 336 by 453.\n\nWait, maybe I can compute 336 \u00d7 450 + 336 \u00d7 3.\n\n336 \u00d7 450: 336 \u00d7 45 \u00d7 10. 336 \u00d745. Let me compute 336\u00d740 =13,440 and 336\u00d75=1,680. Adding those gives 13,440 +1,680 =15,120. Then times 10 is 151,200. Then 336\u00d73 is 1,008. Adding those gives 151,200 +1,008 =152,208. Yep, same result. Okay, so that confirms it again.\n\nHmm, so seems like 152,208 is the correct answer. Let me just do one more check with a calculator-like approach step by step.\n\nAlternatively, let's do straight multiplication:\n\n\u202f453  \n\u00d7336  \n------  \nFirst, multiply by 6:  \n453 \u00d76:  \n3\u00d76=18, write down 8 carryover 1  \n5\u00d76=30 +1=31, write 1 carryover3  \n4\u00d76=24 +3=27. So 2718.\n\nNext, multiply by 3 (the tens place, so it's 30):\n\n453 \u00d73 (but shifted one position to the left):  \n3\u00d73=9  \n5\u00d73=15, write 5 carryover1  \n4\u00d73=12 +1=13. So 1359, but shifted left once becomes 13590.\n\nMultiply by 3 (the hundreds place, so 300):\n\n453 \u00d73 (shifted two positions left):  \nSame as before 1359, shifted two becomes 135900.\n\nAdding all three:\n\n2718  \n13590  \n135900  \nTotal:\n\nStart with 2718 +13590:  \n2718 + 13590. Let's add 2718 + 13000 =15718, then +590 =16308.\n\nThen 16308 +135900: 16308 +135,900. \n\n135,900 + 16,308. \n\nAdding 135,900