imately 1000, so 1000 * 661 = 661,000. But since 980 is 20 less than 1000, so subtract 20*661 = 13,220. 661,000 - 13,220 = 647,780. Exactly the same as before. So that works.\n\nTherefore, I'm confident the answer is 647,780.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 980 and 661 is \\boxed{647780}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 980 and 661, we can use the standard multiplication method and verify it with different approaches:\n\n1. **Standard Multiplication:**\n   - Multiply 980 by 1 (units place): \\(980 \\times 1 = 980\\).\n   - Multiply 980 by 60 (tens place): \\(980 \\times 60 = 58,800\\).\n   - Multiply 980 by 600 (hundreds place): \\(980 \\times 600 = 588,000\\).\n   - Add the partial products:\n     \\[\n     980 + 58,800 + 588,000 = 647,780\n     \\]\n\n2. **Distributive Property:**\n   - Break down 980 and 661 using distributive property:\n     \\[\n     980 \\times 661 = (1000 - 20) \\times 661 = 1000 \\times 661 - 20 \\times 661\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each term:\n     \\[\n     1000 \\times 661 = 661,000 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 20 \\times 661 = 13,220\n     \\]\n   - Subtract the results:\n     \\[\n     661,000 - 13,220 = 647,780\n     \\]\n\n3. **Breaking Down Numbers:**\n   - Express 980 as \\(98 \\times 10\\) and use distributive property:\n     \\[\n     98 \\times 661 = (100 - 2) \\times 661 = 100 \\times 661 - 2 \\times 661\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each term:\n     \\[\n     100 \\times 661 = 66,100 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 2 \\times 661 = 1,322\n     \\]\n   - Subtract and multiply by 10:\n     \\[\n     66,100 - 1,322 = 64,778 \\quad \\text{then} \\quad 64,778 \\times 10 = 647,780\n     \\]\n\n4. **Expanding Both Numbers:**\n   - Break down both numbers and multiply each term:\n     \\[\n     (900 + 80) \\times (600 + 60 + 1)\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each term and sum them up:\n     \\[\n     540,000 + 54,000 + 900 + 48,000 + 4,800 + 80 = 647,780\n     \\]\n\nAll methods consistently yield the same result. Therefore, the product of 980 an