tial product here is 6642, but shifted two places to the left, so it becomes 664200.\n\nNow, adding up all the partial products:.\n\nFirst partial product: 3690  .\nSecond partial product: 0 (but shifted, so maybe written as 00000?)  .\nThird partial product: 664200  .\nWait, maybe I need to write them aligned properly. Let me structure it again.\n\nActually, when writing the partial products, the first one (from the 5) is 3690. The second one (from the 0) would be 0 shifted one place, so 00000 (but with a zero in the tens place). The third one (from the 9) is 6642 shifted two places, so 664200. Then adding them all together:.\n\n\u2003\u202f3690  .\n+\u202f00000  .\n+664200  .\n________.\n\nAdding the first two gives 3690 + 0 = 3690. Then 3690 + 664200. Let me add those. .\n\n664200 + 3690. Let's see:.\n\n664200 + 3000 = 667200. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
