rryover 5.\n\n4\u00d78=32 +5=37, write down 7, carryover 3. Wait, but 4 is in the hundreds place, so actually, 400\u00d78=3200, but when doing the step-by-step:\n\nWait, maybe I confused the order here. Let me actually write it properly:\n\nMultiplying 463 \u00d7 8:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\nUnits place: 3\u00d78=24. Write 4, carryover 2.\n\nTens place: 6\u00d78=48 +2=50. Write 0, carryover 5.\n\nHundreds place:4\u00d78=32 +5=37. Write 37.\n\nSo the first partial product is 3704. Correct.\n\nNext, multiplying by the tens digit (6 in the tens place, so 60):\n\n463\u00d76\u00d710 (since it's the tens place).\n\nSo first compute 463\u00d76:\n\nUnits place:3\u00d76=18, write 8, carryover 1.\n\nTens place:6\u00d76=36 +1=37, write 7, carryover 3.\n\nHundreds place:4\u00d76=24 +3=27, write 27.\n\nSo that gives 2778. Then, since it's the tens place, multiply by 10, so 27,780. That's the second partial product. Correct.\n\nThird partial product is 463\u00d71 (hundreds place, which is 100).\n\nSo 463\u00d71\u00d7100. 463\u00d71=463, then times 100 is 46,300. Correct.\n\nAdding them all:\n\n3704\n\n27780\n\n+46300\n\nLet's add them step by step again:\n\nFirst, 3704 + 27780. As before, that's 31,484.\n\nThen, 31,484 +46,300. Adding the two numbers:\n\n31,484 +46,300:\n\n31,000 +46,000 =77,000\n\n484 + 300 =784\n\nTotal 77,000 +784 =77,784. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another method, like the column addition:\n\nFirst, write all three numbers aligned:\n\n\u202f\u00a03704\n\n\u202f27780\n\n+46300\n\n----------\n\nStart from the rightmost digit:\n\nFirst number: 3704\n\nSecond: 27780\n\nThird:46300\n\nAligning:\n\n\u2003\u20033704\n\n\u200327780\n\n+46300\n\n------------\n\nLet me write them with commas for clarity:\n\n3,704\n\n27,780\n\n46,300\n\nAdding these:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units):\n\n4 (from 3,704) +0 (from 27,780) +0 (from46,300)=4\n\nTens place:\n\n0 (from 3,704) +8 (from27,780) +0 (from46,300)=8\n\nHundreds place:\n\n7 (from3,704) +7 (from27,780) +3 (from46,300)= 7+7=14, 14+3=17. Write down 7, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place:\n\n3 (from3,704) +7 (from27,780) +6 (from46,300)= 3+7=10, 10+6=16, plus the carried over 1 is 17. Write down 7, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands place:\n\n0 (from3,704) +2 (from27,780) +4 (from46,300)= 2+4=6, plus carried over 1 is 7.\n\nHundred-thousands place:\n\nOnly 4 from46,300? Wait, no, 46,300 is 4 ten thousands and 6 thousands. Wait, let me see:\n\nWait, 3,704 is 3 thousands, 7 hundreds, etc.\n\n27,780 is 2 ten thousands, 7 thousands, 7 hundreds, etc.\n\n46,300 is 4 ten thousands, 6 thousands, etc.\n\nWait, so ten thousands place:\n\nFor 3,704: 0 in ten thousands place.\n\nFor27,780: 2 in ten thousands.\n\nFor46,300:4 in ten thousands.\n\nSo adding those: 0 +2 +4=6, plus any carried over?\n\nWait, in the thousands place, we had 17, so carried over 1 to the ten thousands.\n\nWait, let me retrace:\n\nWhen adding the thousands place:\n\nThe thousands digits are:\n\nFrom 3,704: the thousands digit is 3 (since it's 3 thousands).\n\nFrom27,780: the thousands digit is7 (the second digit from the right in 27,780 is the thousands place: 2 (ten thousands),7 (thousands),7 (hundreds), etc.\n\nFrom46,300: the thousands digit is6 (since it's 4 ten thousands and 6 thousands).\n\nSo the thousands digits are 3,7,6. Sum is 3+7+6 =16, plus the carried over 1 from the hundreds place (which was 17, so carryover 1). So total is 17. So we write 7 in thousands place and carryover 1 to the ten thousands.\n\nThen the ten thousands place:\n\nDigits are 0 (from 3,704),2 (from27,780),4 (from46,300). So 0+2+4=6, plus the carried over 1 makes 7. So the ten thousands place is 7.\n\nThere are no digits beyond the ten thousands place except the 4 in 46,300 which is in the ten thousands place. Wait, actually the 4 in 46,300 is the ten thousands digit, so yes, that's accounted for.\n\nSo putting it all together, the total is 77,784. So that matches again.\n\nHmm, so after multiple methods and checks, I think the product is 77,784. I don't see any errors in my calculations. Let me just try one more verification, perhaps using calculator-like step-by-step.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another breakdown. Let me see:\n\n463 \u00d7 168 = (400 + 60 +3) \u00d7 (100 +60 +8). But expanding this would be tedious, but perhaps doing a couple terms to check.\n\nAlternatively, multiply 463\u00d7160 +463\u00d78.\n\nWait, 160 is 16\u00d710, so 463\u00d716\u00d710. Let's see:\n\n463\u00d716: 463\u00d710=4630; 463\u00d76=2778. So 4630+2778=7408. Then \u00d710=74,080. Then add 463\u00d78=3,704. So 74,080 +3,704=77,784. Same result again.\n\nAlright, so that's consistent. I think this is solid. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 463 and 168 is 77,784.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 463 and 168 is \\boxed{77784}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 463 and 168, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm by breaking it down into partial products and then summing them up.\n\nFirst, multiply 463 by 8:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n463 \\times 8 &= (400 \\times 8) + (60 \\times 8) + (3 \\times 8) \\\\\n&= 3200 + 480 + 24 \\\\\n&= 3704\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nNext, multiply 463 by 60 (since 6 is in the tens place):\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n463 \\times 60 &= (463 \\times 6) \\times 10 \\\\\n&= (2778) \\times 10 \\\\\n&= 27780\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nThen, multiply 463 by 100 (since 1 is in the hundreds place):\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n463 \\times 100 &= 46300\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nNow, sum all the partial products:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n3704 + 27780 + 46300 &= 3704 + 27780 + 46300 \\\\\n&= 31484 + 46300 \\\\\n&= 77784\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 463 and 168 is \\boxed{77784}.",
