ands place):.\n\nFirst number: 0.\n\nSecond number:0 (since 87,030 has no hundred thousands digit).\n\nThird number:5 (from 580,200).\n\nPlus the carryover 1: 5 +1 =6. Write down 6.\n\nAny higher digits? The third number has a hundred thousands place, so that's covered. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
