messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 250 and 948?', "<think>Okay, so I need to find the product of 250 and 948. Hmm, let me think about how to approach this. Multiplying large numbers can be tricky, but maybe I can break it down into smaller parts to make it easier. .\n\nFirst, I know that 250 times 948 is the same as 250 multiplied by 900 plus 250 multiplied by 48. That way, I can handle each part separately and then add the results together. Let me write that down:.\n\n250 × 948 = 250 × (900 + 48) = (250 × 900) + (250 × 48).\n\nAlright, starting with the first part, 250 multiplied by 900. Since 900 is 9 times 100, maybe I can simplify this. .\n\n250 × 900 = 250 × 9 × 100. .\n\nCalculating 250 × 9 first. Let me do that step by step. 250 times 9: 200 times 9 is 1800, and 50 times 9 is 450. Adding those together, 1800 + 450 = 2250. Then multiply by 100, so that's 2250 × 100 = 225,000. Okay, so the first part is 225,000.\n\nNow the second part: 250 × 48. Hmm, 48 can be broken down into 40 + 8. Let me try that.\n\n250 × 48 = 250 × (40 + 8) = (250 × 40) + (250 × 8).\n\nCalculating each term separately. .\n\nFirst, 250 × 40. Well, 250 times 4 is 1000, so 250 times 40 would be 1000 × 10 = 10,000. .\n\nNext, 250 × 8. That's straightforward: 250 × 8 = 2000. .\n\nAdding those two results together: 10,000 + 2000 = 12,000. .\n\nSo the second part is 12,000.\n\nNow, adding both parts together: 225,000 + 12,000. Let me add those. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
