      "text": "225,000 + 12,000 = 237,000. Wait, that seems straightforward, but let me verify to make sure I didn't make a mistake anywhere.\n\nLet me check using another method. Maybe using the standard multiplication algorithm. Let's write it out:\n\n       250\n    \u00d7 948\n    ______\n\nFirst, multiply 250 by 8. 250 \u00d7 8 = 2000. Write that down.\n\nThen multiply 250 by 40 (since the 4 is in the tens place, so it's actually 40). 250 \u00d7 40 = 10,000. But since it's the tens place, we need to shift one position to the left, so it's 10,000 \u00d7 10 = 100,000? Wait, no. Wait, actually, in standard multiplication, when you multiply by the tens digit, you shift one place. Let me correct that. \n\nWait, actually, let me do it step by step properly. \n\nMultiplying 250 by 948. Let's break it down digit by digit.\n\nStarting with the units place:\n\nFirst step: Multiply 250 by 8 (units place): \n\n250 \u00d7 8 = 2000.\n\nSecond step: Multiply 250 by 4 (tens place). Since it's the tens place, it's actually 40. So 250 \u00d7 40 = 10,000. But in the standard algorithm, you write it shifted one position to the left, so it's like 250 \u00d7 4 (which is 1000) and then add a zero at the end, making it 10,000. \n\nThird step: Multiply 250 by 9 (hundreds place). Since it's the hundreds place, it's actually 900. So 250 \u00d7 900 = 225,000. Again, in the standard algorithm, you write it shifted two positions to the left (because it's the hundreds place). \n\nNow, adding all three results:\n\n2000 (from units)\n+10,000 (from tens)\n+225,000 (from hundreds)\n= Total?\n\nAdding 2000 + 10,000 = 12,000; then 12,000 + 225,000 = 237,000. Okay, same result. So that's consistent. \n\nAlternatively, maybe another way to check is using the distributive property differently. Let's see:\n\n250 \u00d7 948 can also be thought of as 250 \u00d7 (950 - 2). Because 950 minus 2 is 948. \n\nSo, 250 \u00d7 950 = ?\n\nWell, 250 \u00d7 950. Since 950 is 95 \u00d7 10, so 250 \u00d7 95 \u00d7 10. \n\n250 \u00d7 95: Maybe split 95 into 100 - 5. \n\n250 \u00d7 (100 - 5) = 250\u00d7100 - 250\u00d75 = 25,000 - 1,250 = 23,750. \n\nThen multiply by 10: 23,750 \u00d7 10 = 237,500. \n\nThen subtract 250\u00d72 (since we did 250\u00d7(950 - 2)), so subtract 500. \n\n237,500 - 500 = 237,000. \n\nSame answer again. Okay, so that method also gives me 237,000. \n\nHmm, seems like all methods are converging to 237,000. Maybe that's correct. \n\nWait, but just to be thorough, maybe do a quick estimate. \n\n250 is a quarter of 1000, right? So 250 \u00d7 948 is like (1000/4) \u00d7 948 = 948,000 / 4. \n\nDivide 948,000 by 4: 948 divided by 4 is 237, so 948,000 divided by 4 is 237,000. Exactly. \n\nSo that's another way to see it. So the answer is definitely 237,000. \n\nI think that's solid. I tried three different methods: breaking into hundreds and tens, standard multiplication algorithm, and using the relationship with 1000. All give the same result. So I can be confident that the product of 250 and 948 is 237,000.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 250 and 948 is \\boxed{237000}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 250 and 948, we can use the distributive property to break it down into smaller parts:\n\n\\[\n250 \\times 948 = 250 \\times (900 + 48) = (250 \\times 900) + (250 \\times 48)\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(250 \\times 900\\):\n\\[\n250 \\times 900 = 250 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 2250 \\times 100 = 225000\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(250 \\times 48\\):\n\\[\n250 \\times 48 = 250 \\times (40 + 8) = (250 \\times 40) + (250 \\times 8)\n\\]\n\\[\n250 \\times 40 = 10000 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 250 \\times 8 = 2000\n\\]\n\\[\n10000 + 2000 = 12000\n\\]\n\nAdd the two results together:\n\\[\n225000 + 12000 = 237000\n\\]\n\nVerification using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n     250 \\\\\n\\times 948 \\\\\n\\hline\n     2000 \\quad (\\text{250} \\times 8) \\\\\n    10000 \\quad (\\text{250} \\times 40) \\\\\n+ 225000 \\quad (\\text{250} \\times 900) \\\\\n\\hline\n    237000 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nAnother method using the relationship with 1000:\n\\[\n250 \\times 948 = \\frac{1000}{4} \\times 948 = \\frac{948000}{4} = 237000\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm the result is the same. Therefore, the product of 250 and 948 is \\(\\boxed{237000}\\).",
