0 +9,804 = 89,604. Exactly the same result again.\n\nHmm, seems like all methods are converging to 89,604. So maybe that is correct. But let me do the multiplication step-by-step once again, just to be thorough.\n\nStarting with the vertical multiplication:\n\nFirst, write down the numbers:\n\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 786\n\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00d7114\n\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 ---------\n\nMultiply 786 by 4 (units place):\n\n4\u00d76=24, write down 4, carryover 2.\n\n4\u00d78=32 +2=34, write down 4, carryover 3.\n\n4\u00d77=28 +3=31, write down 31. So first partial product is 3,144.\n\nNext, multiply 786 by 1 (tens place). Since it's the tens place, we shift one position to the left:\n\n1\u00d76=6, write down 6 in the tens column (so actually the second digit from the right, but shifted left once). Wait, let's do it properly:\n\nMultiplying by the tens digit (the middle 1 in 114), so:\n\n1\u00d76 = 6, but since it's the tens place, the result is in the tens column, so it's 60? Wait, perhaps writing it out:\n\nPartial product for the tens digit (1 in tens place):\n\n1\u00d7786 = 786, but shifted one place to the left, so it becomes 7,860.\n\nSo writing it as:\n\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 786\n\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00d7114\n\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 ---------\n\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 3144\n\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 7860\n\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a078600\n\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0--------\n\nAdding these up.\n\nWait, the third partial product is multiplying by the hundreds digit (1 in hundreds place), so 1\u00d7786 shifted two places left, which is 78,600.\n\nSo adding them all:\n\n3,144\n\n+7,860 = 11,004\n\n11,004 +78,600 = 89,604. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do it all in one go:\n\n3,144 (from units)\n7,860 (from tens, shifted)\n78,600 (from hundreds, shifted)\n\nTotal is 3,144 + 7,860 = 11,004; 11,004 +78,600=89,604.\n\nAlright, so all these 