en 900\u00d7600 and 879\u00d7570 is:\n\n900\u00d7600 =540,000\n\n879\u00d7570 = ?\n\nThe difference would be 900\u00d7600 - 879\u00d7570 = ?\n\nBut maybe not necessary. The estimation is just to check if 501k is in the ballpark. Since 501,030 is 540,000 minus approximately (21\u00d7600 + 30\u00d7879 - 21\u00d730). Hmm, but perhaps not needed. Since two exact calculations give the same, I think it's safe.\n\nTherefore, the product of 879 and 570 is 501,030.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 879 and 570 is \\boxed{501030}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 879 and 570, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers:\n\n1. Break down 570 into 500 and 70:\n   \\[\n   879 \\times 570 = 879 \\times (500 + 70)\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate each part separately:\n   - First part: \\(879 \\times 500\\)\n     \\[\n     879 \\times 500 = 879 \\times 5 \\times 100 = 4395 \\times 100 = 439500\n     \\]\n   - Second part: \\(879 \\times 70\\)\n     \\[\n     879 \\times 70 = 879 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 6153 \\times 10 = 61530\n     \\]\n\n3. Add the results of the two parts:\n   \\[\n   439500 + 61530 = 501030\n   \\]\n\n4. Verification by reversing the multiplication (570 \u00d7 879):\n   - \\(570 \\times 800 = 456000\\)\n   - \\(570 \\times 70 = 39900\\)\n   - \\(570 \\times 9 = 5130\\)\n   - Adding these results:\n     \\[\n     456000 + 39900 + 5130 = 501030\n     \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 879 and 570 is \\(\\boxed{501030}\\).",
