on algorithm and verify using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, we break down the multiplication using the distributive property:\n\\[\n(500 + 3)(700 + 60 + 2)\n\\]\nExpanding this, we get:\n\\[\n500 \\times 700 + 500 \\times 60 + 500 \\times 2 + 3 \\times 700 + 3 \\times 60 + 3 \\times 2\n\\]\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n500 \\times 700 &= 350000, \\\\\n500 \\times 60 &= 30000, \\\\\n500 \\times 2 &= 1000, \\\\\n3 \\times 700 &= 2100, \\\\\n3 \\times 60 &= 180, \\\\\n3 \\times 2 &= 6.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\nAdding these results together:\n\\[\n350000 + 30000 + 1000 + 2100 + 180 + 6 = 383286\n\\]\n\nWe can also verify this using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n     503 \\\\\n\\times 762 \\\\\n\\hline\n    1006 \\quad (\\text{503} \\times 2) \\\\\n   30180 \\quad (\\text{503} \\times 60) \\\\\n352100 \\quad (\\text{503} \\times 700) \\\\\n\\hline\n383286 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\nAdding the partial products:\n\\[\n1006 + 30180 + 352100 = 383286\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 503 and 762 is \\(\\boxed{383286}\\).",
