00 +13,840 = 83,040. Then +692 gives 83,732. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe compute 692 \u00d7121 as (700 -8) \u00d7121. Let's see if that's easier.\n\nExpanding that would be 700\u00d7121 -8\u00d7121. \n\n700\u00d7121: 700\u00d7100=70,000; 700\u00d720=14,000; 700\u00d71=700. Adding those: 70,000 +14,000 =84,000 +700 =84,700.\n\nThen subtract 8\u00d7121. 8\u00d7120=960, plus 8\u00d71=8, so 968. \n\nTherefore, 84,700 - 968 = ?\n\nCompute 84,700 - 968:\n\nSubtract 1,000 from 84,700 to get 83,700, but since we subtracted 32 more (because 968 is 32 less than 1000), add back 32: 83,700 +32 = 83,732. \n\nWow, that also gives the same answer. Okay, so that's another method and still the same result. So I think that confirms it.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check using prime factors? Hmm, not sure if that's easier here. Let's see.\n\n692 can be factored: 692 divided by 2 is 346, divided by 2 again is 173. 173 is a prime number, I think. Let me check: 173 divided by primes up to sqrt(173) which is about 13.1. 2,3,5,7,11,13. 173/2 no, 173/3 is 57.666, nope, 5? ends with 3, no. 7? 173/7 \u224824.7, nope. 11? 15.7, 13? 13\u00d713 is 169, 13\u00d714=182. So yes, 173 is prime. So 692 is 2\u00d72\u00d7173.\n\n121 is 11\u00d711. \n\nSo, multiplying together, the product is 2\u00d72\u00d7173\u00d711\u00d711. Not sure if that helps in calculating the actual number, but maybe rearranging?\n\nLet me see: 2\u00d711 =22, so two of the factors can be 2\u00d711=22, and another 2\u00d711=22. So, (22\u00d722) \u00d7 (173). 22\u00d722 is 484, so 484\u00d7173. Hmm, that might not be easier, but let me see:\n\n484 \u00d7 173. Let's compute that.\n\nBreakdown:\n\n484 \u00d7 100 =48,400  \n484 \u00d770 =33,880  \n484 \u00d73 =1,452  \n\nAdding them together: 48,400 +33,880 =82,280. Then +1,452 =83,732. \n\nSame result! So that also gives 83,732. Okay, this is getting redundant but in a good way. It's consistent across multiple methods, so I must be correct.\n\nI think that's thorough enough. All different methods lead to 83,732, so I can be confident that's the right answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 692 and 121 is \\boxed{83732}.\n</think>\n\nTo solve the product of 692 and 121, we can use the distributive property and break down the multiplication into smaller, manageable parts.\n\nFirst, we split 121 into 120 and 1:\n\\[\n692 \\times 121 = 692 \\times (120 + 1) = (692 \\times 120) + (692 \\times 1)\n\\]\n\nCalculating \\(692 \\times 120\\):\n\\[\n692 \\times 120 = 692 \\times (12 \\times 10) = (692 \\times 12) \\times 10\n\\]\nBreaking down \\(692 \\times 12\\):\n\\[\n692 \\times 12 = 692 \\times (10 + 2) = (692 \\times 10) + (692 \\times 2) = 6920 + 1384 = 8304\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\n692 \\times 120 = 8304 \\times 10 = 83040\n\\]\n\nNext, calculating \\(692 \\times 1\\):\n\\[\n692 \\times 1 = 692\n\\]\n\nAdding the two results together:\n\\[\n83040 + 692 = 83732\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we use another method by breaking down 121 into 100, 20, and 1:\n\\[\n692 \\times 121 = 692 \\times (100 + 20 + 1) = (692 \\times 100) + (692 \\times 20) + (692 \\times 1)\n\\]\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n692 \\times 100 = 69200\n\\]\n\\[\n692 \\times 20 = 13840\n\\]\n\\[\n692 \\times 1 = 692\n\\]\n\nAdding these results:\n\\[\n69200 + 13840 + 692 = 83732\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the product is consistent. Therefore, the product of 692 and 121 is \\(\\boxed{83732}\\).",
