ens place, so it's 20, so we shift one position left.\n\nMultiply 317 \u00d72 (for the 20), so same as before 634, but shifted one left: 6340.\n\nThen the hundreds digit (the first 2 from the right, which is the hundreds place, so 200). So multiply 317\u00d72 again, getting 634, shifted two places left: 63400.\n\nAdding them all:.\n\nFirst partial product: 634.\n\nSecond: 6340.\n\nThird: 63400.\n\nAdding first two: 634 +6340 = 6974.\n\nThen 6974 +63400: 6974 +63,400. Let's see, 6974 + 60,000 =66,974. Then add 3,400 more: 66,974 +3,400 =70,374. Exactly. So that's consistent.\n\nHmm, okay. I think that's solid. Therefore, the product of 317 and 222 is 70,374.\n\nWait, just to make sure I didn't make any addition errors. Let me add the three partial products again:\n\n634 (units)\n\n+6340 (tens)\n\n+63400 (hundreds).\n\nAdding 634 and 6340 first. 634 + 6340.\n\nLet me write it vertically:\n\n   634.\n\n+6340.\n\n--------\n\nAligning the numbers:\n\n  634.\n\n+6340.\n\n= ?\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n4 + 0 =4.\n\n3 +4=7.\n\n6 +3=9.\n\n0 +6=6 (since 6340 has a 6 in the thousands place).\n\nSo total is 6,974.\n\nThen adding 63,400:\n\n6,974\n\n+63,400\n\n= ?\n\nAdding vertically:\n\n  6,974\n\n+63,400\n\n--------\n\nAligning:\n\n   6,974\n\n+63,400\n\n= ?\n\nUnits:4+0=4\n\nTens:7+0=7\n\nHundreds:9+4=13, write 3, carryover 1\n\nThousands: 6 + 3=9 plus 1 carried over is 10, write 0 carryover 1\n\nTen-thousands: 0 +6=6 plus carried over 1 is 7.\n\nSo total is 70,374. Yep, that's the same as before.\n\nTherefore, after multiple checks, I believe the answer is 70,374. I can't see any mistakes in my calculations, and the cross-verification methods all lead to the same result. So I think that's the correct product.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 317 and 222 is \\boxed{70374}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 317 and 222, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 317 by the units digit (2):**\n   \\[\n   317 \\times 2 = 634\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 317 by the tens digit (20):**\n   \\[\n   317 \\times 20 = 6340\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 317 by the hundreds digit (200):**\n   \\[\n   317 \\times 200 = 63400\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   634 + 6340 + 63400\n   \\]\n\n   - Adding the first two partial products:\n     \\[\n     634 + 6340 = 6974\n     \\]\n\n   - Adding the result to the third partial product:\n     \\[\n     6974 + 63400 = 70374\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 317 and 222 is \\(\\boxed{70374}\\).",
