96. I think that's solid. I don't see any miscalculations in my steps, so I feel confident this is the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 318 and 372 is \\boxed{118296}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 318 and 372, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify through multiple methods:\n\n1. **Standard Multiplication Algorithm:**\n   - Multiply 318 by 2: \n     \\[\n     318 \\times 2 = 636\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 318 by 70 (which is 318 \u00d7 7 \u00d7 10):\n     \\[\n     318 \\times 7 = 2226 \\quad \\text{(then add a zero)} \\quad 22260\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 318 by 300 (which is 318 \u00d7 3 \u00d7 100):\n     \\[\n     318 \\times 3 = 954 \\quad \\text{(then add two zeros)} \\quad 95400\n     \\]\n   - Add the results together:\n     \\[\n     636 + 22260 + 95400 = 118296\n     \\]\n\n2. **Verification using Distributive Property:**\n   - Break down the numbers into components:\n     \\[\n     (300 + 18)(300 + 72) = 300 \\times 300 + 300 \\times 72 + 18 \\times 300 + 18 \\times 72\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each term:\n     \\[\n     300 \\times 300 = 90000, \\quad 300 \\times 72 = 21600, \\quad 18 \\times 300 = 5400, \\quad 18 \\times 72 = 1296\n     \\]\n   - Sum the terms:\n     \\[\n     90000 + 21600 + 5400 + 1296 = 118296\n     \\]\n\n3. **Alternative Verification:**\n   - Express 372 as \\(400 - 28\\):\n     \\[\n     318 \\times (400 - 28) = 318 \\times 400 - 318 \\times 28\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each term:\n     \\[\n     318 \\times 400 = 127200, \\quad 318 \\times 28 = 8904\n     \\]\n   - Subtract the results:\n     \\[\n     127200 - 8904 = 118296\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 318 and 372 is \\(\\boxed{118296}\\).",
