hods are giving me the same answer, so I think that's solid.\n\nWait, but just to be thorough, let me check using another multiplication method, maybe the lattice method or something else. Hmm, maybe the grid method?\n\nLet me try the grid method for multiplication. Let's split both numbers into their hundreds, tens, and units.\n\n604 can be split into 600 + 4,\n\n215 can be split into 200 + 10 + 5.\n\nSo creating a grid:\n\n```.\n        | 600   | 4    |\n-----------------------\n200     |       |      |\n-----------------------\n10      |       |      |\n-----------------------\n5       |       |      |\n```.\n\nNow multiply each pair:\n\n600\u00d7200 = 120,000,\n\n600\u00d710 = 6,000,\n\n600\u00d75 = 3,000,\n\n4\u00d7200 = 800,\n\n4\u00d710 = 40,\n\n4\u00d75 = 20.\n\nNow add all these products together:\n\n120,000 + 6,000 + 3,000 + 800 + 40 + 20.\n\nAdding step by step:\n\n120,000 + 6,000 = 126,000,\n\n126,000 + 3,000 = 129,000,\n\n129,000 + 800 = 129,800,\n\n129,800 + 40 = 129,840,\n\n129,840 + 20 = 129,860.\n\nAgain, the same result. Hmm, okay, so all these different methods are leading me to 129,860, so I think that's the right answer.\n\nJust to be extra cautious, maybe I can reverse the multiplication: 215 \u00d7 604 and see if I get the same result.\n\nLet's compute 215 \u00d7 604.\n\nAgain, using standard algorithm:\n\n215 \u00d7 604.\n\nMultiply 215 by 4 (units place): 215\u00d74 = 860.\n\nMultiply 215 by 0 (tens place, but since it's the tens place, we need to shift one zero, but since the digit is 0, that term will be 0. Wait, actually, 604's tens digit is 0, so 215 \u00d7 0 (tens place) is 0 shifted one place, so 0.\n\nThen multiply 215 by 6 (hundreds place) which is 215\u00d76 = 1,290, then shift two places (because it's the hundreds place), so 129,000.\n\nAdding the three results: 860 + 0 + 129,000 = 129,860. Same answer. Perfect, that confirms it.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do 215 \u00d7 600 + 215 \u00d74 as before, which gives 129,000 +860=129,860. Yep.\n\nAlright, so after multiple methods and cross-verifying, I'm confident that the product of 604 and 215 is 129,860.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 604 and 215 is \\boxed{129860}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 604 and 215, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify with different methods:\n\n1. **Standard Multiplication Algorithm:**\n   - Multiply 604 by 5 (units place of 215):\n     \\[\n     604 \\times 5 = 3020\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 604 by 10 (tens place of 215):\n     \\[\n     604 \\times 10 = 6040\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 604 by 200 (hundreds place of 215):\n     \\[\n     604 \\times 200 = 120800\n     \\]\n   - Add the results:\n     \\[\n     3020 + 6040 + 120800 = 129860\n     \\]\n\n2. **Distributive Property:**\n   - Break down 215 into 200, 10, and 5:\n     \\[\n     604 \\times 215 = 604 \\times (200 + 10 + 5)\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each part:\n     \\[\n     604 \\times 200 = 120800, \\quad 604 \\times 10 = 6040, \\quad 604 \\times 5 = 3020\n     \\]\n   - Sum the results:\n     \\[\n     120800 + 6040 + 3020 = 129860\n     \\]\n\n3. **Grid Method:**\n   - Split both numbers into hundreds, tens, and units:\n     \\[\n     604 = 600 + 4 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 215 = 200 + 10 + 5\n     \\]\n   - Multiply each pair and sum the results:\n     \\[\n     600 \\times 200 = 120000, \\quad 600 \\times 10 = 6000, \\quad 600 \\times 5 = 3000\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     4 \\times 200 = 800, \\quad 4 \\times 10 = 40, \\quad 4 \\times 5 = 20\n     \\]\n   - Add all products:\n     \\[\n     120000 + 6000 + 3000 + 800 + 40 + 20 = 129860\n     \\]\n\n4. **Reverse Multiplication:**\n   - Multiply 215 by 604:\n     \\[\n     215 \\times 604 = (215 \\times 600) + (215 \\times 4) = 129000 + 860 = 129860\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 604 and 215 is \\(\\boxed{129860}\\).",
