 is approximately 400, and 868 is approximately 870. 400\u00d7870 = 348,000. Since both numbers were rounded up, the actual product should be a bit less than 348,000. 344,596 is 3,404 less, which makes sense, since we subtracted 3\u00d7870 (2,610) and 400\u00d72 (800), so total subtraction is 3,410, which is close. So that approximation checks out.\n\nAlternatively, 397 is 3 less than 400, so the difference would be 3*(868) subtracted from 400*868. So 400*868 is 347,200. Then subtract 3\u00d7868 = 2,604. So 347,200 - 2,604 = 344,596. Same result again.\n\nTherefore, I can be confident that the product is 344,596.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 397 and 868 is \\boxed{344596}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 397 and 868, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here are the key steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 397 by 8 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   397 \\times 8 = 3176\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 397 by 6 (tens place) and shift one position to the left:**\n   \\[\n   397 \\times 6 = 2382 \\quad \\text{(shifted left gives 23820)}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 397 by 8 (hundreds place) and shift two positions to the left:**\n   \\[\n   397 \\times 8 = 3176 \\quad \\text{(shifted left twice gives 317600)}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     3176 \\\\\n   + 23820 \\\\\n   +317600 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     344596 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\nTo verify, we can use the distributive property:\n\\[\n(400 - 3) \\times (800 + 60 + 8)\n\\]\nExpanding and simplifying:\n\\[\n400 \\times 800 + 400 \\times 60 + 400 \\times 8 - 3 \\times 800 - 3 \\times 60 - 3 \\times 8\n\\]\n\\[\n= 320000 + 24000 + 3200 - 2400 - 180 - 24\n\\]\n\\[\n= 347200 - 2604 = 344596\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the product is \\(\\boxed{344596}\\).",
