rray}\n   \\]\n   Calculation: \\(188 \\times 9 = 1692\\).\n\n2. **Multiply 188 by 40 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     188 \\\\\n   \\times 40 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     7520 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   Calculation: \\(188 \\times 4 = 752\\), then shift one position left: \\(752 \\times 10 = 7520\\).\n\n3. **Multiply 188 by 500 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     188 \\\\\n   \\times 500 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     94000 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   Calculation: \\(188 \\times 5 = 940\\), then shift two positions left: \\(940 \\times 100 = 94000\\).\n\n4. **Add all partial products:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     1692 \\\\\n   + 7520 \\\\\n   +94000 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     103212 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   - Adding \\(1692 + 7520 = 9212\\)\n   - Then adding \\(9212 + 94000 = 103212\\)\n\nVerification using different methods (distributive property and algebraic identity) confirms the result.\n\n### Final Answer\nThe product of 188 and 549 is \\boxed{103212}.",
