\u00d770: 699\u00d77\u00d710.\n\n699\u00d77: 700\u00d77=4,900 minus 1\u00d77=7, so 4,900 -7=4,893. Multiply by 10 gives 48,930.\n\n699\u00d75 is 3,495, as before.\n\nAdding those: 48,930 +3,495 =52,425.\n\nThen add that to the 559,200 from the first part: 559,200 +52,425=611,625. Same result again. So that's good.\n\nHmm, so seems like the answer is 611,625.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another method, like the difference of squares or something else? Let me see.\n\nWait, 699 is 700-1, and 875 is... Well, 875 is 700-125? Not sure. Alternatively, 875 is 7\u00d7125, since 7\u00d7125=875. Let me note that.\n\nSo 699 \u00d7 875 = 699 \u00d7 7 \u00d7 125.\n\nLet me compute 699 \u00d77 first, then multiply by 125.\n\n699 \u00d77: 700\u00d77=4900, minus 1\u00d77=7, so 4900 -7=4893.\n\nThen, 4893 \u00d7125. Hmm, 125 is 1000/8, so maybe that can be helpful?\n\nYes, because multiplying by 125 is the same as multiplying by 1000 and dividing by 8. Let me try that.\n\nSo 4893 \u00d7 125 = 4893 \u00d7 (1000/8) = (4893 \u00d71000)/8 = 4,893,000 /8.\n\nDividing 4,893,000 by 8: Let's compute that.\n\nDivide step by step:\n\n4,893,000 \u00f78:\n\nFirst, 4,000,000 \u00f78 =500,000.\n\nThen 893,000 \u00f78: 800,000 \u00f78=100,000. So 893,000=800,000 +93,000.\n\nSo 100,000 + (93,000 \u00f78). 93,000 \u00f78 is 11,625 (since 8\u00d711,625=93,000). Wait, 8\u00d711,625 = 93,000?\n\nWait, 11,625 \u00d78: 10,000\u00d78=80,000; 1,625\u00d78=13,000. So total would be 80,000 +13,000=93,000. Yes. So 93,000\u00f78=11,625. So total is 100,000 +11,625=111,625.\n\nTherefore, adding the initial 500,000 +111,625 =611,625. So again the same result.\n\nWow, so that method also works. So, that's a third way to confirm it.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another approach, like the lattice method? Hmm, but that might take longer. Alternatively, perhaps check with a calculator?\n\nBut since I don't have a calculator here, but since all methods so far give me 611,625, I think that's solid. Let me just confirm once again with another breakdown.\n\nAlternatively, maybe 875 \u00d7 700 = 612,500, then subtract 875, so 612,500 -875 =611,625. Which is exactly what I did first. So that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I can note that 699 \u00d7875 = (700 -1)\u00d7875 = 700\u00d7875 -875. Which is exactly the first method. So all methods converge to the same answer.\n\nHmm, so I think I can be confident that the product is 611,625. I don't see any mistakes in the calculations, and cross-verified with multiple methods. Therefore, I think that's the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 699 and 875 is \\boxed{611625}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 699 and 875, we can use the distributive property by breaking down 699 into 700 - 1:\n\n\\[\n699 \\times 875 = (700 - 1) \\times 875\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(700 \\times 875\\):\n\n\\[\n700 \\times 875 = 7 \\times 100 \\times 875 = 7 \\times 875 \\times 100\n\\]\n\nBreaking down \\(7 \\times 875\\):\n\n\\[\n7 \\times 800 = 5600 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 7 \\times 75 = 525\n\\]\n\\[\n5600 + 525 = 6125\n\\]\n\\[\n6125 \\times 100 = 612500\n\\]\n\nNext, subtract \\(1 \\times 875\\) from the result:\n\n\\[\n612500 - 875 = 611625\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can use another method by breaking down 875 into \\(800 + 75\\):\n\n\\[\n699 \\times 800 + 699 \\times 75\n\\]\n\nCalculating each part:\n\n\\[\n699 \\times 800 = 559200 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 699 \\times 75 = 52425\n\\]\n\\[\n559200 + 52425 = 611625\n\\]\n\nAnother verification using the fact that \\(875 = 7 \\times 125\\):\n\n\\[\n699 \\times 7 \\times 125 = 4893 \\times 125 = \\frac{4893 \\times 1000}{8} = \\frac{4893000}{8} = 611625\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm the result. The product of 699 and 875 is \\(\\boxed{611625}\\).",
