64 \u00d7 806. Let me check with another method to see if I get the same answer, just in case I made a mistake in the difference of squares approach.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do standard multiplication:\n\n864 \u00d7 806.\n\nLet me break down 806 as 800 + 6. So 864 \u00d7 800 + 864 \u00d76.\n\nFirst, 864 \u00d7 800: 864 \u00d78 \u00d7100. 864 \u00d78: 800\u00d78=6400, 64\u00d78=512, so total is 6400+512=6912. Then \u00d7100 is 691,200.\n\nThen 864 \u00d76: 800\u00d76=4,800; 64\u00d76=384; total is 4,800 + 384 = 5,184.\n\nAdding both parts: 691,200 +5,184 = 696,384. Okay, that's the same result as before. So that's reassuring.\n\nSo both methods give me 696,384, so that must be the correct answer. \n\nAlternatively, I can also check using another method, maybe the distributive property in another way. Let's see, 864\u00d7806. Maybe write them as (800 + 64)*(800 +6). Wait, but that might complicate, but let's try.\n\nWait, (800 +64)(800 +6) = 800\u00d7800 + 800\u00d76 +64\u00d7800 +64\u00d76. Let's compute each term:\n\n800\u00d7800 = 640,000\n\n800\u00d76 = 4,800\n\n64\u00d7800 = 51,200 (since 64\u00d78=512, so \u00d7100)\n\n64\u00d76 = 384.\n\nAdding all together: 640,000 +4,800 = 644,800; plus 51,200 gives 696,000; plus 384 gives 696,384. Yep, same answer. So that's consistent.\n\nTherefore, I can be confident that the product of 864 and 806 is 696,384.\n\nWait, but let me also confirm with the difference of squares approach again to see if I messed up any step there. The key step was expressing the numbers as (a + b)(a - b). \n\nOriginal numbers: 864 and 806. The average was (864 + 806)/2 = 1670/2 = 835. Correct. The difference between them is 864 -806 =58, so half of that is 29. Therefore, 864 =835 +29 and 806=835 -29. So the product is indeed 835\u00b2 -29\u00b2. \n\nCalculating 835 squared:\n\nBreaking down 835 squared: 800\u00b2 + 2*800*35 +35\u00b2. Which is 640,000 + 56,000 + 1,225 = 640,000 +56,000 is 696,000; plus 1,225 is 697,225. Correct.\n\n29 squared is