orrect.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 864 and 806 is \\boxed{696384}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 864 and 806, we can use the difference of squares formula. \n\nFirst, we note that the numbers 864 and 806 can be expressed as \\( (a + b) \\) and \\( (a - b) \\) where \\( a \\) is the average of the two numbers and \\( b \\) is half their difference. \n\n1. Calculate the average of 864 and 806:\n   \\[\n   a = \\frac{864 + 806}{2} = \\frac{1670}{2} = 835\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate half the difference of 864 and 806:\n   \\[\n   b = \\frac{864 - 806}{2} = \\frac{58}{2} = 29\n   \\]\n\n3. Express the product using the difference of squares formula:\n   \\[\n   (a + b)(a - b) = a^2 - b^2\n   \\]\n   Substituting \\( a = 835 \\) and \\( b = 29 \\):\n   \\[\n   835^2 - 29^2\n   \\]\n\n4. Calculate \\( 835^2 \\):\n   \\[\n   835^2 = (800 + 35)^2 = 800^2 + 2 \\cdot 800 \\cdot 35 + 35^2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 640000 + 56000 + 1225 = 697225\n   \\]\n\n5. Calculate \\( 29^2 \\):\n   \\[\n   29^2 = 841\n   \\]\n\n6. Subtract the squares:\n   \\[\n   697225 - 841 = 696384\n   \\]\n\nTo verify, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n1. Break down the multiplication:\n   \\[\n   864 \\times 806 = 864 \\times (800 + 6) = 864 \\times 800 + 864 \\times 6\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   864 \\times 800 = 691200 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 864 \\times 6 = 5184\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   691200 + 5184 = 696384\n   \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the product is \\(\\boxed{696384}\\).",
