t.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 666 and 338 is \\boxed{225108}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 666 and 338, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm by breaking down the multiplication into partial products and then summing them up.\n\nFirst, we compute the partial products:\n1. Multiply 666 by 8 (units place of 338):\n   \\[\n   666 \\times 8 = 5328\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 666 by 30 (tens place of 338, which is 3 \\times 10):\n   \\[\n   666 \\times 30 = 19980\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 666 by 300 (hundreds place of 338, which is 3 \\times 100):\n   \\[\n   666 \\times 300 = 199800\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum these partial products:\n1. Add the first two partial products:\n   \\[\n   5328 + 19980 = 25308\n   \\]\n2. Add the result to the third partial product:\n   \\[\n   25308 + 199800 = 225108\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 666 and 338 is \\(\\boxed{225108}\\).",
