ndreds), 1 (tens), 6 (units). Wait, that gives 173,316?\n\nWait, let me check again:\n\nWait, the thousands place after carryover:\n\nOriginal thousands digits: in 171600, the thousands digit is 1 (since 171,600 is 1 (100,000), 7 (10,000), 1 (1,000)), so the thousands digit is 1. The thousands digit in 1,716 is 1 (the first digit from the right is units, then tens, hundreds, thousands). So adding those two thousands digits: 1 + 1 = 2, plus the carryover 1 from the hundreds place makes 3. So thousands digit is 3.\n\nThen the ten-thousands place: 7 (from 171,600) and 0 (since 1,716 doesn't have a ten-thousands digit). So 7 remains.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 1 from 171,600 and 0 from 1,716. So total is 1.\n\nSo the result is 1 (hundred-thousands), 7 (ten-thousands), 3 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 6 (units). So 173,316.\n\nHmm, so that would mean the total is 173,316? But I thought earlier I had 173,316. Wait, but when I did the first addition, I thought 171,600 + 1,716 is 173,316? But initially, I thought maybe 172,600 + 716, which would be different. Maybe I confused the numbers. Let me check again:\n\nWait, 171,600 plus 1,716. Let's do it step by step:\n\n171,600 + 1,000 = 172,600\n\nThen add 716: 172,600 + 700 = 173,300, plus 16 is 173,316. Yes, that's correct.\n\nWait, so why did I get confused earlier? Maybe I made a miscalculation when I first tried adding. So the total product should be 173,316. But let me verify this another way to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do the multiplication the standard way:\n\nMultiplying 303 by 572.\n\nFirst, write it down as:\n\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0303\n\nx\u00a0\u00a0572\n\n------------\n\nMultiply 303 by 2: 606\n\nMultiply 303 by 70: 21,210 (since 303*7=2,121, so times 10 is 21,210)\n\nMultiply 303 by 500: 151,500 (since 303*5=1,515, so times 100 is 151,500)\n\nNow add those three results together:\n\n606 + 21,210 = 21,816\n\n21,816 + 151,500 = 173,316\n\nOkay, that matches the previous result. S