1. Break down 303 into \\(300 + 3\\) and 572 into \\(500 + 70 + 2\\).\n2. Multiply each part of 303 by each part of 572 and then sum the results.\n\nFirst, calculate the products of 300 with each part of 572:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n300 \\times 500 &= 150000, \\\\\n300 \\times 70 &= 21000, \\\\\n300 \\times 2 &= 600.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\nAdding these results:\n\\[\n150000 + 21000 + 600 = 171600.\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate the products of 3 with each part of 572:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n3 \\times 500 &= 1500, \\\\\n3 \\times 70 &= 210, \\\\\n3 \\times 2 &= 6.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\nAdding these results:\n\\[\n1500 + 210 + 6 = 1716.\n\\]\n\nFinally, add the two results together:\n\\[\n171600 + 1716 = 173316.\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n     303 \\\\\n\\times 572 \\\\\n\\hline\n     606 \\quad (\\text{303} \\times 2) \\\\\n   21210 \\quad (\\text{303} \\times 70) \\\\\n+ 151500 \\quad (\\text{303} \\times 500) \\\\\n\\hline\n   173316 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 303 and 572 is \\(\\boxed{173316}\\).",
