So first partial product is 4476.\n\nNext, multiply by 3 (the tens place, so shift one left):\n\n746 \u00d73 (tens place, so actually 30).\n\n3\u00d76=18, write 8, carryover 1.\n\n3\u00d74=12 +1=13, write 3, carryover 1.\n\n3\u00d77=21 +1=22. So partial product is 2238, but shifted one left, so 22380.\n\nThird, multiply by 5 (hundreds place, so 500).\n\n746 \u00d75 (hundreds place, so actually 500).\n\n5\u00d76=30, write 0, carryover 3.\n\n5\u00d74=20 +3=23, write 3, carryover 2.\n\n5\u00d77=35 +2=37. So partial product is 3730, shifted two left, so 373000.\n\nAdding them all:\n\n4476 +22380 =26856\n\n26856 +373000 = 399,856. Same result.\n\nHmm, okay, so that seems consistent. But let me try another check using estimation to see if it makes sense.\n\nEstimate 700 \u00d7500 =350,000. The actual numbers are both a bit higher, so 750\u00d7540 would be 405,000. Our result is 399,856, which is a bit less, which makes sense because 746 is 3 less than 750 and 536 is 4 less than 540. So the estimate is in the ballpark. So maybe the answer is correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use a calculator? But since I can't, perhaps compute 746 \u00d7536 in another way.\n\nLet me try the standard algorithm once again, just step by step.\n\nFirst partial product:\n\n746 \u00d76:\n\n6\u00d76 =36. So units digit 6, carryover 3.\n\nNext digit: 4\u00d76=24 +3=27. So 7, carryover 2.\n\nNext digit: 7\u00d76=42 +2=44. So write 44. So first partial is 4476. Correct.\n\nSecond partial product (\u00d73, tens place):\n\n3\u00d76=18, so 8 in tens place. Wait, actually, since it's the tens digit, the first digit (units) will be 8, but shifted left by one.\n\nWait, let's write the partial products properly aligned:\n\nFirst partial product (\u00d76):\n\n4476\n\nSecond partial product (\u00d730):\n\n2238 shifted left one: 22380\n\nThird partial product (\u00d7500):\n\n3730 shifted left two: 373000\n\nAdding them:\n\n4476\n\n+22380\n\n= 26856\n\nThen 26856 +373000:\n\n26,856 + 373,000 = 399,856.\n\nYes, so that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, to be thorough, maybe perform the addition step-by-step again.\n\nAdding 4476 and 22380:\n\n4476\n\n+22380\n\n= (4000 + 400 +70 +6) + (20000 + 2000 + 300 +80)\n\nAdding the thousands: 4000 +20000 =24000, 4000+20000=24000? Wait no, 4476 has 4 thousands, and 22380 has 22 thousands (since 22,380). Wait, actually, breaking down:\n\n4476 is 4 thousands, 4 hundreds, 7 tens, 6 units.\n\n22380 is 22 thousands, 3 hundreds, 8 tens, 0 units.\n\nSo adding:\n\nThousands: 4 +22 =26 thousands.\n\nHundreds:4 +3 =7 hundreds.\n\nTens:7 +8=15 tens (which is 1 hundred 5 tens).\n\nUnits:6 +0=6.\n\nSo total is 26 thousands + 7 hundreds +15 tens +6 units.\n\nBut the 15 tens is 100 +50, so that adds 1 hundred and 5 tens. So:\n\nThousands:26\n\nHundreds:7 +1=8.\n\nTens:5.\n\nUnits:6.\n\nSo that makes 26,856. Correct.\n\nThen adding 26,856 +373,000:\n\n26,856 + 300,000 =326,856\n\n326,856 +73,000 = 326,856 +70,000 =396,856; then +3,000 =399,856. Correct.\n\nSo after multiple checks, I believe the product of 746 and 536 is indeed 399,856. I think that's the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 746 and 536 is \\boxed{399856}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 746 and 536, we use the standard algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 746 by 6 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   6 \\times 6 &= 36 \\quad (\\text{write 6, carry over 3}) \\\\\n   6 \\times 4 &= 24 + 3 = 27 \\quad (\\text{write 7, carry over 2}) \\\\\n   6 \\times 7 &= 42 + 2 = 44 \\quad (\\text{write 44}) \\\\\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n   Result: 4476\n\n2. **Multiply 746 by 3 (tens place, shift one position left):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   3 \\times 6 &= 18 \\quad (\\text{write 8, carry over 1}) \\\\\n   3 \\times 4 &= 12 + 1 = 13 \\quad (\\text{write 3, carry over 1}) \\\\\n   3 \\times 7 &= 21 + 1 = 22 \\quad (\\text{write 22}) \\\\\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n   Result (shifted left): 22380\n\n3. **Multiply 746 by 5 (hundreds place, shift two positions left):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   5 \\times 6 &= 30 \\quad (\\text{write 0, carry over 3}) \\\\\n   5 \\times 4 &= 20 + 3 = 23 \\quad (\\text{write 3, carry over 2}) \\\\\n   5 \\times 7 &= 35 + 2 = 37 \\quad (\\text{write 37}) \\\\\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n   Result (shifted left): 373000\n\n4. **Add all partial products:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   4476 + 22380 &= 26856 \\\\\n   26856 + 373000 &= 399856 \\\\\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 746 and 536 is \\(\\boxed{399856}\\).",
