 Algorithm:**\n   - Multiply 548 by 7 (units place):\n     \\[\n     548 \\times 7 = 3836\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 548 by 0 (tens place), resulting in 0 (shifted one place left).\n   - Multiply 548 by 6 (hundreds place), then shift two places left:\n     \\[\n     548 \\times 6 = 3288 \\quad \\text{(shifted two places left becomes 328800)}\n     \\]\n   - Add the partial products:\n     \\[\n     3836 + 0 + 328800 = 332636\n     \\]\n\n2. **Distributive Property:**\n   - Break down 607 into 600 + 7:\n     \\[\n     548 \\times 607 = 548 \\times (600 + 7) = 548 \\times 600 + 548 \\times 7\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each term:\n     \\[\n     548 \\times 600 = 328800 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 548 \\times 7 = 3836\n     \\]\n   - Sum the results:\n     \\[\n     328800 + 3836 = 332636\n     \\]\n\n3. **Approximation and Verification:**\n   - Estimate using 500 and 600, then adjust for the differences:\n     \\[\n     (500 + 48) \\times (600 + 7) \\quad \\text{expands to} \\quad 500 \\times 600 + 500 \\times 7 + 40 \\times 600 + 40 \\times 7 + 8 \\times 600 + 8 \\times 7\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each term and sum them:\n     \\[\n     300000 + 3500 + 24000 + 280 + 4800 + 56 = 332636\n     \\]\n\n4. **Alternative Breakdown:**\n   - Use (550 - 2) for 548:\n     \\[\n     (550 - 2) \\times 607 = 550 \\times 607 - 2 \\times 607\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each term and subtract:\n     \\[\n     550 \\times 607 = 333850 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 2 \\times 607 = 1214\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     333850 - 1214 = 332636\n     \\]\n\nAfter verifying through multiple methods, the product of 548 and 607 is \\(\\boxed{332636}\\).",
