al products:\n\n1. **Units place (5):**\n   \\[\n   282 \\times 5 = 1410\n   \\]\n\n2. **Tens place (80):**\n   \\[\n   282 \\times 80 = 282 \\times 8 \\times 10 = 2256 \\times 10 = 22560\n   \\]\n\n3. **Hundreds place (800):**\n   \\[\n   282 \\times 800 = 282 \\times 8 \\times 100 = 2256 \\times 100 = 225600\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the partial products:\n\n1. Add the first two partial products:\n   \\[\n   1410 + 22560 = 23970\n   \\]\n\n2. Add the result to the third partial product:\n   \\[\n   23970 + 225600 = 249570\n   \\]\n\nWe verified the result using alternative methods such as breaking down the numbers and using the distributive property, both of which confirmed the result.\n\nThus, the product of 282 and 885 is \\(\\boxed{249570}\\).",
