r**\nThe product of 424 and 911 is \\boxed{386264}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 424 and 911, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 424 by the units digit (1):**\n   \\[\n   424 \\times 1 = 424\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 424 by the tens digit (1), shifted one position to the left:**\n   \\[\n   424 \\times 10 = 4240\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 424 by the hundreds digit (9), shifted two positions to the left:**\n   \\[\n   424 \\times 900 = 424 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 3816 \\times 100 = 381600\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the results of the three multiplications:**\n   \\[\n   424 + 4240 + 381600\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add 424 and 4240:\n     \\[\n     424 + 4240 = 4664\n     \\]\n\n   - Then add the result to 381600:\n     \\[\n     4664 + 381600 = 386264\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 424 and 911 is \\(\\boxed{386264}\\).",
