messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 446 and 275?', "<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 446 and 275. Hmm, let me think about the best way to do this. I remember that multiplying larger numbers can be done by breaking them down into smaller parts. Maybe I can use the distributive property here. Let me try that.\n\nFirst, I'll write down the numbers:.\n\n446 × 275.\n\nHmm, maybe I can split 275 into 200 + 70 + 5. That way, I can multiply each part separately and then add the results together. Let's see.\n\nStarting with 446 × 200. Since 200 is 2 × 100, multiplying by 200 is the same as multiplying by 2 and then by 100. So, 446 × 2 = 892. Then, 892 × 100 = 89,200. Okay, that part seems straightforward.\n\nNext, 446 × 70. Similarly, 70 is 7 × 10. So first multiply 446 by 7, then by 10. Let's do 446 × 7. Breaking that down: 400 × 7 = 2,800 and 46 × 7. 40 × 7 is 280 and 6 ×7 is 42, so 280 +42= 322. Adding that to the 2,800 gives 2,800 + 322 = 3,122. Then multiply by 10 to get 31,220. Wait, no, actually, since 70 is 7×10, multiplying 446×7 first and then ×10. So yes, 446×7=3,122 and then ×10 is 31,220. Got that.\n\nNow the last part is 446 × 5. Let me compute that. 400×5 is 2,000 and 46×5 is 230. Adding those together gives 2,000 + 230 = 2,230. .\n\nNow I have to add all three results together: 89,200 + 31,220 + 2,230. Let me add the first two first. 89,200 + 31,220. Let's see: 89,200 + 30,000 is 119,200, then add 1,220 more: 119,200 +1,220 = 120,420. Then add the last part, 2,230. So 120,420 + 2,230. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
