roperty by breaking down the numbers into smaller parts and then summing the results.\n\n1. **Breaking down 275 into 200 + 70 + 5:**\n   - Calculate \\(446 \\times 200\\):\n     \\[\n     446 \\times 200 = 446 \\times 2 \\times 100 = 892 \\times 100 = 89,200\n     \\]\n   - Calculate \\(446 \\times 70\\):\n     \\[\n     446 \\times 70 = 446 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 3,122 \\times 10 = 31,220\n     \\]\n   - Calculate \\(446 \\times 5\\):\n     \\[\n     446 \\times 5 = 2,230\n     \\]\n\n2. **Summing the results:**\n   - Add the three results together:\n     \\[\n     89,200 + 31,220 + 2,230\n     \\]\n   - First, add \\(89,200 + 31,220\\):\n     \\[\n     89,200 + 31,220 = 120,420\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to \\(2,230\\):\n     \\[\n     120,420 + 2,230 = 122,650\n     \\]\n\n3. **Verification using different methods:**\n   - **Multiplying by breaking down 275 into 25 \u00d7 11:**\n     \\[\n     446 \\times 25 = 11,150 \\quad \\text{and then} \\quad 11,150 \\times 11 = 122,650\n     \\]\n   - **Expanding each term individually using distributive property:**\n     \\[\n     (400 + 40 + 6) \\times (200 + 70 + 5) = 80,000 + 28,000 + 2,000 + 8,000 + 2,800 + 200 + 1,200 + 420 + 30 = 122,650\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 446 and 275 is \\(\\boxed{122650}\\).",
