he partial products:\n   \\[\n   2451 + 65360 + 81700 = 149511\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n1. Break down 183 into 180 + 3:\n   \\[\n   817 \\times 183 = 817 \\times (180 + 3)\n   \\]\n2. Calculate \\(817 \\times 180\\):\n   \\[\n   817 \\times 180 = 817 \\times (18 \\times 10) = (817 \\times 18) \\times 10\n   \\]\n   - \\(817 \\times 10 = 8170\\)\n   - \\(817 \\times 8 = 6536\\)\n   - Adding these: \\(8170 + 6536 = 14706\\)\n   - Multiply by 10: \\(14706 \\times 10 = 147060\\)\n3. Calculate \\(817 \\times 3\\):\n   \\[\n   817 \\times 3 = 2451\n   \\]\n4. Add the results:\n   \\[\n   147060 + 2451 = 149511\n   \\]\n\nAnother verification using decomposition:\n1. Break down 817 into 800 + 17 and 183 into 200 - 17:\n   \\[\n   (800 + 17) \\times (200 - 17)\n   \\]\n2. Expand using the distributive property:\n   \\[\n   800 \\times 200 + 800 \\times (-17) + 17 \\times 200 + 17 \\times (-17)\n   \\]\n3. Calculate each term:\n   \\[\n   160000 - 13600 + 3400 - 289 = 149511\n   \\]\n\nAll methods consistently yield the result \\(\\boxed{149511}\\).",
