o 58,782? Wait, but 4242 + 54540.\n\nWait, 4242 + 54540:.\n\nLet me compute 4242 + 54540:.\n\n54540 + 4000 = 58540.\n\n58540 + 242 = 58782. Yes, that's correct.\n\nNow, adding the third partial product, which is 424200.\n\nSo 58,782 + 424,200.\n\nLet me add those:.\n\n58,782.\n+424,200.\n----------.\nAdding units: 2 + 0 = 2.\nTens: 8 + 0 = 8.\nHundreds: 7 + 2 = 9.\nThousands: 8 + 4 = 12 (write down 2, carryover 1).\nTen thousands: 5 + 2 = 7 plus the carried 1 = 8.\nHundred thousands: 4 (from 424200) + 0 = 4.\n\nWait, maybe better to align:.\n\n    58,782.\n+ 424,200.\n------------.\nStarting from the right:.\n\nUnits: 2 + 0 = 2.\n\nTens: 8 + 0 = 8.\n\nHundreds: 7 + 2 = 9.\n\nThousands: 8 + 4 = 12 (write 2, carryover 1).\n\nTen-thousands: 5 + 2 = 7 + 1 (carry) = 8.\n\nHundred-thousands: 4 (from 424200) + 0 = 4.\n\nWait, actually, 424,200 is 4 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), etc.\n\nWait, let me write it as:.\n\n424200 is 424,200.\n\n58,782 is  58,782.\n\nAdding:.\n\n424,200.\n\n+  58,782.\n\n= ?.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nUnits: 0 + 2 = 2.\n\nTens: 0 + 8 = 8.\n\nHundreds: 2 + 7 = 9.\n\nThousands: 4 + 8 = 12 (write 2, carryover 1).\n\nTen-thousands: 2 + 5 = 7 + 1 (carryover) = 8.\n\nHundred-thousands: 4 + 0 = 4. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
