8,782 + 424,200 = 482,982. Same as before.\n\nOkay, so that's consistent. Alternatively, maybe do it another way for verification.\n\nAlternatively, using calculator-like approach, but since I can't use a calculator, perhaps approximate to see if it's reasonable.\n\n600 \u00d7 800 = 480,000. Since 606 is 6 more than 600 and 797 is 3 less than 800, so the actual product should be (600 +6)(800-3) = 600\u00d7800 +6\u00d7800 -600\u00d73 -6\u00d73 = 480,000 + 4,800 - 1,800 -18 = 480,000 + 3,000 -18 = 483,000 - 18 = 482,982. Exactly the same result!\n\nSo that's a third method giving me the same answer. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 606 and 797 is 482,982.\n\nWait, but just to be absolutely thorough, let me do the multiplication in another way, maybe breaking down both numbers.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps compute 606 \u00d7 797 as (600 + 6) \u00d7 (700 + 90 + 7). But that might be too tedious, but let me try.\n\nExpanding (600 + 6)(700 + 90 +7):\n\nFirst, multiply 600 by each term in the second factor:\n\n600 \u00d7700 = 420,000\n\n600 \u00d790 = 54,000\n\n600 \u00d77 = 4,200\n\nThen multiply 6 by each term in the second factor:\n\n6 \u00d7700 = 4,200\n\n6 \u00d790 = 540\n\n6 \u00d77 = 42.\n\nNow add all these together:\n\n420,000 + 54,000 + 4,200 + 4,200 + 540 + 42.\n\nLet's compute step by step:\n\nStart with 420,000 + 54,000 = 474,000.\n\n474,000 + 4,200 = 478,200.\n\n478,200 + 4,200 = 482,400.\n\n482,400 + 540 = 482,940.\n\n482,940 + 42 = 482,982.\n\nSame result again! Wow, that's four different methods all leading to 482,982. I think that's solid.\n\nSo, I think the answer is 482,982. But just to make sure, let me try multiplying in reverse: 797 \u00d7606 and see if it's the same.\n\nStarting with 797 \u00d7606.\n\nUsing the standard algorithm:\n\n     797\n\n   \u00d7606\n\n   --------\n\nMultiply 797 by 6 (units place):\n\n7\u00d76=42 \u2192 write 2, carryover 4.\n\n9\u00d76=54 +4=58 \u2192 write 8, carryover5.\n\n7\u00d76=42 +5=47 \u2192 write 47