carry over 4)\n   - \\(7 \\times 0 = 0 + 4 = 4\\)\n   - \\(7 \\times 6 = 42\\)\n   - Result shifted left: \\(424200\\)\n\n4. **Add all partial products:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     4242 \\\\\n   + 54540 \\\\\n   +424200 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     482982 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   - First addition: \\(4242 + 54540 = 58782\\)\n   - Second addition: \\(58782 + 424200 = 482982\\)\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n- \\(606 \\times 797 = 606 \\times (800 - 3) = 606 \\times 800 - 606 \\times 3\\)\n- \\(606 \\times 800 = 484800\\)\n- \\(606 \\times 3 = 1818\\)\n- Result: \\(484800 - 1818 = 482982\\)\n\nThus, the product of 606 and 797 is \\(\\boxed{482982}\\).",
