      "text": "25,420 + 62,000.\n\nWait, 25,420 + 62,000. Let me compute that. 25,000 + 62,000 = 87,000, and then 420 more gives 87,420. So total is 87,420?\n\nHmm, but let me check again because sometimes when I do mental math, I might make an error.\n\nAlternatively, let me write it down vertically to add:\n\n25,420\n\n+62,000\n\n--------\n\nAdding the thousands: 25,420 + 62,000.\n\n25,000 + 62,000 = 87,000. Then add the remaining 420: 87,000 + 420 = 87,420. Okay, that seems correct.\n\nWait a second, but let me verify using another method to ensure I didn't make a mistake in the partial products.\n\nAnother way to compute 310 \u00d7 282 is to use the distributive property: 310 \u00d7 (200 + 80 + 2) = 310\u00d7200 + 310\u00d780 + 310\u00d72, which is exactly the same as above, so that checks out.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I can use another method like breaking down the numbers into smaller parts. Let me try that.\n\n310 is 300 + 10. 282 is 280 + 2. Then, multiplying (300 + 10) \u00d7 (280 + 2). Using the distributive property (FOIL method):\n\nFirst: 300 \u00d7 280.\n\nOuter: 300 \u00d7 2.\n\nInner: 10 \u00d7 280.\n\nLast: 10 \u00d7 2.\n\nCompute each term:\n\nFirst: 300 \u00d7 280 = 84,000 (since 3 \u00d7 28 = 84, and then add three zeros: 84,000).\n\nOuter: 300 \u00d7 2 = 600.\n\nInner: 10 \u00d7 280 = 2,800.\n\nLast: 10 \u00d7 2 = 20.\n\nNow add them all together:\n\n84,000 + 600 = 84,600.\n\n84,600 + 2,800 = 87,400.\n\n87,400 + 20 = 87,420. Same result as before. Okay, that's a good sign.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another approach, like the standard algorithm but compute it step by step again to check.\n\nLet me do the multiplication vertically again step by step.\n\nFirst, writing it as:\n\n      310\n\n    \u00d7282\n\n    -------\n\nStarting with the units digit of 282, which is 2:\n\nMultiply 2 \u00d7 310. 2 \u00d7 0 is 0, 2 \u00d7 1 is 2, 2 \u00d7 3 is 6. So that gives 620. Write that down.\n\nNext, the tens digit is 8. Multiply 8 \u00d7 310. Since it's