 (280 + 2) as before, but let me compute it step by step again:\n\n300\u00d7280 = 84,000\n\n300\u00d72 = 600\n\n10\u00d7280 = 2,800\n\n10\u00d72 = 20\n\nAdding them all: 84k + 600 = 84,600; 84,600 + 2,800 = 87,400; 87,400 + 20 = 87,420. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps use calculator-like step-by-step:\n\n310 \u00d7 282.\n\nFirst, write 282 as 200 + 80 + 2, as before.\n\n310\u00d7200 = 62,000.\n\n310\u00d780 = 24,800.\n\n310\u00d72 = 620.\n\nAdding those gives 62,000 + 24,800 = 86,800; plus 620 gives 87,420.\n\nAlright, so all methods lead to the same result. Therefore, I think the answer is 87,420. I don't see any errors in my calculations, and multiple methods confirm the result. So I'm confident that's the correct product.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 310 and 282 is \\boxed{87420}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 310 and 282, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify it with multiple methods.\n\n1. **Standard Multiplication Algorithm:**\n   - Multiply 310 by the units digit (2):\n     \\[\n     310 \\times 2 = 620\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 310 by the tens digit (8), shifted one position to the left:\n     \\[\n     310 \\times 8 = 2480 \\quad \\text{(shifted one position left gives 24,800)}\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 310 by the hundreds digit (2), shifted two positions to the left:\n     \\[\n     310 \\times 2 = 620 \\quad \\text{(shifted two positions left gives 62,000)}\n     \\]\n   - Add the partial products:\n     \\[\n     620 + 24,800 + 62,000 = 87,420\n     \\]\n\n2. **Distributive Property:**\n   - Break down the numbers:\n     \\[\n     310 \\times 282 = (300 + 10) \\times (280 + 2)\n     \\]\n   - Expand using the distributive property:\n     \\[\n     300 \\times 280 + 300 \\times 2 + 10 \\times 280 + 10 \\times 2\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each term:\n     \\[\n     300 \\times 280 = 84,000\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     300 \\times 2 = 600\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     10 \\times 280 = 2,800\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     10 \\times 2 = 20\n     \\]\n   - Sum the results:\n     \\[\n     84,000 + 600 + 2,800 + 20 = 87,420\n     \\]\n\n3. **Verification with Another Method:**\n   - Compute \\(310 \\times 280\\) and add \\(310 \\times 2\\):\n     \\[\n     310 \\times 280 = 86,800 \\quad \\text{(since \\(310 \\times 28 \\times 10 = 86,800\\))}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     310 \\times 2 = 620\n     \\]\n   - Add the results:\n     \\[\n     86,800 + 620 = 87,420\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 310 and 282 is \\(\\boxed{87420}\\).",
