w add all three results together:\n\n0 (from the units)  \n+18,180 (from the tens)  \n+40,400 (from the hundreds)  \n= 18,180 + 40,400 = 58,580. \n\nSame result again. Okay, so that's consistent.\n\nHmm, so all methods lead to 58,580. Maybe I can do a quick estimation to check if this is reasonable.\n\n200 \u00d7 300 is 60,000. The actual numbers are 202 (a bit more than 200) and 290 (a bit less than 300). So the result should be a bit less than 60,000. Since 202 is 1% more than 200, and 290 is 3.3% less than 300. The net effect might be roughly 60,000 minus some percentage. Since 58,580 is 1,420 less than 60,000, that seems reasonable.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use calculator-like step-by-step:\n\n202 \u00d7 290.\n\nFirst, 200 \u00d7 200 = 40,000, but that's not helpful. Wait, perhaps breaking down both numbers:\n\n202 = 200 + 2\n\n290 = 200 + 90\n\nWait, maybe use the distributive property fully:\n\n(200 + 2) \u00d7 (200 + 90) = 200\u00d7200 + 200\u00d790 + 2\u00d7200 + 2\u00d790\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n200\u00d7200 = 40,000\n\n200\u00d790 = 18,000\n\n2\u00d7200 = 400\n\n2\u00d790 = 180\n\nAdding them all together: 40,000 + 18,000 = 58,000; 400 + 180 = 580; so total is 58,000 + 580 = 58,580. Yep, same answer again.\n\nI think this confirms that the product is 58,580. I can't see any mistakes in these calculations. All different methods give the same result, so I'm confident that's the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 202 and 290 is \\boxed{58580}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 202 and 290, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy:\n\n1. **Breaking down 290 into 29 and 10:**\n   - First, calculate \\(202 \\times 29\\):\n     - \\(202 \\times 20 = 4040\\)\n     - \\(202 \\times 9 = 1818\\)\n     - Adding these results: \\(4040 + 1818 = 5858\\)\n   - Then multiply by 10: \\(5858 \\times 10 = 58580\\)\n\n2. **Using the distributive property with 290 as \\(300 - 10\\):**\n   - Calculate \\(202 \\times 300 = 60600\\)\n   - Calculate \\(202 \\times 10 = 2020\\)\n   - Subtract these results: \\(60600 - 2020 = 58580\\)\n\n3. **Standard multiplication algorithm:**\n   - Multiply 202 by 0 (units place): \\(202 \\times 0 = 0\\)\n   - Multiply 202 by 9 (tens place, shifted one position): \\(202 \\times 9 = 1818\\) becomes \\(18180\\)\n   - Multiply 202 by 2 (hundreds place, shifted two positions): \\(202 \\times 2 = 404\\) becomes \\(40400\\)\n   - Add the results: \\(0 + 18180 + 40400 = 58580\\)\n\n4. **Distributive property with full breakdown:**\n   - \\(202 = 200 + 2\\) and \\(290 = 200 + 90\\)\n   - Calculate each term:\n     - \\(200 \\times 200 = 40000\\)\n     - \\(200 \\times 90 = 18000\\)\n     - \\(2 \\times 200 = 400\\)\n     - \\(2 \\times 90 = 180\\)\n   - Sum all terms: \\(40000 + 18000 + 400 + 180 = 58580\\)\n\nAll methods confirm the product is \\(\\boxed{58580}\\).",
