lying 949 by 6 (units digit):\n\n949 \u00d76 = 5,694. (as before)\n\nThen multiply 949 by 80 (tens digit: 8\u00d710):\n\n949 \u00d78 = 7,592, so \u00d710 gives 75,920 (as before).\n\nThen multiply 949 by 700 (hundreds digit:7\u00d7100):\n\n949 \u00d77 = 6,643, \u00d7100 gives 664,300 (as before).\n\nNow, adding these three:\n\n5,694\n\n75,920\n\n664,300\n\nAdding them together:\n\nFirst add 5,694 +75,920 = 81,614.\n\nThen 81,614 +664,300 = 745,914. Yep, same result.\n\nHmm, so that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, let me check with calculator steps.\n\nLet me compute 949 \u00d7 700:\n\n949 \u00d77 = 6,643, so \u00d7100 is 664,300.\n\n949 \u00d780 = 949\u00d78\u00d710 = (7,592)\u00d710 =75,920.\n\n949\u00d76 = 5,694.\n\nAdding all three:\n\n664,300 +75,920 = 740,220. Then 740,220 +5,694 = 745,914. So that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do 949 \u00d7786 as (900 +49) \u00d7 (700 +80 +6). But that might complicate more, but let me see.\n\nFirst, expand as:\n\n900\u00d7700 +900\u00d780 +900\u00d76 +49\u00d7700 +49\u00d780 +49\u00d76.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n900\u00d7700 = 630,000.\n\n900\u00d780 =72,000.\n\n900\u00d76 =5,400.\n\n49\u00d7700 = 34,300.\n\n49\u00d780 = 3,920.\n\n49\u00d76 =294.\n\nNow add all these:\n\n630,000 +72,000 =702,000.\n\n702,000 +5,400 =707,400.\n\n707,400 +34,300 =741,700.\n\n741,700 +3,920 =745,620.\n\n745,620 +294 =745,914.\n\nSame result. So that's good.\n\nHmm, so multiple methods give me 745,914. So probably that's the correct answer. Let me see if I can spot any error in my calculations.\n\nWait, in the first approach when adding 664,300 +75,920, I got 740,220. Then adding 5,694 gives 745,914. That's correct. The expanded method also gives the same.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another check: take the product modulo 9 or 11 to verify.\n\nLet me try modulo 9.\n\nFirst, compute 949 mod9:\n\n9 +4 +9 =22 \u2192 2+2=4. So 949 \u22614 mod9.\n\n786 mod9:\n\n7+8+6=21 \u21922+1=3. So 786\u22613 mod9.\n\nThus product should be 4\u00d73=12\u2261