atively, if I go left to right with alternating signs:\n\nStarting with the leftmost digit (7) as positive:\n\n+7 -4 +5 -9 +1 -4.\n\n7-4=3; 3+5=8; 8-9= -1; -1 +1=0; 0-4= -4. Which is -4 mod11=7 mod11. That's conflicting.\n\nWait, so inconsistency here because direction matters. So to avoid confusion, perhaps better to take the standard method from the right.\n\nBut the key is that if done correctly, it should give the congruence.\n\nSince from the right it gives 4 mod11, which matches the expected 4 mod11 (since 3\u00d75=15\u22614 mod11). So that's okay.\n\nTherefore, the mod11 check works.\n\nTherefore, the result 745,914 seems correct.\n\nTherefore, after all these checks, I believe the product of 949 and 786 is 745,914.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 949 and 786 is \\boxed{745914}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 949 and 786, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into smaller parts:\n\n1. Calculate \\( 949 \\times 700 \\):\n   \\[\n   949 \\times 700 = 949 \\times 7 \\times 100 = 6643 \\times 100 = 664300\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\( 949 \\times 80 \\):\n   \\[\n   949 \\times 80 = 949 \\times 8 \\times 10 = 7592 \\times 10 = 75920\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate \\( 949 \\times 6 \\):\n   \\[\n   949 \\times 6 = 5694\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the results of the three calculations:\n   \\[\n   664300 + 75920 + 5694\n   \\]\n\nFirst, add \\( 664300 \\) and \\( 75920 \\):\n   \\[\n   664300 + 75920 = 740220\n   \\]\n\nThen, add the result to \\( 5694 \\):\n   \\[\n   740220 + 5694 = 745914\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 949 and 786 is \\(\\boxed{745914}\\).",
