messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 977 and 940?', "<think>Okay, let's see, I need to find the product of 977 and 940. Hmm, multiplying these two numbers. Alright, let me think about the best way to do this. Maybe I can use the standard multiplication algorithm, but that might take a while. Alternatively, maybe there's a trick or a shortcut to make it easier?.\n\nFirst, let me recall how multiplication works. If I have two numbers, say a and b, their product is a × b. Since both numbers are three-digit numbers, multiplying them directly would involve several steps. Let me try breaking it down.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the distributive property. Let me see. 977 times 940. Hmm, perhaps I can express one of the numbers as a sum or difference to make the multiplication simpler. For example, 940 is close to 900, and 977 is close to 1000. Wait, maybe that's a good approach.\n\nLet me think: 977 is 1000 minus 23, right? Because 1000 - 23 = 977. And 940 is 900 plus 40. Hmm, so maybe I can write this as (1000 - 23) × (900 + 40). Then expand that using the distributive property. Let me try that.\n\nFirst, expanding (1000 - 23)(900 + 40). That would be 1000×900 + 1000×40 - 23×900 - 23×40. Let me compute each term individually.\n\nStarting with 1000 × 900. That's straightforward. 1000 multiplied by 900 is 900,000.\n\nNext term is 1000 × 40. That's 40,000.\n\nThird term is -23 × 900. Let me compute 23 × 900 first. 23 times 9 is 207, so 23 × 900 is 20,700. So with the negative sign, that's -20,700.\n\nFourth term is -23 × 40. 23 × 40 is 920, so with the negative sign, that's -920.\n\nNow, adding all these together: 900,000 + 40,000 - 20,700 - 920.\n\nFirst, add 900,000 + 40,000. That gives 940,000.\n\nThen subtract 20,700 from that. 940,000 - 20,700. Let me compute that. 940,000 minus 20,000 is 920,000, and then subtract another 700, so 920,000 - 700 = 919,300.\n\nNow subtract the last term, which is 920. 919,300 - 920. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
