      "text": "574,400 + 70,364 = 644,764? Wait, let me compute this properly:.\n\n574,400 + 70,364.\n\nFirst, add 574,400 + 70,000 = 644,400.\n\nThen add remaining 364: 644,400 +364 = 644,764.\n\nWait, but hold on, the sum of 70364 and 574400:.\n\n574400.\n\n+ 70364.\n\n= 574400 + 70,364 = 644,764? Yes, that seems right.\n\nWait a minute, but let me check again all steps because I initially made a mistake in the first partial product. Let me verify the total.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps there is a better way to compute 718 \u00d7898.\n\nAlternatively, use the distributive property: 718\u00d7(900 - 2) = 718\u00d7900 - 718\u00d72.\n\nThat might be easier.\n\nCalculating 718\u00d7900: 718\u00d79\u00d7100.\n\n718\u00d79: as before, 700\u00d79=6300, 18\u00d79=162, so total 6300+162=6462. Then \u00d7100 gives 646,200.\n\nThen subtract 718\u00d72 = 1,436.\n\nTherefore, 646,200 - 1,436 = ?\n\n646,200 minus 1,000 is 645,200, then minus 436 more: 645,200 -436= 644,764. So that matches the previous result.\n\nSo the product is 644,764.\n\nWait, so that's the same as before. So I think that's correct. So the answer is 644,764.\n\nBut let me confirm with another method. Maybe breaking down both numbers.\n\nAlternatively, 718\u00d7898 = (700+18)\u00d7(900-2).\n\nMultiply using FOIL or distributive:.\n\n700\u00d7900 +700\u00d7(-2) +18\u00d7900 +18\u00d7(-2).\n\n= 630,000 -1,400 + 16,200 -36.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n630,000 -1,400 = 628,600.\n\n628,600 +16,200 = 644,800.\n\n644,800 -36 = 644,764. Same result again.\n\nOkay, so that seems consistent. Therefore, the product of 718 and 898 is 644,764.\n\nWait, but just to make sure I didn't make a mistake in the first calculation when I did the vertical multiplication. Let me retrace.\n\nFirst partial product was 718\u00d78: 5744. Correct.\n\nSecond partial product is 718\u00d79 (tens place), shifted one: so 6462 shifted left one digit becomes 64,620. Wait, 6462 \u00d710=64,620. That's correct.\n\nThird partial product is 718\u00d78 (hundreds place), shifted two digits: 718\u00d78=5,744, shifted two becomes 574,400. Correct.\n\nAdding all three: 5,744 + 64,620 = 70,364. Then 70,364 +574,400 = 644,764. Yep, same as the other methods.\n\nTherefore, I think that's correct. So the answer is 644,764.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 718 and 898 is \\boxed{644764}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 718 and 898, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 718 by 8 (units place):\n   \\[\n   718 \\times 8 = 5744\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 718 by 9 (tens place) and shift one position to the left:\n   \\[\n   718 \\times 9 = 6462 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by one digit gives 64620)}\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 718 by 8 (hundreds place) and shift two positions to the left:\n   \\[\n   718 \\times 8 = 5744 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by two digits gives 574400)}\n   \\]\n\n4. Add all the partial products:\n   \\[\n   5744 + 64620 + 574400\n   \\]\n   - Adding the first two partial products:\n     \\[\n     5744 + 64620 = 70364\n     \\]\n   - Adding the result to the third partial product:\n     \\[\n     70364 + 574400 = 644764\n     \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n\\[\n718 \\times 898 = 718 \\times (900 - 2) = 718 \\times 900 - 718 \\times 2\n\\]\n- Calculate \\(718 \\times 900\\):\n  \\[\n  718 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 6462 \\times 100 = 646200\n  \\]\n- Calculate \\(718 \\times 2\\):\n  \\[\n  718 \\times 2 = 1436\n  \\]\n- Subtract the results:\n  \\[\n  646200 - 1436 = 644764\n  \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 718 and 898 is \\(\\boxed{644764}\\).",
