      "text": "356,800 + 2,716 = 359,516? Wait, hold on, let me check that addition again.\n\nWait, 346,800 plus 12,716. Let me line them up:\n\n346,800\n\n+\u00a0 12,716\n\n----------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n0 + 6 = 6\n\n0 + 1 = 1\n\n8 (thousands place?) Wait, actually, let's see:\n\nWait, 346,800 is 3 4 6 8 0 0\n\nand 12,716 is 0 1 2 7 1 6?\n\nWait, maybe I should write it properly:\n\n346800\n\n+\u00a0 12716\n\n= ?\n\nStarting from the units digit:\n\n0 + 6 =6\n\n0 +1 =1\n\n8 +7 =15, carry over 1\n\n6 +2 +1 (carry) =9\n\n4 +1 =5?\n\nWait, maybe it's easier to do in numbers:\n\n346,800 + 12,716:\n\n346,800 + 10,000 = 356,800\n\nThen add 2,716: 356,800 + 2,000 = 358,800\n\nThen add 716: 358,800 +700=359,500, plus 16 is 359,516. Okay, so that seems right.\n\nWait, but let me confirm with another method just to be sure. Maybe using another multiplication approach, like the standard algorithm.\n\nLet me try multiplying 578 \u00d7 622 the traditional way.\n\nFirst, write down 578\n\n\u00d7622\n\n------------\n\nMultiply 578 by 2 (units place): 578\u00d72=1,156\n\nMultiply 578 by 20 (tens place): 578\u00d72=1,156, then add a zero: 11,560\n\nMultiply 578 by 600 (hundreds place): 578\u00d76=3,468, then add two zeros: 346,800\n\nNow add them all up:\n\n1,156\n\n11,560\n\n346,800\n\nAdding the first two: 1,156 + 11,560 = 12,716 (which matches the previous calculation)\n\nThen add 346,800 +12,716 = 359,516. Okay, that's the same result.\n\nHmm, so seems correct. But maybe I can check using another method, like the difference of squares? Since 578 and 622 are numbers that add up to 1200?\n\nWait, 578 + 622 = 1200? Let me check: 500+600=1100, 78+22=100, so total is 1200. Oh, interesting. So 578 and 622 add up to 1200. That might be useful.\n\nSo, if I think of them as (600 - 22) and (600 + 22), then their product is (600)^2 - (22)^2. Wait, that formula is (a - b)(a + b) = a\u00b2 - b\u00b2. So since 578 = 600 -22 and 622 =600 +22, that's exactly the case. So 578\u00d7622 = 600\u00b2 - (22)\u00b2.\n\nLet me compute that. 600 squared is 360,000. 22 squared is 484. Therefore, 360,000 - 484 = 359,516. Exactly the same result as before! So that confirms it. That's a good check.\n\nSo using the difference of squares formula made it much simpler. So the answer is 359,516.\n\nI think that's solid. Both methods give the same result. So I can be confident that the product of 578 and 622 is 359,516.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 578 and 622 is \\boxed{359516}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 578 and 622, we can use the difference of squares formula. \n\nFirst, note that:\n\\[\n578 + 622 = 1200\n\\]\nThis can be rewritten as:\n\\[\n578 = 600 - 22 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 622 = 600 + 22\n\\]\nUsing the difference of squares formula \\((a - b)(a + b) = a^2 - b^2\\), we get:\n\\[\n(600 - 22)(600 + 22) = 600^2 - 22^2\n\\]\nCalculating each term separately:\n\\[\n600^2 = 360000\n\\]\n\\[\n22^2 = 484\n\\]\nSubtracting these results:\n\\[\n360000 - 484 = 359516\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 578 and 622 is \\(\\boxed{359516}\\).",
