al Answer**\nThe product of 461 and 570 is \\boxed{262770}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 461 and 570, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify with the distributive property.\n\nFirst, using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 461 by 0 (units place of 570):\n   \\[\n   461 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 461 by 70 (tens place of 570):\n   \\[\n   461 \\times 7 = 3227 \\quad \\text{(shifted one position to the left)} \\quad 32270\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 461 by 500 (hundreds place of 570):\n   \\[\n   461 \\times 5 = 2305 \\quad \\text{(shifted two positions to the left)} \\quad 230500\n   \\]\n\nAdding the partial products:\n\\[\n0 + 32270 + 230500 = 262770\n\\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n\\[\n461 \\times 570 = 461 \\times (500 + 70) = (461 \\times 500) + (461 \\times 70)\n\\]\nCalculating each part:\n\\[\n461 \\times 500 = 230500\n\\]\n\\[\n461 \\times 70 = 32270\n\\]\nAdding these results:\n\\[\n230500 + 32270 = 262770\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 461 and 570 is \\(\\boxed{262770}\\).",
