95. That confirms it.\n\nTherefore, the product of 129 and 955 is 123,195.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 129 and 955 is \\boxed{123195}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 129 and 955, we can use the distributive property and break down the numbers into smaller parts:\n\n1. Break down 955 into 900 + 50 + 5.\n2. Multiply each part by 129:\n   - \\(129 \\times 900 = 116100\\)\n   - \\(129 \\times 50 = 6450\\)\n   - \\(129 \\times 5 = 645\\)\n3. Add the results together:\n   - \\(116100 + 6450 = 122550\\)\n   - \\(122550 + 645 = 123195\\)\n\nVerification using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n- Multiply 955 by 9 (units place): \\(955 \\times 9 = 8595\\)\n- Multiply 955 by 2 (tens place, shifted one position left): \\(955 \\times 20 = 19100\\)\n- Multiply 955 by 1 (hundreds place, shifted two positions left): \\(955 \\times 100 = 95500\\)\n- Add the results together:\n  - \\(8595 + 19100 = 27695\\)\n  - \\(27695 + 95500 = 123195\\)\n\nAnother verification using division:\n- Divide 123195 by 129 to get 955, confirming the product is correct.\n\nThus, the product of 129 and 955 is \\(\\boxed{123195}\\).",
