 digit (hundreds place?), and carryover 3.\n\nThen 4 × 4 (the hundreds digit of 499): 4×4=16, plus 3 = 19. So write 19 in the next digits. So putting it all together, the partial product is 1996, but shifted one place to the left, so adding a zero at the end? Wait, no, actually, the partial products are written with an offset. So the first partial product (from the 3) is 1497, then the second (from the 4) is 1996 shifted left by one, so it becomes 19960, then the third partial product (from the 5 in the hundreds place) will be shifted left by two places.\n\nHmm, maybe I need to write them down as:.\n\nFirst partial product: 1497 (from ×3).\n\nSecond partial product: 1996 shifted left by one → 19960 (from ×40).\n\nThird partial product: 5 (hundreds place) × 499, shifted left by two → 5×499=2495, shifted left two → 249500.\n\nThen add all three together: 1497 + 19960 + 249500.\n\nWait, let me confirm that.\n\nAlternatively, let me do each step properly.\n\nStarting over, the multiplication of 499 by 543:.\n\nFirst, write down 499 × 3 = 1497 (this is correct).\n\nSecond, 499 × 40 (since the 4 is in the tens place) = 499 × 4 × 10 = 1996 ×10 = 19960.\n\nThird, 499 × 500 (since the 5 is in the hundreds place) = 499 ×5 × 100 = 2495 ×100 = 249500.\n\nNow, add them all together:.\n\n1497 + 19960 + 249500.\n\nLet's compute step by step.\n\nFirst, 1497 + 19960:.\n\n1497 + 19960. Let's see, 1497 + 20000 would be 21497, but since it's 19960, subtract 40: 21497 -40 = 21457?.\n\nWait, let me do it properly:.\n\n1497 + 19960:.\n\nAdding the thousands: 1000 + 19000 = 20000.\n\nHundreds: 400 + 900 = 1300 → total so far 21300.\n\nTens: 90 + 60 = 150 → 21450.\n\nOnes: 7 + 0 =7 → total 21457. Wait, but let me check:.\n\n1497.\n\n+19960.\n\n--------.\n\nAlign the numbers:.\n\n  1497.\n\n+19960.\n\n=?.\n\nLet me write them aligned:.\n\n   1497.\n\n+19960.\n\n--------.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\n7 + 0 =7.\n\n9 + 6 =15, write down 5, carryover 1.\n\n4 + 9 +1 (carryover) =14, write down