n step by step again as if I was doing it manually, just to ensure that my initial calculation didn't have an error.\n\nLet me try the multiplication again:\n\n499 \u00d7543.\n\nStarting with the 3 (units place):\n\n3\u00d79 =27, write 7, carryover2.\n\n3\u00d79 =27 +2 =29, write 9, carryover2.\n\n3\u00d74 =12 +2 =14, write 14.\n\nSo first partial product is 1497.\n\nNext, multiplying by 4 (tens place):\n\n4\u00d79 =36, write 6, carryover3.\n\n4\u00d79 =36 +3 =39, write 9, carryover3.\n\n4\u00d74 =16 +3 =19, write 19.\n\nBut since this is the tens place, we shift one to the left, so it's 19960.\n\nThird, multiplying by 5 (hundreds place):\n\n5\u00d79 =45, write 5, carryover4.\n\n5\u00d79 =45 +4 =49, write 9, carryover4.\n\n5\u00d74 =20 +4 =24, write24.\n\nSince this is hundreds place, shift two to the left, so 249500.\n\nAdding all three partial products:\n\n1497\n\n+19960\n\n=21457.\n\nThen 21457 +249500 =270,957. Yes, same as before.\n\nTherefore, confident that 270,957 is the correct answer.\n\nWait a second, just to be thorough, perhaps I can approximate to check if this is reasonable.\n\n499 is approximately 500, and 543 is approximately 500. 500\u00d7500=250,000. But since both numbers are slightly less than 500 and more, actually 499 is 1 less than 500, and 543 is 43 more. So the actual product should be a bit more than 500\u00d7543=271,500, but subtract 1\u00d7543. So 271,500-543=270,957. Which matches exactly. So the approximation also makes sense.\n\nAlternatively, if I had 500\u00d7500=250,000, but since one is 500-1 and the other is 500+43, the difference would be accounted for. But the exact calculation is better.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another check: digit sums or casting out nines.\n\nLet me try the digit sum method for verification.\n\nCompute the digit sum of each number:\n\n499: 4+9+9 =22 \u2192 2+2=4.\n\n543:5+4+3=12 \u21921+2=3.\n\nMultiply their digit sums:4\u00d73=12 \u21921+2=3.\n\nNow compute the digit sum of the result 270,957:\n\n2+7