ed becomes 90,900  \nNow add them up: 606 + 15,150 = 15,756. Then 15,756 + 90,900 = 106,656.  \n\nSame result. Hmm, so that seems to confirm it. Maybe I was correct the first time.  \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use estimation to check. 300 times 350 is 105,000. Since the actual numbers are 303 and 352, which are a bit more than those, so 105,000 plus some extra. 3 more in the first number and 2 more in the second. So, 3*352 = 1,056 and 300*2=600, totaling 1,656 added to 105,000 would be 106,656. Exactly matches. So that seems to confirm.  \n\nTherefore, the product of 303 and 352 is 106,656. I think that's correct. I've checked it multiple ways so I feel confident now.  \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 303 and 352 is \\boxed{106656}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 303 and 352, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify using different methods.\n\nFirst, we multiply 352 by each digit of 303 (starting from the rightmost digit) and then sum the partial products:\n\n1. **Units place (3):**\n   \\[\n   352 \\times 3 = 1056\n   \\]\n   Partial product: 1056\n\n2. **Tens place (0):**\n   \\[\n   352 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n   Partial product: 0 (shifted one position to the left)\n\n3. **Hundreds place (3):**\n   \\[\n   352 \\times 3 = 1056\n   \\]\n   Partial product: 105600 (shifted two positions to the left)\n\nAdding all the partial products together:\n\\[\n1056 + 0 + 105600 = 106656\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can break down the multiplication using the distributive property:\n\\[\n303 \\times 352 = (300 + 3) \\times 352 = 300 \\times 352 + 3 \\times 352\n\\]\n\\[\n300 \\times 352 = 105600\n\\]\n\\[\n3 \\times 352 = 1056\n\\]\n\\[\n105600 + 1056 = 106656\n\\]\n\nAnother verification method using the standard algorithm with the numbers reversed:\n\\[\n303 \\times 352\n\\]\n1. **Units place (2):**\n   \\[\n   303 \\times 2 = 606\n   \\]\n2. **Tens place (5):**\n   \\[\n   303 \\times 5 = 1515 \\quad (\\text{shifted one position left: } 15150)\n   \\]\n3. **Hundreds place (3):**\n   \\[\n   303 \\times 3 = 909 \\quad (\\text{shifted two positions left: } 90900)\n   \\]\nAdding these:\n\\[\n606 + 15150 + 90900 = 106656\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 303 and 352 is \\boxed{106656}.",
