      "text": "360,000 + 30,240 = 390,240.\n\nWait, but let me check that addition again. 360,000 plus 30,240. 360,000 + 30,000 is 390,000, then plus 240 is 390,240. Yes, that's correct.\n\nHmm, but let me verify this using another method to ensure I didn't make a mistake. Maybe using the distributive property in a different way. Let's see.\n\n720 \u00d7 542 can be written as 720 \u00d7 (500 + 40 + 2) which is exactly what I did before, so that's consistent. The components were 720\u00d7500=360,000, 720\u00d740=28,800, and 720\u00d72=1,440. Adding those gives 360k +28.8k = 388,800 + 1,440 = 390,240. That matches my previous result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another approach, like rounding or something else. Let me see.\n\nAlternatively, 542 can be thought of as 540 + 2, so 720\u00d7540 + 720\u00d72. Let's compute 720\u00d7540 first. 720 \u00d7 500 is 360,000, and 720\u00d740 is 28,800. So adding those gives 360,000 +28,800 = 388,800. Then adding 720\u00d72=1,440 gives 388,800 +1,440 = 390,240. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the standard vertical multiplication:\n\n      720\n    \u00d7 542\n    -------\n       1440   (720\u00d72)\n      28800   (720\u00d740, shifted one position to the left)\n    +360000   (720\u00d7500, shifted two positions to the left)\n    -----------\n      390240\n\nYes, that seems to add up. Let me check each multiplication again just to be thorough.\n\nFirst step: 720 \u00d7 2. 0\u00d72=0, 2\u00d72=4, 7\u00d72=14. So 1440. Correct.\n\nSecond step: 720 \u00d7 4. Since it's the tens place, it's actually 40, so 720\u00d74=2,880, then add a zero to make it 28,800. That's right.\n\nThird step: 720 \u00d75 is 3,600, but since it's the hundreds place, multiply by 100, so 3,600 \u00d7100 = 360,000. Correct.\n\nAdding them all together: 1,440 + 28,800 = 30,240; 30,240 + 360,000 = 390,240. Okay, that seems consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can compute 700\u00d7542 and 20\u00d7542, then add them.\n\nLet's try that. 700\u00d7542.