0*600 = 420,000.\n\n700*63 = 44,100.\n\nSo 420,000 +44,100 = 464,100.\n\nThen subtract 16*(600 +63):\n\n16*600 = 9,600.\n\n16*63 = 1,008.\n\nTotal subtraction: 9,600 +1,008 = 10,608.\n\nTherefore, 464,100 -10,608 = ?\n\n464,100 - 10,000 = 454,100.\n\nThen subtract 608 more: 454,100 -608 = 453,492. Same result. Okay, that's four different methods and all give the same answer. I think that solidifies that 453,492 is correct. Therefore, I can confidently say the product of 684 and 663 is 453,492.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 684 and 663 is \\boxed{453492}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 684 and 663, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify using different methods:\n\n1. **Standard Multiplication Algorithm:**\n   - Multiply 684 by 3: \\(684 \\times 3 = 2052\\)\n   - Multiply 684 by 60: \\(684 \\times 60 = 41040\\)\n   - Multiply 684 by 600: \\(684 \\times 600 = 410400\\)\n   - Add the results together:\n     \\[\n     2052 + 41040 + 410400 = 453492\n     \\]\n\n2. **Using the Distributive Property:**\n   - Break down the numbers into hundreds, tens, and units:\n     \\[\n     (600 + 80 + 4)(600 + 60 + 3)\n     \\]\n   - Expand and compute each term:\n     \\[\n     \\begin{aligned}\n     &600 \\times 600 = 360000, \\\\\n     &600 \\times 60 = 36000, \\\\\n     &600 \\times 3 = 1800, \\\\\n     &80 \\times 600 = 48000, \\\\\n     &80 \\times 60 = 4800, \\\\\n     &80 \\times 3 = 240, \\\\\n     &4 \\times 600 = 2400, \\\\\n     &4 \\times 60 = 240, \\\\\n     &4 \\times 3 = 12.\n     \\end{aligned}\n     \\]\n   - Sum all the terms:\n     \\[\n     360000 + 36000 + 1800 + 48000 + 4800 + 240 + 2400 + 240 + 12 = 453492\n     \\]\n\n3. **Using Algebraic Identity:**\n   - Express 663 as \\(684 - 21\\):\n     \\[\n     684 \\times 663 = 684 \\times (684 - 21) = 684^2 - 21 \\times 684\n     \\]\n   - Compute \\(684^2\\):\n     \\[\n     684^2 = (600 + 84)^2 = 600^2 + 2 \\times 600 \\times 84 + 84^2 = 360000 + 100800 + 7056 = 467856\n     \\]\n   - Compute \\(21 \\times 684\\):\n     \\[\n     21 \\times 684 = 13680 + 684 = 14364\n     \\]\n   - Subtract:\n     \\[\n     467856 - 14364 = 453492\n     \\]\n\n4. **Another Breakdown:**\n   - Express numbers as \\((700 - 16)\\) and \\((600 + 63)\\):\n     \\[\n     (700 - 16)(600 + 63) = 700 \\times (600 + 63) - 16 \\times (600 + 63)\n     \\]\n   - Compute each part:\n     \\[\n     \\begin{aligned}\n     &700 \\times 600 = 420000, \\\\\n     &700 \\times 63 = 44100, \\\\\n     &16 \\times 600 = 9600, \\\\\n     &16 \\times 63 = 1008.\n     \\end{aligned}\n     \\]\n   - Combine results:\n     \\[\n     (420000 + 44100) - (9600 + 1008) = 464100 - 10608 = 453492\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm the product of 684 and 663 is \\(\\boxed{453492}\\).",
