t is indeed 314,358. So I think that's the correct answer. I went through multiple methods to verify, so I feel confident.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 433 and 726 is \\boxed{314358}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 433 and 726, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm by breaking it down into partial products and then summing them up.\n\n1. **Multiply 433 by 6 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   433 \\times 6 &= 2598 \\\\\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 433 by 20 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   433 \\times 20 &= 8660 \\\\\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 433 by 700 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   433 \\times 700 &= 303100 \\\\\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   2598 + 8660 + 303100 &= 2598 + 8660 + 303100 \\\\\n   &= 11258 + 303100 \\\\\n   &= 314358 \\\\\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n\nTo verify, we can check the division:\n- Dividing 314358 by 433 gives 726, confirming the result is correct.\n\nThus, the product of 433 and 726 is \\(\\boxed{314358}\\).",
