uct: 21,120.\n\nThird partial product: 633,600.\n\nAdding them together. Let me start with the first two: 6,336 + 21,120. .\n\n6,336 + 21,120. Let's add 6,000 +21,000 =27,000. Then 336 +120 = 456. So total is 27,456. .\n\nNow add that to the third partial product: 27,456 + 633,600. .\n\nHmm, 27,456 + 600,000 is 627,456. Then add the remaining 33,600? Wait, no. Wait, 633,600 is 600,000 + 33,600. Wait, no, actually 633,600 is 600,000 plus 33,600? Wait, no, 600,000 + 33,600 is 633,600? Wait, 600k plus 33k is 633k, yes. .\n\nWait, but adding 27,456 to 633,600. Let me do it step by step. .\n\n27,456 + 633,600. .\n\nAdding the thousands: 27,000 + 633,000 = 660,000. Then the remaining 456. So total is 660,456. .\n\nWait, is that right? Let me check again. .\n\nWait 27,456 + 633,600. .\n\nAlternatively, 633,600 + 27,456. .\n\n633,600 + 20,000 = 653,600.\n\n653,600 +7,000 = 660,600. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
