s 7. This is the hundreds place, so it's actually 700. So we need to multiply 820 by 700. .\n\nAgain, let's do 820 x 7 first, then add two zeros. .\n\n820 x 7 = 5740, so adding two zeros gives 574000. .\n\nNow, add all the partial products together:.\n\nFirst partial product: 5740.\n\nSecond partial product: 24600.\n\nThird partial product: 574000.\n\nAdding them up: 5740 + 24600 = let's see, 5740 + 24600. .\n\n5740 + 24600: .\n\nAdding the thousands: 5000 + 24000 = 29000.\n\nThen the hundreds: 700 + 600 = 1300 → 29000 + 1300 = 30300.\n\nThen the tens and units: 40 + 0 = 40 → 30300 + 40 = 30340. Wait, that can't be right. Wait, maybe I should do it more carefully.\n\nWait, 5740 + 24600:.\n\nStart with the units digit:.\n\n0 + 0 = 0.\n\n4 + 0 = 4.\n\n7 + 6 = 13, so write 3 and carry over 1.\n\n5 + 4 + 1 (carry) = 10, so write 0 and carry over 1.\n\nFinally, the 2 (from 24600) plus the carried over 1 is 3. Wait, actually, hold on:.\n\nWait, maybe I should write them aligned properly:.\n\n\u202f\xa05740.\n\n+24600.\n\n________.\n\nLet me align them:.\n\n\u2003\u202f5740.\n\n+24600.\n\n________.\n\nAdding the units place: 0 + 0 = 0.\n\nTens place: 4 + 0 = 4.\n\nHundreds place: 7 + 6 = 13. Write down 3, carry over 1.\n\nThousands place: 5 + 4 = 9, plus the carried 1 is 10. Write down 0, carry over 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 2 (from 24600) plus the carried 1 is 3.\n\nSo the total is 30340. Wait, so 5740 + 24600 = 30340. Then adding the third partial product which is 574000.\n\nSo 30340 + 574000. Let's compute that.\n\n30340 + 574000. Let's align them:.\n\n\u200330340.\n\n+574000.\n\n________.\n\nAdding:.\n\n0 + 0 = 0.\n\n4 + 0 = 4.\n\n3 + 0 = 3.\n\n0 + 4 = 4.\n\n3 +7 = 10, so write 0 and carry over 1.\n\n5 + the carried 1 = 6. .\n\nWait, maybe better:.\n\n574000 is 574,000.\n\nplus 30,340.\n\nAdding together:.\n\n574,000.\n\n+\xa030,340. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
