 820 and 737 is 604,340.\n\nWait, but let me check once more with another approach. Let's use the standard algorithm again.\n\nMultiplying 820 by 737.\n\nFirst, write 820 \u00d7 737.\n\nStart with the 7 (units place):\n\n7 \u00d7 0 =0\n\n7 \u00d72 =14 (write 4, carryover 1)\n\n7 \u00d78 =56 +1 =57. So first partial product: 5740.\n\nNext, the 3 (tens place). Since it's the tens digit, we shift one position left. So we can think of multiplying by 30, so the partial product will be 820\u00d73\u00d710.\n\n3\u00d70=0\n\n3\u00d72=6\n\n3\u00d78=24. So 2460, but shifted left by one, so 24600.\n\nThird digit, the 7 (hundreds place): multiplying by 700. So 820\u00d77\u00d7100.\n\n7\u00d70=0\n\n7\u00d72=14 (write 4, carryover 1)\n\n7\u00d78=56 +1=57. So 5740, then times 100 is 574000.\n\nNow, adding all three partial products:\n\n5740\n\n+24600\n\n= 30340\n\n30340 + 574000 = 604,340. Yep, same result.\n\nTherefore, I'm pretty confident the answer is 604,340.\n\nWait, hold on a second. Let me try multiplying 820 \u00d7737 in another way. Maybe breaking down 737 into 700+37. So:\n\n820\u00d7700 = 574,000.\n\n820\u00d737: Let's compute that separately.\n\nCompute 820\u00d737:\n\nAgain, 820\u00d730 =24,600; 820\u00d77=5,740. So 24,600 +5,740 =30,340.\n\nThus, total is 574,000 +30,340 =604,340. Same answer.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps using the commutative property, multiply 737\u00d7820.\n\nLet me try that way.\n\n737 \u00d7 800 = 589,600.\n\n737 \u00d720 =14,740.\n\nAdding them gives 589,600 +14,740 =604,340. Same result.\n\nTherefore, after multiple methods and checks, I believe the correct answer is 604,340.\n\nI don't see any errors in the steps I took, and all different approaches converge to the same number. So I think that's the right product.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 820 and 737 is \\boxed{604340}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 820 and 737, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify the result through multiple methods.\n\nFirst, we break down the multiplication step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 820 by 7 (units place of 737):**\n   \\[\n   820 \\times 7 = 5740\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 820 by 30 (tens place of 737):**\n   \\[\n   820 \\times 30 = 24600\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 820 by 700 (hundreds place of 737):**\n   \\[\n   820 \\times 700 = 574000\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the partial products:\n\\[\n5740 + 24600 + 574000\n\\]\n\nAdding the first two partial products:\n\\[\n5740 + 24600 = 30340\n\\]\n\nThen adding the result to the third partial product:\n\\[\n30340 + 574000 = 604340\n\\]\n\nWe verified this result using different methods:\n- **Distributive property:**\n  \\[\n  820 \\times (700 + 30 + 7) = 820 \\times 700 + 820 \\times 30 + 820 \\times 7 = 574000 + 24600 + 5740 = 604340\n  \\]\n\n- **Alternative breakdown:**\n  \\[\n  820 \\times 737 = 820 \\times (700 + 37) = 574000 + 30340 = 604340\n  \\]\n\n- **Commutative property:**\n  \\[\n  737 \\times 820 = 737 \\times (800 + 20) = 589600 + 14740 = 604340\n  \\]\n\nAll methods consistently yield the same result. Therefore, the product of 820 and 737 is \\(\\boxed{604340}\\).",
