\u00d7100 =112,200,\n\n1,122 \u00d79=10,098,\n\nTotal: 112,200 +10,098=122,298. Yay! So that matches. So that confirms the product is indeed 122,298.\n\nTherefore, I think that's the correct answer. I did multiple methods: standard multiplication, breaking into components, and prime factorization leading to the same result. So I'm confident that 218 multiplied by 561 equals 122,298.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 218 and 561 is \\boxed{122298}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 218 and 561, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm by breaking down the numbers and summing the results:\n\n1. Multiply 218 by 1 (the units place of 561):\n   \\[\n   218 \\times 1 = 218\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 218 by 60 (the tens place of 561, which is \\(6 \\times 10\\)):\n   \\[\n   218 \\times 6 = 1308 \\quad \\text{(then add a zero)} \\quad 13080\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 218 by 500 (the hundreds place of 561, which is \\(5 \\times 100\\)):\n   \\[\n   218 \\times 5 = 1090 \\quad \\text{(then add two zeros)} \\quad 109000\n   \\]\n\n4. Sum the results of the three multiplications:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     \\quad \\quad 218 \\\\\n     \\quad 13080 \\\\\n   + 109000 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     122298 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\nTo verify, we can use prime factorization:\n- \\(218 = 2 \\times 109\\)\n- \\(561 = 3 \\times 11 \\times 17\\)\n\nMultiplying these factors together:\n\\[\n(2 \\times 109) \\times (3 \\times 11 \\times 17) = 2 \\times 3 \\times 11 \\times 17 \\times 109\n\\]\n\nCalculating step-by-step:\n\\[\n2 \\times 3 = 6 \\\\\n6 \\times 11 = 66 \\\\\n66 \\times 17 = 1122 \\\\\n1122 \\times 109 = 122298\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 218 and 561 is \\(\\boxed{122298}\\).",
