vious result. So that's a good check.\n\nTherefore, the product is indeed 714,598.\n\nAlternatively, I can also use a calculator for verification, but since I don't have one here, these cross-checks help ensure that the answer is correct.\n\nWait, just to be thorough, let me try multiplying 829 by 862 in the other order, maybe that will help confirm.\n\nCalculating 829 \u00d7862.\n\nLet me do the same step-by-step:\n\nFirst, break down 862 into 800 +60 +2, so multiply 829 by each part.\n\nFirst, 829 \u00d72 = 1,658.\n\nSecond, 829 \u00d760 = 829 \u00d76 \u00d710. 829\u00d76 is 4,974. \u00d710 is 49,740.\n\nThird, 829 \u00d7800 =829 \u00d78 \u00d7100. 829\u00d78 is 6,632. \u00d7100 is 663,200.\n\nNow add those three results:\n\n1,658 +49,740 =51,398.\n\n51,398 +663,200 = 714,598. Same result! Okay, so that's even better. So the answer is consistent both ways.\n\nTherefore, I can be confident that the product of 862 and 829 is 714,598.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 862 and 829 is \\boxed{714598}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 862 and 829, we use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 862 by 9 (units place of 829):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   862 \\times 9 &= 7758 \\\\\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 862 by 20 (tens place of 829):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   862 \\times 2 &= 1724 \\\\\n   1724 \\times 10 &= 17240 \\\\\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 862 by 800 (hundreds place of 829):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   862 \\times 8 &= 6896 \\\\\n   6896 \\times 100 &= 689600 \\\\\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   7758 + 17240 &= 24998 \\\\\n   24998 + 689600 &= 714598 \\\\\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Verification using an alternative method:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   862 \\times 829 &= 862 \\times (830 - 1) \\\\\n   &= 862 \\times 830 - 862 \\times 1 \\\\\n   &= (862 \\times 800 + 862 \\times 30) - 862 \\\\\n   &= (689600 + 25860)