arby, but since I can't, I'll see if my two methods agree. Since both the standard algorithm and the distributive method give me 444,486, I think that's correct.\n\nWait, just to be thorough, maybe do another check with approximate estimation. Let's see. 798 is roughly 800, and 557 is roughly 550. 800\u00d7550 = 440,000. Our result is 444,486, which is about 4,486 more. Since we approximated both numbers down a bit, the actual product should be a bit higher than 440k, which it is. So that seems plausible.\n\nAlternatively, compute 800\u00d7557 = 800\u00d7500 +800\u00d757 =400,000 +45,600 =445,600. Then subtract 2\u00d7557 = 1,114. So 445,600 -1,114 =444,486. Yep, that's the same as before.\n\nTherefore, I'm confident that the product of 798 and 557 is 444,486.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 798 and 557 is \\boxed{444486}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 798 and 557, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify it using the distributive property.\n\n### Step-by-Step Multiplication:\n\n1. **Multiply 798 by 7 (units place of 557):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   7 \\times 8 &= 56 \\quad (\\text{write 6, carry over 5}) \\\\\n   7 \\times 9 &= 63 + 5 = 68 \\quad (\\text{write 8, carry over 6}) \\\\\n   7 \\times 7 &= 49 + 6 = 55 \\quad (\\text{write 55})\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n   Result: 5586\n\n2. **Multiply 798 by 5 (tens place of 557, shifted one position left):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   5 \\times 8 &= 40 \\quad (\\text{write 0, carry over 4}) \\\\\n   5 \\times 9 &= 45 + 4 = 49 \\quad (\\text{write 9, carry over 4}) \\\\\n   5 \\times 7 &= 35 + 4 = 39 \\quad (\\text{write 39})\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n   Result (shifted left by one): 39900\n\n3. **Multiply 798 by 5 (hundreds place of 557, shifted two positions left):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   5 \\times 8 &= 40 \\quad (\\text{write 0, carry over 4}) \\\\\n   5 \\times 9 &= 45 + 4 = 49 \\quad (\\text{write 9, carry over 4}) \\\\\n   5 \\times 7 &= 35 + 4 = 39 \\quad (\\text{write 39})\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n   Result (shifted left by two): 399000\n\n4. **Add all partial products:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align}\n   5586 + 39900 &= 45486 \\\\\n   45486 + 399000 &= 444486\n   \\end{align}\n   \\]\n\n### Verification using Distributive Property:\n\\[\n(800 - 2) \\times (500 + 50 + 7)\n\\]\n1. Expand and compute:\n   \\[\n   800 \\times (500 + 50 + 7) = 400000 + 40000 + 5600 = 445600\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   2 \\times (500 + 50 + 7) = 1000 + 100 + 14 = 1114\n   \\]\n2. Subtract:\n   \\[\n   445600 - 1114 = 444486\n   \\]\n\n### Final Answer:\nThe product of 798 and 557 is \\boxed{444486}.",
