messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 911 and 308?', "<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 911 and 308. Hmm, let me think. I remember that multiplying larger numbers can be done by breaking them down into smaller parts. Maybe I can use the distributive property here. Let me write this out step by step.\n\nFirst, I'll write down the numbers:.\n\n911 × 308.\n\nI think breaking down 308 into 300 + 8 might make it easier. So, using the distributive property:.\n\n911 × (300 + 8) = (911 × 300) + (911 × 8).\n\nAlright, let me compute each part separately. Starting with 911 × 300. Since 300 is 3 × 100, I can do 911 × 3 first and then multiply by 100.\n\nCalculating 911 × 3:.\n\n900 × 3 = 2700.\n11 × 3 = 33.\nAdding those together: 2700 + 33 = 2733.\n\nSo, 911 × 300 = 2733 × 100 = 273,300.\n\nNow, the second part is 911 × 8. Let me compute that.\n\nBreaking down 911 × 8:.\n\n900 × 8 = 7,200.\n11 × 8 = 88.\nAdding them together: 7,200 + 88 = 7,288.\n\nSo, 911 × 8 = 7,288.\n\nNow, add the two results together:.\n\n273,300 + 7,288.\n\nLet me add these step by step. .\n\n273,300 + 7,000 = 280,300. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
