 them gives 273,300 +7,288. Let me add the thousands first: 273,300 +7,000 = 280,300, then add the remaining 288 gives 280,588. Yep.\n\nAlternatively, let me check if 280,588 divided by 308 equals 911, to verify.\n\nSo 280,588 \u00f7 308. Let's see:\n\n308 \u00d7 900 = 277,200.\n\nSubtract that from 280,588: 280,588 - 277,200 = 3,388.\n\nNow, 308 \u00d7 11 = 3,388 (since 308\u00d710 is 3,080 plus 308 is 3,388).\n\nSo total is 900 + 11 = 911. Perfect, that checks out. So yes, 308 \u00d7 911 is indeed 280,588.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 280,588.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 911 and 308 is \\boxed{280588}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 911 and 308, we can use the distributive property by breaking down 308 into 300 and 8:\n\n\\[\n911 \\times 308 = 911 \\times (300 + 8) = (911 \\times 300) + (911 \\times 8)\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(911 \\times 300\\):\n\n\\[\n911 \\times 300 = 911 \\times 3 \\times 100 = 2733 \\times 100 = 273300\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(911 \\times 8\\):\n\n\\[\n911 \\times 8 = (900 \\times 8) + (11 \\times 8) = 7200 + 88 = 7288\n\\]\n\nAdd the two results together:\n\n\\[\n273300 + 7288 = 280588\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n- Multiply 911 by 8 (units place): \\(911 \\times 8 = 7288\\)\n- Multiply 911 by 0 (tens place): \\(911 \\times 0 = 0\\)\n- Multiply 911 by 3 (hundreds place): \\(911 \\times 300 = 273300\\)\n\nAdding these results:\n\n\\[\n7288 + 0 + 273300 = 280588\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 911 and 308 is \\(\\boxed{280588}\\).",
