47: 847\u00d76=5,082, so \u00d710 is 50,820. So adding 254,100 +50,820 = 304,920. Then subtract 847. 304,920 -847: 304,920 - 800 is 304,120, then subtract 47 more gives 304,073. Yes, correct.\n\nTherefore, both methods give me the same answer, so I think that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do another check using digital roots or modulo 9.\n\nThe digital root method: the digital root of a product is the product of the digital roots modulo 9.\n\nFirst, compute digital root of 359.\n\n3 +5 +9 =17 \u2192 1+7=8.\n\nDigital root of 847: 8+4+7=19 \u21921+9=10\u21921+0=1.\n\nSo the product's digital root should be 8\u00d71=8 mod9.\n\nNow, let's compute the digital root of the answer 304,073.\n\n3+0+4+0+7+3 = 3+0=3, +4=7, +0=7, +7=14, +3=17 \u21921+7=8. So that matches. So that gives another check.\n\nAlternatively, check modulo 11.\n\nThe alternating sum for 359: (3 -5 +9)=7.\n\nFor 847: (8 -4 +7)=11 \u2192 which is 11 mod11=0.\n\nThe product's modulo11 would be 7\u00d70=0 mod11.\n\nSo let's check 304,073.\n\nAlternating sum: 3 -0 +4 -0 +7 -3 = (3+4+7) - (0+0+3)=14 -3=11. 11 mod11 is 0. Which matches.\n\nTherefore, that also checks out.\n\nOkay, so with multiple methods cross-verifying, I'm pretty sure that the product is indeed 304,073. So I think that's the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 359 and 847 is \\boxed{304073}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 359 and 847, we use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 359 by the units digit (7):**\n   \\[\n   359 \\times 7 = 2513\n   \\]\n   - \\(9 \\times 7 = 63\\) (write 3, carry over 6)\n   - \\(5 \\times 7 + 6 = 35 + 6 = 41\\) (write 1, carry over 4)\n   - \\(3 \\times 7 + 4 = 21 + 4 = 25\\) (write 25)\n\n2. **Multiply 359 by the tens digit (4) and shift one position left:**\n   \\[\n   359 \\times 40 = 14360\n   \\]\n   - \\(359 \\times 4 = 1436\\)\n   - Shift left by one: \\(14360\\)\n\n3. **Multiply 359 by the hundreds digit (8) and shift two positions left:**\n   \\[\n   359 \\times 800 = 287200\n   \\]\n   - \\(359 \\times 8 = 2872\\)\n   - Shift left by two: \\(287200\\)\n\n4. **Add all partial products:**\n   \\[\n   2513 + 14360 + 287200\n   \\]\n   - First, add \\(2513 + 14360 = 16873\\)\n   - Then, add \\(16873 + 287200 = 304073\\)\n\nCross-verifying using the distributive property and modulo checks confirms the result.\n\n### Final Answer\nThe product of 359 and 847 is \\boxed{304073}.",
