nfirms that 504 \u00d7 791 is indeed 398,664.\n\nTherefore, after multiple checks using different methods and verification through division, I'm confident the answer is correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 504 and 791 is \\boxed{398664}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 504 and 791, we use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 504 by 1 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   504 \\times 1 = 504\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 504 by 90 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   504 \\times 9 = 4536 \\quad \\text{(then add a zero)} \\quad 45360\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 504 by 700 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   504 \\times 7 = 3528 \\quad \\text{(then add two zeros)} \\quad 352800\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     \\phantom{0}504 \\\\\n     45360 \\\\\n   + 352800 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     398664 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add \\(504 + 45360 = 45864\\)\n   - Then add \\(45864 + 352800 = 398664\\)\n\nTo verify, we can use the distributive property:\n\\[\n504 \\times 791 = (500 + 4) \\times 791 = 500 \\times 791 + 4 \\times 791\n\\]\n- \\(500 \\times 791 = 395500\\)\n- \\(4 \\times 791 = 3164\\)\n- Adding these results: \\(395500 + 3164 = 398664\\)\n\nAdditionally, verifying by division:\n\\[\n398664 \\div 504 = 791\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 504 and 791 is \\(\\boxed{398664}\\).",
