ethods lead to 143,820. \n\nWait, but just to be thorough, maybe I can compute it digit by digit. Let's try the standard multiplication:\n\n       705  \n     x204  \n     ------\n       705 x 4 = 2,820  \n       705 x 0 (tens place, so actually 0 shifted one to the left) = 0 shifted left once is 0000  \n       705 x 2 (hundreds place, so 200, so shifted two places) = 1,410 shifted two places is 141,000  \n     Adding them together:  \n       2,820  \n     +   0  \n     +141,000  \n     =143,820.  \n\nYes, that's consistent. I think my initial concern was unnecessary. All methods confirm the same result. Therefore, the product of 705 and 204 is 143,820. \n\nAlternatively, just to ensure there's no arithmetic mistake, let me compute 705*200 first. 700*200=140,000 and 5*200=1,000, so total 141,000. Then 705*4=2,820. Adding those gives 141,000 + 2,820 =143,820. \n\nAlternatively, perhaps use another method: the difference of squares or some other trick? Let me see. Hmm, 705 and 204, not sure if they can be expressed as numbers that would fit into such a formula. Let me check if (a+b)(a-b) or something. Maybe not applicable here. Alternatively, 705 is 700+5, 204 is 200+4, so expanding the product as (700+5)(200+4) which is exactly what I did first. \n\nAlternatively, maybe compute 700*204 +5*204. Let's try that. \n\n700*204: 700*200=140,000 and 700*4=2,800. So total 140,000 +2,800=142,800. \n\nThen 5*204=1,020. \n\nAdding those together: 142,800 +1,020 = 143,820. \n\nSame answer again. \n\nOkay, so multiple methods all give me 143,820. Therefore, I think that's the correct product. I don't see any errors in my calculations now. So, I can confidently say the answer is 143,820.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 705 and 204 is \\boxed{143820}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 705 and 204, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into smaller parts:\n\n\\[\n705 \\times 204 = (700 + 5) \\times (200 + 4)\n\\]\n\nExpanding this using the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n(700 + 5) \\times (200 + 4) = 700 \\times 200 + 700 \\times 4 + 5 \\times 200 + 5 \\times 4\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term separately:\n\n1. \\(700 \\times 200 = 140,000\\)\n2. \\(700 \\times 4 = 2,800\\)\n3. \\(5 \\times 200 = 1,000\\)\n4. \\(5 \\times 4 = 20\\)\n\nAdding these results together:\n\n\\[\n140,000 + 2,800 + 1,000 + 20 = 143,820\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this using the standard vertical multiplication method:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n      705 \\\\\n\\times 204 \\\\\n\\hline\n     2820 \\quad (\\text{705} \\times 4) \\\\\n   0000 \\quad \\quad (\\text{705} \\times 0 \\text{, shifted one position left}) \\\\\n141000 \\quad \\quad (\\text{705} \\times 2 \\text{, shifted two positions left}) \\\\\n\\hline\n143820 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 705 and 204 is \\(\\boxed{143820}\\).",
