right answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 664 and 988 is \\boxed{656032}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 664 and 988, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy:\n\n### Method 1: Distributive Property\n1. Express 988 as \\(1000 - 12\\):\n   \\[\n   664 \\times 988 = 664 \\times (1000 - 12)\n   \\]\n2. Apply the distributive property:\n   \\[\n   664 \\times 1000 - 664 \\times 12\n   \\]\n3. Calculate each term:\n   \\[\n   664 \\times 1000 = 664000\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   664 \\times 12 = 7968\n   \\]\n4. Subtract the results:\n   \\[\n   664000 - 7968 = 656032\n   \\]\n\n### Method 2: Standard Multiplication\n1. Multiply 664 by each digit of 988 and sum the partial products:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     \\quad 664 \\\\\n   \\times 988 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     \\quad 5312 \\quad (\\text{664} \\times 8) \\\\\n    +53120 \\quad (\\text{664} \\times 80) \\\\\n  +597600 \\quad (\\text{664} \\times 900) \\\\\n   \\hline\n     656032 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n2. Summing these gives:\n   \\[\n   5312 + 53120 + 597600 = 656032\n   \\]\n\n### Method 3: Difference of Squares\n1. Express the numbers as \\(826 \\pm 162\\):\n   \\[\n   664 \\times 988 = (826 - 162)(826 + 162)\n   \\]\n2. Apply the difference of squares formula:\n   \\[\n   826^2 - 162^2\n   \\]\n3. Calculate each square:\n   \\[\n   826^2 = 682276 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 162^2 = 26244\n   \\]\n4. Subtract the results:\n   \\[\n   682276 - 26244 = 656032\n   \\]\n\n### Method 4: Breaking into Components\n1. Break down 988 into 900, 80, and 8:\n   \\[\n   664 \\times 988 = 664 \\times (900 + 80 + 8)\n   \\]\n2. Calculate each term:\n   \\[\n   664 \\times 900 = 597600, \\quad 664 \\times 80 = 53120, \\quad 664 \\times 8 = 5312\n   \\]\n3. Sum the results:\n   \\[\n   597600 + 53120 + 5312 = 656032\n   \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 664 and 988 is \\(\\boxed{656032}\\).",
