+1=6. So that gives 675. Then adding two zeros makes it 67500.\n\nNow I need to add all three partial products together:.\n\nFirst partial product: 135.\n\nSecond partial product: 12,150.\n\nThird partial product: 67,500.\n\nAdding them up step by step. Let's start with 135 + 12,150. .\n\n135 + 12,150: 12,150 + 100 is 12,250, then +35 is 12,285.\n\nThen add 67,500 to that. 12,285 + 67,500. Let's see, 12,285 + 60,000 = 72,285. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
