243,660.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 465 and 524 is \\boxed{243660}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 465 and 524, we use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 465 by 4 (units place of 524):**\n   \\[\n   4 \\times 465 = 1860\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 465 by 20 (tens place of 524, shifted one position left):**\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 465 = 930 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by one digit: 9300)}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 465 by 500 (hundreds place of 524, shifted two positions left):**\n   \\[\n   5 \\times 465 = 2325 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by two digits: 232500)}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   1860 + 9300 + 232500\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add 1860 and 9300:\n     \\[\n     1860 + 9300 = 11160\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to 232500:\n     \\[\n     11160 + 232500 = 243660\n     \\]\n\nVerification using different methods (breaking down numbers and distributive property) confirms the result.\n\nThe product of 465 and 524 is \\(\\boxed{243660}\\).",
