product of 851 and 816, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 851 by 6 (units place of 816):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   851 \\times 6 &= 5106 \\\\\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 851 by 1 (tens place of 816, shifted one position to the left):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   851 \\times 10 &= 8510 \\\\\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 851 by 8 (hundreds place of 816, shifted two positions to the left):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   851 \\times 800 &= 680800 \\\\\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   5106 + 8510 + 680800 &= 5106 + 8510 + 680800 \\\\\n   &= 13616 + 680800 \\\\\n   &= 694416 \\\\\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n\nTo verify, we can use the distributive property:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n851 \\times 816 &= 851 \\times (800 + 16) \\\\\n&= 851 \\times 800 + 851 \\times 16 \\\\\n&= 680800 + 13616 \\\\\n&= 694416 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 851 and 816 is \\(\\boxed{694416}\\).",
