=143, 11*14=154, so no. 13? 13*11=143, 13*12=156. So maybe 149 is prime. Hmm, so maybe that's not helpful.\n\nAlternatively, maybe approximate to check. Let's see, 150 times 800 is 120,000. But 149 is 1 less than 150, and 831 is 31 more than 800. So maybe the exact value would be (150 -1)*(800 +31). Let's expand that: 150*800 +150*31 -1*800 -1*31. \n\nCalculating each term:\n\n150\u00d7800 = 120,000.\n\n150\u00d731: 150\u00d730=4,500 and 150\u00d71=150, so total 4,650.\n\nThen subtract (1\u00d7800)=800 and (1\u00d731)=31. \n\nSo total is 120,000 + 4,650 = 124,650. Then subtract 800 +31 = 831. So 124,650 -831 = ?\n\n124,650 minus 800 is 123,850, then minus 31 more is 123,819. \n\nWait, that's the same answer as before! So that's a good sign. So that confirms that the product is indeed 123,819. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check using a calculator, but since I don't have one here, let me try another way. Let me do 149 \u00d7800 = 119,200. Then 149\u00d731. Let's compute 149\u00d730=4,470 and 149\u00d71=149, so total 4,470 +149=4,619. Then 119,200 +4,619=123,819. Yep, same result again. \n\nHmm, so all methods are pointing towards 123,819. Maybe my initial doubt was unfounded. Let me just ensure there's no arithmetic mistake in any step. Let me verify each multiplication again:\n\nFirst step: 149 \u00d7800. 149 \u00d78 is 1,192. Adding two zeros gives 119,200. Correct.\n\nSecond: 149 \u00d730. 149 \u00d73 is 447, times 10 is 4,470. Correct.\n\nThird: 149 \u00d71 is 149. Correct.\n\nAdding them: 119,200 +4,470 = 123,670. Then +149: 123,670 +100 is 123,770, plus 49 is 123,819. \n\nAlternatively, adding 149 to 123,670: 123,670 + 149. Let's add 123,670 + 150 = 123,820, then subtract 1 gives 123,819. That works. \n\nAlright, so after verifying through multiple methods\u2014breaking down the numbers, using the distributive property, and cross-checking with an approximate calculation\u2014I can be confident that the product of 149 and 831 is indeed 123,819. I think that's the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 149 and 831 is \\boxed{123819}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 149 and 831, we can use the distributive property by breaking down 831 into 800 + 30 + 1:\n\n1. Calculate \\(149 \\times 800\\):\n   \\[\n   149 \\times 800 = 149 \\times 8 \\times 100 = 1192 \\times 100 = 119200\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\(149 \\times 30\\):\n   \\[\n   149 \\times 30 = 149 \\times 3 \\times 10 = 447 \\times 10 = 4470\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate \\(149 \\times 1\\):\n   \\[\n   149 \\times 1 = 149\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the results of the three calculations:\n   \\[\n   119200 + 4470 + 149\n   \\]\n\n   First, add \\(119200\\) and \\(4470\\):\n   \\[\n   119200 + 4470 = 123670\n   \\]\n\n   Then add \\(149\\) to the result:\n   \\[\n   123670 + 149 = 123819\n   \\]\n\nTo verify, we can use another method by expanding \\((150 - 1) \\times (800 + 31)\\):\n\\[\n(150 - 1) \\times (800 + 31) = 150 \\times 800 + 150 \\times 31 - 1 \\times 800 - 1 \\times 31\n\\]\n\\[\n= 120000 + 4650 - 800 - 31\n\\]\n\\[\n= 124650 - 831 = 123819\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 149 and 831 is \\(\\boxed{123819}\\).",
