\nLet me recalculate the difference for 235,672.\n\nDigits: 2 (1st),3(2nd),5(3rd),6(4th),7(5th),2(6th).\n\nSum of odd positions (1st,3rd,5th): 2 +5 +7 =14.\n\nSum of even positions (2nd,4th,6th):3 +6 +2 =11.\n\nDifference is 14-11=3. So mod11 is 3.\n\nBut according to the factors, it should be (2\u00d74)=8 mod11.\n\nHmm, so that inconsistency suggests an error somewhere.\n\nWait, so either my final result is wrong, or I messed up the modulo calculation.\n\nWait, let me recalculate 662 mod11.\n\n662 divided by 11:\n\n11\u00d760=660, so 662-660=2. So mod11 is 2. That's correct.\n\n356 divided by11:11\u00d732=352, 356-352=4. So mod11 is4. So 2\u00d74=8 mod11. So the product mod11 should be 8, but the result 235672 mod11 is3. So discrepancy here. Therefore, that suggests that the product is wrong?\n\nHmm, so this is a problem. Let me check my final result again.\n\nWait, first, let me recalculate 662\u00d7356 using another method to see if I actually got 235,672.\n\nLet me compute 662\u00d7356 again step by step using the standard algorithm.\n\n662 \u00d7356.\n\nFirst, multiply by 6 (units place):\n\n662 \u00d76:\n\n2\u00d76=12. Write 2, carryover1.\n\n6\u00d76=36 +1=37. Write7, carryover3.\n\n6\u00d76=36 +3=39. So 3972. Correct.\n\nNext, multiply by 5 (tens place). So 662 \u00d75 =3310, but shifted one place to the left (i.e., \u00d710) \u2192 33100.\n\nThen multiply by3 (hundreds place):662\u00d73=1986, shifted two places to the left (\u00d7100) \u2192198600.\n\nNow add the three partial products:\n\n3972\n\n+33100\n\n=37072.\n\n37072 +198600 =235,672. Wait, but that's what I had before, but modulo11 discrepancy. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps my modulo calculation is wrong.\n\nWait, let me recompute 235,672 mod11 again.\n\nAlternative method for mod11: take alternating sum from the right.\n\nWait, the standard method is to take the digits from right to left, alternating adding and subtracting.\n\nWait, let's do that.\n\nNumber:235,672.\n\nDigits from right:2 (positio