n     \\[\n     662 \\times 6 = 3972\n     \\]\n   - Sum the results:\n     \\[\n     198600 + 33100 + 3972 = 235672\n     \\]\n\n3. **Verification using Russian Peasant Multiplication:**\n   - Halve and double the numbers, then sum the appropriate terms:\n     \\[\n     \\begin{array}{c|c}\n     \\text{Left (a)} & \\text{Right (b)} \\\\\n     \\hline\n     662 & 356 \\\\\n     331 & 712 \\quad (\\text{odd}) \\\\\n     165 & 1424 \\quad (\\text{odd}) \\\\\n     82 & 2848 \\quad (\\text{even}) \\\\\n     41 & 5696 \\quad (\\text{odd}) \\\\\n     20 & 11392 \\quad (\\text{even}) \\\\\n     10 & 22784 \\quad (\\text{even}) \\\\\n     5 & 45568 \\quad (\\text{odd}) \\\\\n     2 & 91136 \\quad (\\text{even}) \\\\\n     1 & 182272 \\quad (\\text{odd}) \\\\\n     \\end{array}\n     \\]\n   - Sum the terms where the left column is odd:\n     \\[\n     712 + 1424 + 5696 + 45568 + 182272 = 235672\n     \\]\n\n4. **Modulo 11 Check:**\n   - Digital roots and modulo calculations confirm the result is consistent.\n\nAfter multiple methods and checks, the product of 662 and 356 is \\boxed{235672}.",
