ro: \\(13410\\)\n\n3. **Multiply 447 by 500 (hundreds place of 539):**\n   \\[\n   500 \\times 447 = 223500\n   \\]\n   - \\(5 \\times 447 = 2235\\)\n   - Add two zeros: \\(223500\\)\n\nNext, we sum the partial products:\n\\[\n4023 + 13410 + 223500\n\\]\n\nAligning and adding the partial products:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   4023 \\\\\n+ 13410 \\\\\n+223500 \\\\\n\\hline\n  240933 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n- Break down 447 and 539 into hundreds, tens, and units:\n  - \\(447 = 400 + 40 + 7\\)\n  - \\(539 = 500 + 30 + 9\\)\n- Multiply each term and sum the results:\n  \\[\n  (400 \\times 500) + (400 \\times 30) + (400 \\times 9) + (40 \\times 500) + (40 \\times 30) + (40 \\times 9) + (7 \\times 500) + (7 \\times 30) + (7 \\times 9)\n  \\]\n  - Calculations:\n    - \\(200000 + 12000 + 3600 + 20000 + 1200 + 360 + 3500 + 210 + 63 = 240933\\)\n\nBoth methods confirm the product is \\(\\boxed{240933}\\).",
