mpute 228 \u00d745 first.\n\n228 \u00d745: 228\u00d7(40 +5) =228\u00d740 +228\u00d75.\n\n228\u00d740: 228\u00d74\u00d710 =912\u00d710=9,120.\n\n228\u00d75: 1,140.\n\nSo 9,120 +1,140 =10,260. Then \u00d710 gives 102,600. Then subtract 228: 102,600 -228 = 102,372. Same answer again. Yay! That's another way to do it and confirms the result.\n\nSo through three different methods: standard multiplication, distributive property expansion, and breaking into 450-1, all leading to 102,372. So I feel confident that's the correct answer. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, so I think that's the product.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 228 and 449 is \\boxed{102372}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 228 and 449, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify it with alternative methods.\n\n### Standard Multiplication Algorithm:\n1. **Multiply 228 by 9 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   228 \\times 9 = 2052\n   \\]\n2. **Multiply 228 by 40 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   228 \\times 40 = 9120\n   \\]\n3. **Multiply 228 by 400 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   228 \\times 400 = 91200\n   \\]\n4. **Sum the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   2052 + 9120 + 91200 = 102372\n   \\]\n\n### Verification using Distributive Property:\n1. **Expand both numbers:**\n   \\[\n   (200 + 28) \\times (400 + 49)\n   \\]\n2. **Calculate each term:**\n   \\[\n   200 \\times 400 = 80000\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   200 \\times 49 = 9800\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   28 \\times 400 = 11200\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   28 \\times 49 = 1372\n   \\]\n3. **Sum the terms:**\n   \\[\n   80000 + 9800 + 11200 + 1372 = 102372\n   \\]\n\n### Verification using 449 as 450 - 1:\n1. **Break down the multiplication:**\n   \\[\n   228 \\times (450 - 1) = 228 \\times 450 - 228 \\times 1\n   \\]\n2. **Calculate each part:**\n   \\[\n   228 \\times 450 = 102600\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   228 \\times 1 = 228\n   \\]\n3. **Subtract the results:**\n   \\[\n   102600 - 228 = 102372\n   \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 228 and 449 is \\(\\boxed{102372}\\).",
