 that matches.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another method, like the lattice method or another way?\n\nAlternatively, perhaps breaking down both numbers further.\n\nAlternatively, using the formula (a + b)(c + d) = ac + ad + bc + bd.\n\nBut perhaps overcomplicating. Since two different methods have given me 158,422, I can be more confident. Let me check with a calculator approach, mentally.\n\nAlternatively, 379 x 418.\n\nIf I approximate 380 x 400 = 152,000. Then 380 x 18 = 6,840, so total would be 152,000 + 6,840 = 158,840. But since I used 380 instead of 379, which is 1 more, so subtract 1 x 418 = 418. So 158,840 - 418 = 158,840 - 400 -18 = 158,440 -18 = 158,422. That matches again. So that's another way to verify. Okay, so that's a third method giving the same answer. So I think that's correct.\n\nThus, the product of 379 and 418 is 158,422.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 379 and 418 is \\boxed{158422}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 379 and 418, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 379 by 8 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   379 \\times 8 = 3032\n   \\]\n   - Breakdown: \\(300 \\times 8 = 2400\\), \\(70 \\times 8 = 560\\), \\(9 \\times 8 = 72\\)\n   - Sum: \\(2400 + 560 + 72 = 3032\\)\n\n2. **Multiply 379 by 10 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   379 \\times 10 = 3790\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 379 by 400 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   379 \\times 400 = 151600\n   \\]\n   - Breakdown: \\(379 \\times 4 = 1516\\), then add two zeros: \\(1516 \\times 100 = 151600\\)\n\n4. **Add all partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   3032 + 3790 + 151600\n   \\]\n   - First, add \\(3032 + 3790\\):\n     \\[\n     3032 + 3790 = 6822\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to \\(151600\\):\n     \\[\n     151600 + 6822 = 158422\n     \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n- \\(379 \\times 418 = 379 \\times (400 + 18) = 379 \\times 400 + 379 \\times 18\\)\n- \\(379 \\times 400 = 151600\\)\n- \\(379 \\times 18 = 6822\\)\n- Sum: \\(151600 + 6822 = 158422\\)\n\nAnother verification using approximation:\n- \\(380 \\times 400 = 152000\\)\n- \\(380 \\times 18 = 6840\\)\n- Total: \\(152000 + 6840 = 158840\\)\n- Adjust for the extra 1 in 380: \\(158840 - 418 = 158422\\)\n\nThus, the product of 379 and 418 is \\(\\boxed{158422}\\).",
