 = 80.\n\n2\u00d73 =6.\n\nNow add all these up:\n\n320,000 +16,000 +1,200 +1,600 +80 +6.\n\nLet's add step by step:\n\n320,000 +16,000 = 336,000.\n\n336,000 +1,200 = 337,200.\n\n337,200 +1,600 = 338,800.\n\n338,800 +80 = 338,880.\n\n338,880 +6 = 338,886.\n\nOkay, so that matches the previous result. So that's a good check.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method, like the lattice method, but that might take longer. Alternatively, verify using calculator steps.\n\nAlternatively, let me do 402 \u00d7 800 = 321,600 (since 402 \u00d78 =3,216, so \u00d7100 gives 321,600).\n\nThen 402 \u00d740 = 16,080 (since 402 \u00d74=1,608, so \u00d710 gives 16,080).\n\nThen 402 \u00d73 = 1,206.\n\nAdding those three: 321,600 +16,080 is 337,680, plus 1,206 gives 338,886. Yep, same answer.\n\nHmm, so that seems consistent. So I think the correct product is 338,886.\n\nWait, but let me confirm once more with another approach. Maybe approximate to check if it's reasonable.\n\n400 \u00d7 800 = 320,000. The actual numbers are a bit higher: 402 is 2 more than 400, and 843 is 43 more than 800. So the product should be a bit more than 320k. 338k seems reasonable.\n\nAlternatively, 400\u00d7843 = 337,200. Then add 2\u00d7843 =1,686. So 337,200 +1,686 = 338,886. Exactly the same result. Perfect, that's another way to compute it.\n\nYes, so that gives me confidence that 338,886 is the correct answer. I think that's solid. So I can conclude that the product of 402 and 843 is 338,886.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 402 and 843 is \\boxed{338886}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 402 and 843, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify the result through different methods.\n\nFirst, we break down the multiplication into partial products:\n\n1. Multiply 402 by 3 (units place of 843):\n   \\[\n   402 \\times 3 = 1206\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 402 by 40 (tens place of 843, which is 4 shifted one position to the left):\n   \\[\n   402 \\times 40 = 16080\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 402 by 800 (hundreds place of 843, which is 8 shifted two positions to the left):\n   \\[\n   402 \\times 800 = 321600\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the partial products:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n1206 + 16080 &= 17286, \\\\\n17286 + 321600 &= 338886.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we use the distributive property:\n\\[\n(400 + 2) \\times (800 + 40 + 3)\n\\]\nExpanding this, we get:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n400 \\times 800 &= 320000, \\\\\n400 \\times 40 &= 16000, \\\\\n400 \\times 3 &= 1200, \\\\\n2 \\times 800 &= 1600, \\\\\n2 \\times 40 &= 80, \\\\\n2 \\times 3 &= 6.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\nSumming these results:\n\\[\n320000 + 16000 + 1200 + 1600 + 80 + 6 = 338886.\n\\]\n\nAnother verification method:\n\\[\n402 \\times 800 = 321600, \\\\\n402 \\times 40 = 16080, \\\\\n402 \\times 3 = 1206.\n\\]\nAdding these:\n\\[\n321600 + 16080 + 1206 = 338886.\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 402 and 843 is \\(\\boxed{338886}\\).",
