Wait, maybe this is getting too involved, but let me try.\n\nDividend: 190,146.\n\nDivisor: 402.\n\nFirst, determine how many times 402 goes into the first three digits: 190. Since 402 is larger than 190, we take the first four digits: 1901.\n\nHow many times does 402 go into 1901?\n\n402 \u00d74 = 1,608.\n\n402\u00d75=2,010 which is too big. So 4 times. 4 \u00d7402 is 1,608. Subtract that from 1,901:\n\n1901 - 1608 = 293.\n\nBring down the next digit, which is 4, making it 2934.\n\nNow, how many times does 402 go into 2934?\n\n402 \u00d77 = 2,814. 402\u00d77=2,814.\n\nSubtract that from 2,934: 2934-2814=120.\n\nBring down the next digit, which is 6, making it 1206.\n\nHow many times does 402 go into 1206?\n\n402\u00d73=1,206. Exactly. So 3 times.\n\nSo putting it all together: 4 (from the first division), then 7, then 3. So the quotient is 473, with no remainder. Therefore, 402 \u00d7473 =190,146. So that checks out.\n\nTherefore, after multiple methods and verification through division, I can be confident that the product is indeed 190,146.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 473 and 402 is \\boxed{190146}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 473 and 402, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 473 by 2 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   473 \\times 2 = 946\n   \\]\n   Result: 946\n\n2. **Multiply 473 by 0 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   473 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n   Shifted one position to the left (equivalent to multiplying by 10): 0000\n\n3. **Multiply 473 by 4 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   473 \\times 4 = 1892\n   \\]\n   Shifted two positions to the left (equivalent to multiplying by 100): 189200\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   946 + 0000 + 189200 = 190146\n   \\]\n\nVerification through division:\n- Dividing 190146 by 402 confirms the result:\n  \\[\n  190146 \\div 402 = 473\n  \\]\n\nThus, the product of 473 and 402 is \\(\\boxed{190146}\\).",
