messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 911 and 467?', "<think>Okay, so I need to find the product of 911 and 467. Hmm, let me think. I remember that multiplying large numbers can be done using the standard algorithm, but I should probably break it down step by step to avoid mistakes. Let me write it out like the multiplication they taught us in school.\n\nFirst, I'll write 911 on top and 467 below it, aligning the digits properly. Wait, actually, since multiplication can be done either way, but I think it's easier to have the smaller number on the bottom. Let me confirm: 911 is a three-digit number and 467 is also three digits, so maybe it doesn't matter. Let me just start.\n\nSo:.\n\n```.\n   911.\n× 467.\n-------.\n```.\n\nAlright, I need to multiply each digit of the bottom number (467) by the top number (911), starting from the rightmost digit. Let's start with the units place first. The units digit of 467 is 7. So I'll multiply 911 by 7 first.\n\nCalculating 911 × 7. Let's do that:.\n\n900 × 7 = 6300.\n\n10 × 7 = 70.\n\n1 × 7 = 7.\n\nAdding those together: 6300 + 70 = 6370, plus 7 is 6377. Wait, is that right? Wait, actually, maybe I should do it digit by digit to be precise.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\n1 (units) ×7 = 7.\n\n1 (tens) ×7 = 7, but since it's the tens place, that's 70.\n\n9 (hundreds) ×7 = 63, which is 6300.\n\nAdding those: 7 + 70 + 6300 = 6377. Okay, that seems correct. So that's the first partial product: 6377.\n\nNow, moving to the next digit in 467, which is the tens place. That's 6, but since it's the tens place, it's actually 60. So I need to multiply 911 by 60. But when writing it out, we can do 911 ×6 first and then shift it one place to the left (because of the tens place). Let me compute 911 ×6.\n\nAgain, breaking it down:.\n\n900 ×6 = 5400.\n\n10 ×6 = 60.\n\n1 ×6 = 6.\n\nAdding them: 5400 + 60 = 5460 +6 = 5466. Wait, but since it's actually 60, the total would be 5466 ×10? Wait no, no. Wait, actually, when you multiply by the tens digit, you just shift the result one place to the left. So 911 ×6 is 5466, and then multiplied by 10, it becomes 54,660? Wait, hold on, maybe I need to check again.\n\nWait, actually, when you do multiplication step by step:.\n\nThe second partial product is 911 ×6 (the tens digit), so the result is 5466, but since it's the tens place, you write it shifted one position to the left, which effectively multiplies it by 10. So that's 54660.\n\nWait, let me verify by calculating 911 ×6:.\n\n911 ×6:.\n\n900×6=5400.\n\n10×6=60 → 5400+60=5460.\n\n1×6=6 → 5460+6=5466. So yes, 5466. Then shifted left by one digit (because of the tens place) becomes 54,660. Okay, that's the second partial product.\n\nNow moving to the hundreds place of 467, which is 4. Since it's the hundreds place, that's 400. So we need to multiply 911 by 400. Again, first multiply 911 ×4, then shift two places to the left (since it's hundreds).\n\nCalculating 911 ×4:.\n\n900×4=3600.\n\n10×4=40 → 3600+40=3640.\n\n1×4=4 → 3640 +4 = 3644.\n\nSo that's 3644, and then multiplied by 100 (shift two places) gives 364,400.\n\nNow, adding up all three partial products:.\n\nFirst partial product: 6,377.\n\nSecond partial product: 54,660.\n\nThird partial product: 364,400.\n\nLet me write them down aligned properly:.\n\n     6,377.\n\n   +54,660.\n\n   +364,400.\n\n----------.\n\nLet me add the first two: 6,377 +54,660.\n\n6,377 + 54,660:.\n\n6,000 +54,000 =60,000.\n\n377 +660 = 1,037.\n\nTotal so far: 60,000 +1,037 =61,037.\n\nWait, that's not right. Wait, actually, adding 6,377 and 54,660:.\n\n6,377.\n\n+54,660.\n\n= ?.\n\nLet me do it digit by digit:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\n7 +0 =7.\n\n7 +6 =13, write down 3, carryover 1.\n\n3 +6 +1 (carryover) = 10, write down 0, carryover 1.\n\n6 +4 +1 (carryover) =11, write down 1, carryover 1.\n\n0 (since 54,660 has no digit there) +5 +1 (carryover) =6.\n\nWait, maybe writing it out:.\n\n6,377.\n\n+54,660.\n\nAlign them:.\n\n   6,377.\n\n+54,660.\n\n=?.\n\nAdding units digit: 7 +0 =7.\n\nTens: 7 +6 =13, write 3, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds: 3 +6 =9 plus 1 carried over is 10, write 0, carryover 1.\n\nThousands: 6 +4 =10 plus 1 carried over is 11, write 1, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands: 0 +5 +1 carried over =6.\n\nSo total is 61,037. Wait, but 54,660 +6,377:.\n\n54,660 +6,000 is 60,660, plus 377 is 61,037. Yes, correct.\n\nNow add that to the third partial product: 61,037 +364,400.\n\nLet me do that:.\n\n61,037.\n\n+364,400.\n\n------------.\n\nAdding units digits:.\n\n7 +0=7.\n\n3 +0=3.\n\n0 +4=4.\n\n1 +6=7.\n\n6 +4=10.\n\nWait, let's do it properly:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nUnits: 7 +0=7.\n\nTens: 3 +0=3.\n\nHundreds: 0 +4=4.\n\nThousands:1 (from 61,037) +4 (from 364,400) =5?.\n\nWait, hold on, perhaps breaking down:.\n\n61,037 is:.\n\n6 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 7 (units).\n\n364,400 is:.\n\n3 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 0 (units).\n\nWait, actually, 364,400 is 3 hundred thousands, 6 ten thousands, 4 thousands, 4 hundreds, 0 tens, 0 units.\n\nWait, but adding 61,037 (which is 0 hundred thousands, 6 ten thousands, 1 thousand, 0 hundreds, 3 tens, 7 units) to 364,400 (3 hundred thousands, 6 ten thousands, 4 thousands, 4 hundreds, 0 tens, 0 units):.\n\nSo aligning:.\n\n          61,037.\n\n+      364,400.\n\n-----------------.\n\nLet me write them vertically:.\n\n    61,037.\n\n+ 364,400.\n\n------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:.\n\nUnits place: 7 +0 =7.\n\nTens place: 3 +0 =3.\n\nHundreds place:0 +4 =4.\n\nThousands place:1 +4 =5.\n\nTen-thousands place:6 +6 =12.\n\nHundred-thousands place:0 +3 =3.\n\nBut wait, let me check again:.\n\nWait, 61,037 is:.\n\nDigit positions:.\n\nHundred thousands: 0.\n\nTen thousands:6.\n\nThousands:1.\n\nHundreds:0.\n\nTens:3.\n\nUnits:7.\n\n364,400 is:.\n\nHundred thousands:3.\n\nTen thousands:6.\n\nThousands:4.\n\nHundreds:4.\n\nTens:0.\n\nUnits:0.\n\nAdding each