ial product.\n\nNow the hundreds digit is 4, which is 400. So 4\u00d7911 and then shifted two places.\n\n4\u00d7911:\n\n4\u00d71=4 (units).\n\n4\u00d71=4 (tens).\n\n4\u00d79=36 (hundreds).\n\nSo 3644. Then shifted two places gives 364,400. Correct.\n\nAdding the three partial products:\n\n6,377.\n\n+54,660.\n\n=61,037.\n\n+364,400.\n\n=425,437.\n\nHmm, that seems consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe check with another method, like estimating to see if the answer is reasonable.\n\nEstimate: 900 \u00d7450 = 405,000. Since 911 is a bit more than 900 and 467 is a bit more than 450, so 405,000 plus some extra. The actual answer we got is 425,437, which is 20,437 more. That seems plausible.\n\nAlternatively, another way to compute 911 \u00d7467.\n\nLet me try breaking down 467 into 400 +60 +7, so:\n\n911\u00d7400 = 364,400.\n\n911\u00d760 =54,660.\n\n911\u00d77 =6,377.\n\nSame as before, adding them gives 364,400 +54,660 =419,060; plus 6,377 is 425,437. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, cross-multiplying.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps using a calculator would be best, but since I can't do that here, I have to trust my step-by-step.\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the addition step when adding 6,377 +54,660.\n\nWait, 6,377 +54,660.\n\nLet me add 6,000 +54,000 =60,000.\n\n377 +660 = 1,037.\n\nSo total is 61,037. Then adding 364,400:.\n\n61,037 +364,400.\n\n61,000 + 364,400 =425,400.\n\nThen add the remaining 37: 425,400 +37 =425,437. Correct.\n\nHmm, so all methods lead to the same result. So I think the product of 911 and 467 is 425,437.\n\nBut wait, just to be extra sure, let me try multiplying 467 by 911 in another way.\n\nFor instance, using the distributive property:\n\n467 \u00d7911 = 467\u00d7(900 +11) = 467\u00d7900 +467\u00d711.\n\nCompute 467\u00d7900 first:\n\n467\u00d7900 =467\u00d79\u00d7100.\n\n467\u00d79: Let's compute that.\n\n400\u00d79=3,600.\n\n60\u00d79=540.\n\n7\u00d79=63.\n\nTotal: 3,600 +540 =4,140 +63 =4,203. So \u00d7100 gives 420,300.\n\nThen 467\u00d71