od. Let me try the cross-multiplication method.\n\nWait, another way: Let me compute 657 \u00d7 952 as 657*(950 + 2) = 657\u00d7950 + 657\u00d72.\n\nCompute 657\u00d7950: 657\u00d795\u00d710. Let's first compute 657\u00d795.\n\n657\u00d795 can be written as 657*(100 -5) = 657\u00d7100 -657\u00d75 = 65,700 - 3,285 = 62,415.\n\nThen multiply by 10 to get 657\u00d7950: 624,150.\n\nThen add 657\u00d72 = 1,314. So total is 624,150 + 1,314 = 625,464. Again, same result. So this confirms it.\n\nTherefore, I can be confident that the product of 657 and 952 is 625,464.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 657 and 952 is \\boxed{625464}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 657 and 952, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify it with alternative methods.\n\nFirst, we break down the multiplication step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 657 by 2 (units place of 952):**\n   \\[\n   657 \\times 2 = 1314\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 657 by 50 (tens place of 952):**\n   \\[\n   657 \\times 50 = 657 \\times 5 \\times 10 = 3285 \\times 10 = 32850\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 657 by 900 (hundreds place of 952):**\n   \\[\n   657 \\times 900 = 657 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 5913 \\times 100 = 591300\n   \\]\n\nNext, we add the results of these multiplications:\n\\[\n1314 + 32850 + 591300\n\\]\n\nAdding the first two results:\n\\[\n1314 + 32850 = 34164\n\\]\n\nThen adding the third result:\n\\[\n34164 + 591300 = 625464\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we use another method by expanding the numbers:\n\\[\n(600 + 57)(900 + 52) = 600 \\times 900 + 600 \\times 52 + 57 \\times 900 + 57 \\times 52\n\\]\n\\[\n= 540000 + 31200 + 51300 + 2964 = 625464\n\\]\n\nAnother verification using cross-multiplication:\n\\[\n657 \\times 952 = 657 \\times (950 + 2) = 657 \\times 950 + 657 \\times 2\n\\]\n\\[\n= 657 \\times 95 \\times 10 + 1314 = 62415 \\times 10 + 1314 = 624150 + 1314 = 625464\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 657 and 952 is \\(\\boxed{625464}\\).",
