thm steps. Let me go through them again step by step to make sure.\n\nFirst partial product: 283 \u00d74 = 1,132. Correct.\n\nSecond partial product: 283 \u00d790 =283\u00d79\u00d710. 283\u00d79: as before 2,547. So times 10 is 25,470. Correct.\n\nThird partial product: 283 \u00d7800 =226,400. Correct.\n\nAdding them up: 1,132 +25,470 =26,602. Then 26,602 +226,400 =253,002. So that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I can use another multiplication method, like the lattice method, but that might take longer. Alternatively, perhaps use calculator-like step-by-step.\n\nAlternatively, let me compute 283 \u00d7894 directly:\n\n283 \u00d7894.\n\nLet me compute 283 \u00d7800 =226,400.\n\n283 \u00d790 =25,470.\n\n283 \u00d74 =1,132.\n\nAdding them gives 226,400 +25,470 =251,870; then +1,132 would be 253,002. Yes, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do 283 \u00d7894 as (280 +3) \u00d7(800 +90 +4). But that would be more complicated, but let's try expanding it:\n\n(280 +3)(800 +90 +4) =280\u00d7800 +280\u00d790 +280\u00d74 +3\u00d7800 +3\u00d790 +3\u00d74.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n280\u00d7800 =224,000.\n\n280\u00d790 =25,200.\n\n280\u00d74 =1,120.\n\n3\u00d7800=2,400.\n\n3\u00d790=270.\n\n3\u00d74=12.\n\nNow add all these together:\n\n224,000 +25,200 =249,200.\n\n249,200 +1,120 =250,320.\n\n250,320 +2,400 =252,720.\n\n252,720 +270 =252,990.\n\n252,990 +12 =253,002.\n\nSame result! Okay, so that's reassuring. So regardless of the method, the answer is 253,002. Therefore, I think that's correct.\n\nWait, but let me just confirm once more with another approach, maybe breaking down 283 and 894 into smaller components.\n\nAlternatively, let me think of 283 \u00d7894 as (300 -17) \u00d7(900 -6).\n\nExpanding that would give 300\u00d7900 -300\u00d76 -17\u00d7900 +17\u00d76.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n300\u00d7900 =270,000.\n\n-300\u00d76 =-1,800.\n\n-17\u00d7900 =-15,300.\n\n+17\u00d76=+102.\n\nAdding all together: 270,000 -1,800 =268,200.\n\n268,200 -15,300 =252,900.\n\