ts the second method. Wait 82400 +7326:.\n\nBreaking down:\n\n82400\n\n+ 7000 = 89400\n\nThen 89400 + 326 = 89,726. Hmm.\n\nBut according to the second method, using distributive property, I got 889,436. There's a big difference here. So clearly, one of the methods is wrong.\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the second method.\n\nLet me recalculate the second method again:\n\nAlternative approach: 916 \u00d7 971 = 916 \u00d7 (1000 - 29) = 916\u00d71000 - 916\u00d729.\n\nCompute 916\u00d71000 = 916,000.\n\nCompute 916\u00d729:\n\nFirst, 916\u00d730 = 27,480. Then subtract 916 to get 27,480 -916 = ?\n\n27,480 - 900 = 26,580\n\n26,580 - 16 = 26,564.\n\nTherefore, 916\u00d729=26,564.\n\nSo total is 916,000 -26,564 = ?\n\n916,000 -20,000 = 896,000\n\n896,000 -6,564 = 889,436.\n\nHmm, so that's 889,436 vs 89,726. These are two different answers. Clearly, I messed up one of the calculations. Let me check with calculator steps.\n\nAlternatively, let me try the first method again but more carefully.\n\nFirst partial product: 916\u00d71 =916.\n\nSecond partial product: 916\u00d77 (tens place). 7\u00d7916= 6412? Wait, no, wait.\n\nWait 7\u00d7916:\n\nLet me compute 7\u00d7900=6300, 7\u00d716=112. So total 6300+112=6412. Wait, so earlier I thought it was 6410 but actually it's 6412? Wait, that's a mistake here.\n\nWait, let's do it step by step:\n\n7\u00d76=42, write down 2, carryover 4.\n\n7\u00d71=7 plus 4 is 11. Write down 1, carryover 1.\n\n7\u00d79=63 plus 1 is 64. So the result is 6412. Wait, but if the digits are 9 (hundreds place),1 (tens),6 (units). So multiplying by 7:\n\nUnits digit: 7\u00d76=42, so 2, carryover4.\n\nTens digit:7\u00d71=7 plus 4 is 11, so 1, carryover1.\n\nHundreds digit:7\u00d79=63 plus1 is 64. So the partial product is 6412. But since it's the tens place, it should be shifted one to the left, so 64120.\n\nWait, I see now! Earlier, I made a mistake in the partial product for the 7. I thought it was 6410 but actually it's 6412, so shifted becomes 64120. So that's where the error was.\n\nSimilarly, the third partial product: 9\u00d7916.\n\nLet me verify that again.\n\n9\u00d7916: 9\u00d7900=8100, 9\u00d716=144, so 8100+144=8244. So the partial product is 8244, shifted two places (hundreds place) so it becomes 824400.\n\nAh, so I had written 82400 before, but actually it's 824400. That was another mistake.\n\nLet me recast the entire first method with correct partial products.\n\nFirst partial product: 916 \u00d71 = 916.\n\nSecond partial product: 916 \u00d77 (tens) = 6412 shifted left by one \u2192 64120.\n\nThird partial product: 916 \u00d79 (hundreds) =8244 shifted left by two \u2192 824400.\n\nNow adding them all together:\n\nFirst: 916\n\nSecond: 64,120\n\nThird:824,400\n\nNow adding:\n\nStart with 916 + 64,120 = 65,036.\n\nThen add 824,400 to that:\n\n65,036 + 824,400 = 889,436.\n\nAh, that matches the second method's result of 889,436. So my initial mistake was in the partial products' values and shifts. The key errors were:\n\n1. For the second partial product (multiplying by 7), I incorrectly calculated it as 6410 instead of 6412, leading to an undercount.\n\n2. For the third partial product (multiplying by 9), I wrote 82400 instead of 824400 because I probably miscalculated 9\u00d7916 as 824 instead of 8244.\n\nSo the correct total is 889,436.\n\nLet me try another verification approach. Let's compute 916 \u00d7 971 step by step using another method, like breaking down the numbers:\n\n916 \u00d7 971.\n\nWe can write this as (900 + 16) \u00d7 (900 + 71).\n\nUsing the distributive property (FOIL method):\n\n= 900\u00d7900 + 900\u00d771 + 16\u00d7900 + 16\u00d771.\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n900\u00d7900 = 810,000.\n\n900\u00d771 = 900\u00d770 + 900\u00d71 = 63,000 + 900 = 63,900.\n\n16\u00d7900 = 14,400.\n\n16\u00d771 = 1,136.\n\nNow add all together:\n\n810,000 + 63,900 = 873,900.\n\n873,900 +14,400 = 888,300.\n\n888,300 +1,136 = 889,436.\n\nSame result! So that confirms the correct answer is 889,436.\n\nTherefore, the initial mistake was due to miscalculations in the partial products during the first attempt. It's easy to make arithmetic errors when doing multiplication manually, so checking with alternative methods is crucial.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the standard algorithm again but more carefully:\n\nMultiply 916 by 971:\n\nStart with 916 \u00d7 1 (units): 916.\n\nThen 916 \u00d77 (tens):\n\n7\u00d76=42, write 2, carryover4.\n\n7\u00d71=7+4=11, write 1, carryover1.\n\n7\u00d79=63+1=64, so 6412. Then shifted left by one: 64,120.\n\nThen 916 \u00d79 (hundreds):\n\n9\u00d76=54, write 4, carryover5.\n\n9\u00d71=9+5=14, write4, carryover1.\n\n9\u00d79=81+1=82, so 8244. Shifted left by two: 824,400.\n\nAdding:\n\n916 + 64,120 = 65,036.\n\n65,036 +824,400 = 889,436.\n\nYes, that works.\n\nTherefore, the product of 916 and 971 is 889,436.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 916 and 971 is \\boxed{889436}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 916 and 971, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify with alternative methods.\n\nFirst, we write the numbers vertically and multiply step by step:\n\n```\n    916\n\u00d7  971\n--------\n```\n\n1. **Multiply by the units digit (1):**\n   \\[\n   1 \\times 916 = 916\n   \\]\n   This gives the first partial product: 916.\n\n2. **Multiply by the tens digit (7), shifted one place to the left:**\n   \\[\n   7 \\times 916 = 6412 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by one, becomes 64120)}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply by the hundreds digit (9), shifted two places to the left:**\n   \\[\n   9 \\times 916 = 8244 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by two, becomes 824400)}\n   \\]\n\nNext, we add all the partial products together:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n916 & \\\\\n+ 64120 & \\quad \\text{(second partial product)} \\\\\n+ 824400 & \\quad \\text{(third partial product)} \\\\\n\\hline\n916 + 64120 &= 65036, \\\\\n65036 + 824400 &= 889436.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we use the distributive property:\n\\[\n916 \\times 971 = 916 \\times (900 + 71) = 916 \\times 900 + 916 \\times 71\n\\]\nBreaking it down:\n\\[\n916 \\times 900 = 824400, \\quad 916 \\times 71 = 65036\n\\]\nAdding these results:\n\\[\n824400 + 65036 = 889436\n\\]\n\nAnother verification using the distributive property with different breakdown:\n\\[\n(900 + 16) \\times (900 + 71) = 900 \\times 900 + 900 \\times 71 + 16 \\times 900 + 16 \\times 71\n\\]\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n900 \\times 900 = 810000, \\quad 900 \\times 71 = 63900, \\quad 16 \\times 900 = 14400, \\quad 16 \\times 71 = 1136\n\\]\nAdding these together:\n\\[\n810000 + 63900 + 14400 + 1136 = 889436\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 916 and 971 is \\boxed{889436}.",
