      "text": "1687 + 168700 = 170,387? Wait, wait, let me add step by step. 168700 + 1687.\n\nBreaking it down: 168,700 + 1,000 = 169,700; then add 687 more: 169,700 + 687 = 170,387. Hmm, but wait, that seems correct?\n\nWait, let me check that addition again:\n\n168700  \n+\u00a0\u00a01687  \n= ?\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n0 +7 =7  \n0 +8=8  \n7 +6=13, so write 3, carryover 1  \n6 (from 168700's thousands place) plus 1 (carryover) is 7, then add 1 (from 1687's thousands place?) Wait, perhaps it's clearer:\n\n168700 is 1 6 8 7 0 0  \nAdding 0 0 1 6 8 7\n\nWait, aligning:\n\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0168700  \n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0+\u00a0\u00a01687  \n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0=\u00a0?\n\nLet me write them aligned by digits:\n\nHundred thousands: 1 (from 168700)  \nTen thousands: 6  \nThousands: 8  \nHundreds:7  \nTens:0  \nUnits:0\n\nAdding to:\n\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0Thousands:1 (since 1687 is 1 thousand, 6 hundreds, 8 tens, 7 units)\n\nWait, maybe better written as:\n\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0168700  \n+\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a01687  \n=\u00a0?\n\nAdding the units: 0 +7=7  \nTens place:0 +8=8  \nHundreds place:7 +6=13, so write 3, carryover 1  \nThousands place:8 +1 +1 (carryover) = 10, so write 0, carryover 1  \nTen-thousands place:6 +0 +1 (carryover) =7  \nHundred-thousands place:1 remains.\n\nSo putting it together: 1 (hundred thousand), 7 (ten thousand), 0 (thousand), 3 (hundred), 8 (ten), 7 (unit). So 170,387.\n\nHmm, so total is 170,387. Wait, but let me check with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the distributive property: 241 \u00d7 707 = 241 \u00d7 (700 +7) = 241\u00d7700 +241\u00d77.\n\nCompute each part:\n\n241 \u00d7700: 241 \u00d77 \u00d7100. We know 241\u00d77 is 1687, so 1687 \u00d7100 = 168,700.\n\n241\u00d77 = 1,687 as before.\n\nAdding those together: 168,700 +1,687 = 170,387. Same result. So that's good.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do 241 \u00d7707 using another method, like breaking down the numbers more.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps using the standard multiplication as I did first, so let's verify that again.\n\nWait, when I did the original multiplication:\n\n241  \n\u00d7707  \n________\n\nFirst line: 241 \u00d77 =1687  \nSecond line: 241 \u00d70 (tens place) shifted one, so 0  \nThird line: 241 \u00d77 (hundreds place) shifted two, so 241 \u00d77 \u00d7100 =168,700.  \nAdding them gives 1687 +0 +168,700 =170,387. That seems consistent.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I should check with another approach, like the lattice method or some other, but maybe that's overkill. Alternatively, compute 241 \u00d7700 = 168,700, then add 241\u00d77=1,687, so total 168,700 +1,687 =170,387. Yes, that's the same as before. \n\nAlternatively, perhaps use estimation to check if the answer is reasonable. 240 \u00d7700 =168,000. Then 240\u00d77=1,680, so total would be 168,000 +1,680 =169,680. But since we have 241 instead of 240, so adding 1\u00d7707, which is 707, so total would be 169,680 +707 =170,387. Exactly! So that cross-verification works. \n\nTherefore, I think 170,387 is the correct answer. Wait, but let me check once more with actual calculator steps.\n\nAlternatively, let me compute 241 \u00d7707 step by step again.\n\n241 \u00d7707:\n\nBreaking down 707 into 700 +7, as above.\n\nFirst part: 241\u00d7700:\n\n241 \u00d77 =1,687. Then \u00d7100 \u2192168,700.\n\nSecond part:241 \u00d77 =1,687.\n\nAdding together: 168,700 +1,687.\n\n168,700 + 1,000 =169,700.\n\n169,700 +687 =170,387. \n\nYes, that's the same as before. So I think that's correct. Therefore, the product of 241 and 707 is 170,387.\n\nWait a second, but let me just do straight multiplication digit by digit again to ensure no step was missed.\n\nMultiplying 241 by 707:\n\nStart with 7 (units) \u00d7241:\n\n7\u00d71=7, 7\u00d74=28 (write 8, carryover 2), 7\u00d72=14 +2=16. So 1687. Correct.\n\nThen 0 (tens place) \u00d7241 =0, shifted one to the left, so 0000 but actually 0 shifted left once is 0.\n\nThen 7 (hundreds place) \u00d7241, shifted two places (so effectively \u00d7700). So 7\u00d7241 again is 1687, but shifted two places: 168700.\n\nAdding 1687 + 0 +168700 gives 170,387. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can multiply 241 \u00d7707 as (200 +40 +1) \u00d7 (700 +7). Let's see:\n\nExpand using distributive property:\n\n200\u00d7700 +200\u00d77 +40\u00d7700 +40\u00d77 +1\u00d7700 +1\u00d77.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n200\u00d7700 =140,000\n\n200\u00d77 =1,400\n\n40\u00d7700 =28,000\n\n40\u00d77 =280\n\n1\u00d7700 =700\n\n1\u00d77 =7\n\nNow add all these together:\n\n140,000 +1,400 =141,400\n\n141,400 +28,000 =169,400\n\n169,400 +280 =169,680\n\n169,680 +700 =170,380\n\n170,380 +7 =170,387.\n\nSame answer again. So this method also gives 170,387. Therefore, I'm pretty confident that's the correct product.\n\nJust to be absolutely thorough, let me try another approach. Let me compute 707 \u00d7200 +707\u00d740 +707\u00d71.\n\n707\u00d7200: 707\u00d72=1,414; \u00d7100=141,400.\n\n707\u00d740: 707\u00d74=2,828; \u00d710=28,280.\n\n707\u00d71=707.\n\nAdding them together: 141,400 +28,280 =169,680; then +707 is 170,387. Yep, same result.\n\nAlright, so all methods cross-verify that the product is 170,387. I think that's solid. No mistakes detected in my calculations. Therefore, the answer should be 170,387.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 241 and 707 is \\boxed{170387}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 241 and 707, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify with different methods.\n\nFirst, we break down the multiplication step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 241 by 7 (units place of 707):**\n   \\[\n   241 \\times 7 = 1687\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 241 by 0 (tens place of 707):**\n   \\[\n   241 \\times 0 = 0 \\quad \\text{(shifted one position to the left)}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 241 by 7 (hundreds place of 707):**\n   \\[\n   241 \\times 7 = 1687 \\quad \\text{(shifted two positions to the left, resulting in 168700)}\n   \\]\n\nAdding the partial products together:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   1687 \\\\\n+   0 \\\\\n+168700 \\\\\n\\hline\n  170387 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nWe can also verify using the distributive property:\n\\[\n241 \\times 707 = 241 \\times (700 + 7) = 241 \\times 700 + 241 \\times 7\n\\]\n\\[\n241 \\times 700 = 168700 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 241 \\times 7 = 1687\n\\]\n\\[\n168700 + 1687 = 170387\n\\]\n\nAnother verification using expanded form:\n\\[\n(200 + 40 + 1) \\times (700 + 7) = 200 \\times 700 + 200 \\times 7 + 40 \\times 700 + 40 \\times 7 + 1 \\times 700 + 1 \\times 7\n\\]\n\\[\n= 140000 + 1400 + 28000 + 280 + 700 + 7 = 170387\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 241 and 707 is \\(\\boxed{170387}\\).",
