n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 982 and 783 is \\boxed{768906}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 982 and 783, we use the distributive property by breaking down the multiplication step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 982 by 3 (ones place):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   982 \\times 3 &= 2946 \\\\\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 982 by 80 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   982 \\times 80 &= 78560 \\\\\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 982 by 700 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   982 \\times 700 &= 687400 \\\\\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   2946 + 78560 + 687400 &= 2946 + 78560 = 81506 \\\\\n   81506 + 687400 &= 768906 \\\\\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n\nWe verified the result using different methods (distributive property with expanded terms, and the algebraic identity \\((1000 - 18)(800 - 17)\\)), all leading to the same result.\n\nThe product of 982 and 783 is \\(\\boxed{768906}\\).",
