lying 674 by 999.\n\nFirst, write 674  \n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0999  \n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00d7______  \nBut actually, multiplying 674 \u00d7 999 can be done by multiplying 674 \u00d7 9 \u00d7 100 + 674 \u00d7 9 \u00d7 10 + ... Hmm, maybe that's more complicated.\n\nAlternatively, standard multiplication:\n\n674  \n\u00d7 999  \n________\n\nLet me break it down step by step.\n\nFirst, multiply 674 by 9 (the units digit of 999):\n\n674 \u00d7 9 = 6,066\n\nThen multiply 674 by 90 (the tens digit):\n\n674 \u00d7 90 = 60,660\n\nThen multiply 674 by 900 (the hundreds digit):\n\n674 \u00d7 900 = 606,600\n\nWait, but actually, the standard multiplication would be:\n\nWait, 999 has digits 9, 9, 9 in units, tens, hundreds. So actually, multiplying by each digit:\n\nFirst step: 674 \u00d7 9 (units place) = 6,066\n\nSecond step: 674 \u00d7 9 (tens place) shifted one position to the left: 6,066 \u00d7 10 = 60,660\n\nThird step: 674 \u00d7 9 (hundreds place) shifted two positions to the left: 6,066 \u00d7 100 = 606,600\n\nThen add them all up:\n\n6,066  \n60,660  \n606,600  \n________  \nAdding these together:\n\nStart with 6,066 + 60,660 = 66,726\n\nThen add 606,600 + 66,726: 606,600 + 60,000 = 666,600; 666,600 + 6,726 = 673,326. \n\nSo that's the same result as before. Therefore, 674 \u00d7 999 = 673,326. \n\nHmm, so that seems to check out. So maybe my initial subtraction method was correct. Let me just confirm with another approach. \n\nAlternatively, perhaps using the identity that a \u00d7 (b - c) = a\u00d7b - a\u00d7c. Which is exactly what I did first. So that gives me confidence. \n\nAlternatively, let me use a calculator-style approach step by step:\n\nCompute 674 \u00d7 999:\n\nFirst, note that 674 \u00d7 1000 = 674,000. Then subtract 674 once: 674,000 - 674. \n\nCalculating 674,000 minus 674:\n\n674,000 minus 600 is 673,400. Then subtract 74 more: 673,400 - 74 = 673,326. So that matches.\n\nTherefore, I think the correct answer is 673,326. \n\nBut just to be thorough, let me verify using another method. Let's use the standard algorithm for multiplication:\n\nMultiply 674 by 999.\n\nStart by writing 674  \n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0999  \n_________\n\nMultiplying 674 by the units digit (9):\n\n674 \u00d7 9 = 6,066\n\nThen multiply by the tens digit (9), shifted one position left:\n\n674 \u00d7 9 = 6,066, so shifted left one is 60,660\n\nThen multiply by the hundreds digit (9), shifted two positions left:\n\n674 \u00d7 9 = 6,066, shifted two becomes 606,600\n\nNow add them up:\n\n6,066  \n60,660  \n606,600  \n________  \nAdding the thousands:\n\n6,066 + 60,660 = 66,726\n\n66,726 + 606,600 = 673,326. \n\nSame result again. So that's consistent. \n\nAlternatively, perhaps I can check using another mathematical trick. Let me see.\n\nAlternatively, think of 999 as 1000 - 1, so when I multiply 674 by that, it's 674 less than 674,000, which is exactly what I did before, and that gives 673,326. \n\nAlternatively, maybe breaking down 674 into 600 + 70 +4 and multiply each by 999:\n\n(600 + 70 +4) \u00d7 999 = 600\u00d7999 + 70\u00d7999 +4\u00d7999\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n600\u00d7999 = 600\u00d7(1000 -1) = 600,000 - 600 = 599,400\n\n70\u00d7999 = 70\u00d71000 -70\u00d71 = 70,000 -70 = 69,930\n\n4\u00d7999 = 4\u00d71000 -4\u00d71 = 4,000 -4 = 3,996\n\nNow add them all together:\n\n599,400 + 69,930 = 669,330\n\nThen add 3,996: 669,330 + 3,996 = 673,326. \n\nSame result again. \n\nTherefore, all methods point to the same answer, so I think it's safe to conclude that 674 multiplied by 999 is 673,326. \n\nJust to be absolutely sure, maybe plug in approximate values. Let's see, 674 \u00d7 1000 is 674,000, so subtracting 674 gives 673,326. Since 674 is about 700, so 700\u00d71000 is 700,000, so subtract 700, so 699,300. But since 674 is less than 700, the actual result should be a bit higher than that. Wait, maybe that's not the best way. Alternatively, approximate:\n\n674 \u00d7 1000 = 674,000. Subtract 674, so it's 674,000 minus 674, which is clearly 673,326. \n\nAlternatively, if I think of 674 \u00d7 999 as (600 +74) \u00d7 999, but that might complicate. \n\nAlternatively, maybe check with smaller numbers. Let's see, if I do 10 \u00d7 99 = 990, which is 10\u00d7100 -10. That works. So the method works there. Therefore, the same principle applies here. \n\nTherefore, I think my answer is correct. The product of 674 and 999 is 673,326.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 674 and 999 is \\boxed{673326}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 674 and 999, we can use the distributive property by recognizing that 999 is 1000 - 1. \n\nFirst, we calculate:\n\\[\n674 \\times 1000 = 674000\n\\]\n\nNext, we subtract 674 from this result:\n\\[\n674000 - 674\n\\]\n\nBreaking down the subtraction:\n\\[\n674000 - 600 = 673400\n\\]\n\\[\n673400 - 74 = 673326\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n- Multiply 674 by 9 (units place): \\(674 \\times 9 = 6066\\)\n- Multiply 674 by 90 (tens place): \\(674 \\times 90 = 60660\\)\n- Multiply 674 by 900 (hundreds place): \\(674 \\times 900 = 606600\\)\n\nAdding these results together:\n\\[\n6066 + 60660 + 606600 = 673326\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 674 and 999 is \\(\\boxed{673326}\\).",
