g:\n\nFirst, 500\u00d7800 =400,000  \n500\u00d740 =20,000  \n500\u00d73 =1,500  \n32\u00d7800 =25,600  \n32\u00d740 =1,280  \n32\u00d73 =96  \n\nNow add all these:\n\n400,000 +20,000 +1,500 +25,600 +1,280 +96.\n\nLet's compute step by step:\n\nStart with 400,000  \nAdd 20,000 \u2192 420,000  \nAdd 1,500 \u2192 421,500  \nAdd 25,600 \u2192 447,100  \nAdd 1,280 \u2192 448,380  \nAdd 96 \u2192 448,476. \n\nOh! That's the same result as before. So that cross-verification works. So that's good. Therefore, the product is indeed 448,476.\n\nI think that's solid. Therefore, the answer should be 448,476.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 532 and 843 is \\boxed{448476}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 532 and 843, we use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 532 by 3 (units place of 843):**\n   \\[\n   532 \\times 3 = 1596\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 532 by 40 (tens place of 843):**\n   \\[\n   532 \\times 40 = 21280\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 532 by 800 (hundreds place of 843):**\n   \\[\n   532 \\times 800 = 425600\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   1596 + 21280 + 425600\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add 1596 and 21280:\n     \\[\n     1596 + 21280 = 22876\n     \\]\n\n   - Then add the result to 425600:\n     \\[\n     22876 + 425600 = 448476\n     \\]\n\nTo verify, we can use the distributive property:\n\\[\n532 \\times 843 = 532 \\times (800 + 40 + 3) = (532 \\times 800) + (532 \\times 40) + (532 \\times 3)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 425600 + 21280 + 1596 = 448476\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the result is consistent. Therefore, the product of 532 and 843 is \\(\\boxed{448476}\\).",
