n terms of 160*165 + 4*165. 160*165: 160*100=16,000; 160*60=9,600; 160*5=800. So 16,000+9,600=25,600 +800=26,400. Then 4*165=660. So 26,400 +660=27,060. Same answer. \n\nAlright, so after multiple methods, I keep getting 27,060. So I think that's the right answer. Maybe I can check with a calculator, but since I don't have one, but all the manual calculations agree, I can be confident.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 164 and 165 is \\boxed{27060}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 164 and 165, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy:\n\n1. **Standard Multiplication:**\n   - Multiply 164 by 5: \n     \\[\n     164 \\times 5 = 820\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 164 by 60 (shifted one position to the left):\n     \\[\n     164 \\times 60 = 9840\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 164 by 100 (shifted two positions to the left):\n     \\[\n     164 \\times 100 = 16400\n     \\]\n   - Add the results together:\n     \\[\n     820 + 9840 + 16400 = 27060\n     \\]\n\n2. **Using Consecutive Numbers (n(n+1)):**\n   - Calculate \\(164^2 + 164\\):\n     \\[\n     164^2 = 26896\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     26896 + 164 = 27060\n     \\]\n\n3. **Distributive Property:**\n   - Break down 165 into 160 + 5:\n     \\[\n     164 \\times 160 = 26240\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     164 \\times 5 = 820\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     26240 + 820 = 27060\n     \\]\n\nAll methods consistently yield the same result. Therefore, the product of 164 and 165 is \\(\\boxed{27060}\\).",
