ust to be thorough. Maybe using another breakdown. For instance, 886 * 645. Maybe using (900 - 14) * 645. Hmm, 900*645 minus 14*645. Let's see if that works.\n\nFirst, 900*645. 9*645 is 5,805, so 900*645 is 580,500. \n\nThen 14*645. Let's compute that. 10*645 is 6,450, and 4*645 is 2,580. Adding them gives 6,450 + 2,580 = 9,030. \n\nSo subtracting: 580,500 - 9,030 = 571,470. \n\nSame answer again. Hmm, that seems consistent. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use the distributive property in another way. Let me try (800 + 80 + 6)*(600 + 40 +5). But that would be more complicated because it would involve multiplying each term, but just to check:\n\nExpanding the product:\n\n800*600 + 800*40 + 800*5 + 80*600 + 80*40 + 80*5 + 6*600 + 6*40 +6*5.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n800*600 = 480,000\n\n800*40 = 32,000\n\n800*5 = 4,000\n\n80*600 = 48,000\n\n80*40 = 3,200\n\n80*5 = 400\n\n6*600 = 3,600\n\n6*40 = 240\n\n6*5 = 30\n\nNow add all these up:\n\nStart with the largest terms:\n\n480,000\n\n+32,000 = 512,000\n\n+4,000 = 516,000\n\n+48,000 = 564,000\n\n+3,200 = 567,200\n\n+400 = 567,600\n\n+3,600 = 571,200\n\n+240 = 571,440\n\n+30 = 571,470.\n\nWow, that's the same answer again. So that's four different methods all leading to 571,470. \n\nTherefore, I think the product of 886 and 645 is 571,470. \n\nBut just to make sure, maybe use a calculator? Hmm, since I can't use an actual calculator, perhaps approximate the numbers to check if it's reasonable. \n\nApproximating 886 to 900 and 645 to 600, so 900*600 = 540,000. Since both numbers are approximated down, the actual product should be higher. 571,470 is indeed higher than 540,000, so that makes sense. \n\nAlternatively, 886 is 14 less than 900, so 14*645 is 9,030. So subtracting that from 900*645 gives 571,470. Which we did earlier, so that's consistent. \n\nAlternatively, 645 is 5 less than 650. So 886*650 would be 886*(600+50) = 886*600 +886*50. \n\nWait, but maybe that's more steps. Alternatively, 886*645 = 886*(650 -5) = 886*650