00 =336,700; minus (2,000 +72)=2,072 \u2192 336,700 -2,072 = 334,628. Exactly the same as the actual result. That's a perfect check. So that gives me more confidence.\n\nTherefore, the product of 646 and 518 is 334,628.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 646 and 518 is \\boxed{334628}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 646 and 518, we can use the standard algorithm for multiplication. Here are the key steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 646 by 8 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   646 \\times 8 = 5168\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 646 by 1 (tens place) and shift one position to the left:**\n   \\[\n   646 \\times 1 = 646 \\quad \\text{(shifted one position left)} \\quad \\Rightarrow 6460\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 646 by 5 (hundreds place) and shift two positions to the left:**\n   \\[\n   646 \\times 5 = 3230 \\quad \\text{(shifted two positions left)} \\quad \\Rightarrow 323000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   5168 \\\\\n   + \\quad 6460 \\\\\n   + 323000 \\\\\n   \\hline\n   334628\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 646 and 518 is \\(\\boxed{334628}\\).",
