ng this manually, I think the answer is correct. Let me just check one more time.\n\nAlternatively, I can reverse the multiplication: 406 \u00d7809.\n\n406 \u00d79 = 3,654\n\n406 \u00d70 (tens) =0 shifted one.\n\n406 \u00d78 (hundreds place) = 406\u00d78=3,248 shifted two places: 324,800.\n\nAdding 3,654 + 0 +324,800 =328,454. Same answer. So that's a good check.\n\nTherefore, I can be confident that the product of 809 and 406 is 328,454.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 809 and 406 is \\boxed{328454}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 809 and 406, we use the standard multiplication method:\n\n1. **Multiply 809 by 6 (units place of 406):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     809 \\\\\n   \\times \\;\\, 6 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     4854 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   Result: 4854\n\n2. **Multiply 809 by 0 (tens place of 406):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     809 \\\\\n   \\times \\;\\, 0 \\\\\n   \\hline\n       0 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   This result is 0, but shifted one place to the left, so it remains 0.\n\n3. **Multiply 809 by 4 (hundreds place of 406) and shift two places to the left:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     809 \\\\\n   \\times \\;\\, 4 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     3236 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   Shifting two places to the left gives 323600.\n\n4. **Add all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     323600 \\\\\n   + \\;\\, 4854 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     328454 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 809 and 406 is \\(\\boxed{328454}\\).",
