orithm and verify it with different methods.\n\nFirst, we break down the multiplication step by step:\n\n1. Multiply 349 by 1 (units place of 511):\n   \\[\n   349 \\times 1 = 349\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 349 by 10 (tens place of 511):\n   \\[\n   349 \\times 10 = 3490\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 349 by 500 (hundreds place of 511):\n   \\[\n   349 \\times 500 = 174500\n   \\]\n\nNext, we add the partial products together:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n      349 \\\\\n    + 3490 \\\\\n+ 174500 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nAdding these step by step:\n- First, add \\(349 + 3490\\):\n  \\[\n  349 + 3490 = 3839\n  \\]\n- Then add the result to \\(174500\\):\n  \\[\n  3839 + 174500 = 178339\n  \\]\n\nTo verify, we use the difference of squares method:\n- Let \\(a = 349\\) and \\(b = 511\\):\n  \\[\n  349 \\times 511 = \\left( \\frac{349 + 511}{2} \\right)^2 - \\left( \\frac{511 - 349}{2} \\right)^2\n  \\]\n- Calculate the terms:\n  \\[\n  \\frac{349 + 511}{2} = 430 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\frac{511 - 349}{2} = 81\n  \\]\n- Compute the squares and subtract:\n  \\[\n  430^2 - 81^2 = 184900 - 6561 = 178339\n  \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the product is \\(\\boxed{178339}\\).",
