messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 217 and 729?', "<think>Okay, let's see, I need to find the product of 217 and 729. Hmm, multiplication, right? Alright, so 217 times 729. I guess I can do this step by step. Maybe break it down into smaller parts to make it easier. Let me think.. .\n\nFirst, I remember that multiplying larger numbers can be done by breaking them into smaller components. Like, maybe using the distributive property. So, 217 times 729. Let me write this out as 217 × 729. .\n\nWait, maybe I can split 729 into 700 + 29? That might make it easier. So then, 217 × (700 + 29) = 217×700 + 217×29. Yeah, that should work. Let me calculate each part separately.\n\nStarting with 217 × 700. Hmm, 217 multiplied by 700. Since 700 is 7 × 100, maybe I can do 217 × 7 first and then multiply by 100. Let's see, 217 × 7. Let me compute that. .\n\n200 × 7 is 1400, and 17 × 7 is 119. Adding those together: 1400 + 119 = 1519. So 217 × 7 = 1519. Then multiplying by 100 gives 151,900. Okay, so that part is 151,900.\n\nNow the second part: 217 × 29. Hmm, that might be a bit trickier. Let me see. Maybe break down 29 into 30 - 1? So, 217 × (30 - 1) = 217×30 - 217×1. .\n\nCalculating 217 × 30: Well, 217 × 3 is 651, so times 10 would be 6,510. Then subtract 217 × 1, which is just 217. So, 6,510 - 217. Let me do that subtraction: 6,510 minus 200 is 6,310, then minus 17 more is 6,293. Wait, is that right? Let me check again. 6,510 minus 217. 6,510 - 200 is 6,310, then subtract 17: 6,310 - 10 is 6,300, minus 7 more is 6,293. Yeah, that seems correct.\n\nSo the second part is 6,293. .\n\nNow, adding the two parts together: 151,900 + 6,293. Let's see. 151,900 + 6,000 is 157,900. Then add the remaining 293: 157,900 + 293 = 160,193? Wait, hold on, that doesn't seem right. Wait, 151,900 + 6,293. Let me do it step by step. .\n\n151,900  .\n+\xa0\xa06,293  .\n=?.\n\nAdding the thousands: 151,000 + 6,000 = 157,000.  .\nThen the hundreds: 900 + 293.