. Then 6293 +151900.\n\nLet's add 151,900 + 6,293:\n\n151,900 +6,000 =157,900. Then add 293: 157,900 +293 =158,193. Yep, same answer.\n\nAlright, so after multiple methods and cross-verification, I'm confident that the product of 217 and 729 is 158,193. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, and all methods converge to the same result. So I think that's the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 217 and 729 is \\boxed{158193}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 217 and 729, we can use the distributive property and break down the multiplication into smaller, manageable parts.\n\nFirst, we split 729 into 700 and 29:\n\\[\n217 \\times 729 = 217 \\times (700 + 29) = 217 \\times 700 + 217 \\times 29\n\\]\n\nCalculating each part separately:\n\n1. **Calculating \\(217 \\times 700\\):**\n   \\[\n   217 \\times 700 = 217 \\times 7 \\times 100\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   217 \\times 7 = 1519 \\quad \\text{(since } 200 \\times 7 = 1400 \\text{ and } 17 \\times 7 = 119, \\text{ so } 1400 + 119 = 1519\\text{)}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1519 \\times 100 = 151900\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculating \\(217 \\times 29\\):**\n   \\[\n   217 \\times 29 = 217 \\times (30 - 1) = 217 \\times 30 - 217 \\times 1\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   217 \\times 30 = 6510 \\quad \\text{(since } 217 \\times 3 = 651 \\text{ and } 651 \\times 10 = 6510\\text{)}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   6510 - 217 = 6293\n   \\]\n\nAdding the two results together:\n\\[\n151900 + 6293 = 158193\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can also use the standard multiplication method:\n- Multiply 217 by 9 (units place): \\(217 \\times 9 = 1953\\)\n- Multiply 217 by 20 (tens place): \\(217 \\times 20 = 4340\\)\n- Multiply 217 by 700 (hundreds place): \\(217 \\times 700 = 151900\\)\n\nAdding these partial products:\n\\[\n1953 + 4340 + 151900 = 158193\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 217 and 729 is \\(\\boxed{158193}\\).",
