reaking down 775 into 700 + 70 + 5. We then multiply each part separately and sum the results.\n\n1. Calculate \\(428 \\times 700\\):\n   \\[\n   428 \\times 700 = 428 \\times 7 \\times 100 = 2996 \\times 100 = 299600\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\(428 \\times 70\\):\n   \\[\n   428 \\times 70 = 428 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 2996 \\times 10 = 29960\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate \\(428 \\times 5\\):\n   \\[\n   428 \\times 5 = (400 \\times 5) + (28 \\times 5) = 2000 + 140 = 2140\n   \\]\n\n4. Sum the results of the three calculations:\n   \\[\n   299600 + 29960 + 2140\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add \\(299600\\) and \\(29960\\):\n     \\[\n     299600 + 29960 = 329560\n     \\]\n\n   - Then add the result to \\(2140\\):\n     \\[\n     329560 + 2140 = 331700\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 428 and 775 is \\(\\boxed{331700}\\).",
