). 600\u00d7144 is 86,400. 20\u00d7144 is 2,880. 86,400 minus 2,880 is 83,520. Perfect. So that's consistent as well.\n\nAlright, I think that's solid. I can't find any errors here, and all different methods give the same result. So I'm confident that the product of 580 and 144 is 83,520.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 580 and 144 is \\boxed{83520}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 580 and 144, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy:\n\n1. **Breaking down 144 into 100 + 40 + 4:**\n   - \\(580 \\times 100 = 58,000\\)\n   - \\(580 \\times 40 = 23,200\\)\n   - \\(580 \\times 4 = 2,320\\)\n   - Adding these results: \\(58,000 + 23,200 + 2,320 = 83,520\\)\n\n2. **Using the standard algorithm:**\n   - Multiply 580 by 4: \\(580 \\times 4 = 2,320\\)\n   - Multiply 580 by 40: \\(580 \\times 40 = 23,200\\)\n   - Multiply 580 by 100: \\(580 \\times 100 = 58,000\\)\n   - Adding these results: \\(2,320 + 23,200 + 58,000 = 83,520\\)\n\n3. **Breaking down 580 into 500 + 80:**\n   - \\(500 \\times 144 = 72,000\\)\n   - \\(80 \\times 144 = 11,520\\)\n   - Adding these results: \\(72,000 + 11,520 = 83,520\\)\n\n4. **Using the distributive property with 580 as \\(600 - 20\\):**\n   - \\(600 \\times 144 = 86,400\\)\n   - \\(20 \\times 144 = 2,880\\)\n   - Subtracting these results: \\(86,400 - 2,880 = 83,520\\)\n\nAll methods consistently yield the same result. Therefore, the product of 580 and 144 is \\(\\boxed{83520}\\).",
