but 172 is 100 +70 +2, so:\n\n979\u00d72 =1,958.\n\n979\u00d770=68,530.\n\n979\u00d7100=97,900.\n\nAdding all three: 1,958 +68,530 +97,900.\n\nFirst add 1,958 +68,530 =70,488.\n\nThen 70,488 +97,900 =168,388. Same result again. Okay, so this confirms it again.\n\nTherefore, I can be confident the answer is 168,388.\n\nWait, but let me just do it once more in another way to be absolutely sure. Let me use another method.\n\nLet me compute 172 \u00d7979:\n\nLet me compute 170\u00d7979 + 2\u00d7979.\n\nFirst, 170\u00d7979:\n\nCompute 100\u00d7979 =97,900.\n\n70\u00d7979: 70\u00d7900=63,000; 70\u00d779=5,530. So 63,000+5,530=68,530.\n\nSo 170\u00d7979 =97,900 +68,530=166,430.\n\nThen 2\u00d7979=1,958.\n\nAdding those together:166,430 +1,958 =168,388. Same answer again.\n\nHmm, so after multiple methods, all leading to 168,388, I think that must be correct.\n\nTherefore, the product of 172 and 979 is 168,388.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 172 and 979 is \\boxed{168388}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 172 and 979, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify with alternative methods.\n\nFirst, we break down the multiplication step-by-step:\n\n1. **Multiply 172 by 9 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   172 \\times 9 = 1548\n   \\]\n   Partial product: 1548\n\n2. **Multiply 172 by 70 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   172 \\times 70 = 12040\n   \\]\n   Partial product: 12040\n\n3. **Multiply 172 by 900 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   172 \\times 900 = 154800\n   \\]\n   Partial product: 154800\n\nNext, we sum all the partial products:\n\\[\n1548 + 12040 + 154800\n\\]\n\nAdding the first two partial products:\n\\[\n1548 + 12040 = 13588\n\\]\n\nAdding the result to the third partial product:\n\\[\n13588 + 154800 = 168388\n\\]\n\nVerification using alternative methods:\n- **Using distributive property with 979 = 1000 - 21:**\n  \\[\n  172 \\times (1000 - 21) = 172000 - 3612 = 168388\n  \\]\n\n- **Breaking down 172 into 170 + 2:**\n  \\[\n  170 \\times 979 + 2 \\times