o that's correct. Therefore, the answer is 219,926. So both methods agree. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 322 and 683 is 219,926.\n\nJust to recap, the steps using the standard algorithm were:\n\n1. Multiply 322 by 3 (units place) to get 966.\n\n2. Multiply 322 by 8 (tens place) to get 2,576, then shift left one position to get 25,760.\n\n3. Multiply 322 by 6 (hundreds place) to get 1,932, then shift left two positions to get 193,200.\n\n4. Add all three partial products: 966 +25,760 +193,200 =219,926.\n\nAnd cross-verified using the distributive method, breaking down both numbers into hundreds, tens, and units, which also gave the same result.\n\nTherefore, the final answer should be 219,926.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 322 and 683 is \\boxed{219926}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 322 and 683, we use the standard algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 322 by 3 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   322 \\times 3 = 966\n   \\]\n   The first partial product is 966.\n\n2. **Multiply 322 by 8 (tens place) and shift one position left:**\n   \\[\n   322 \\times 8 = 2576\n   \\]\n   Shifting one position left gives 25,760.\n\n3. **Multiply 322 by 6 (hundreds place) and shift two positions left:**\n   \\[\n   322 \\times 6 = 1932\n   \\]\n   Shifting two positions left gives 193,200.\n\n4. **Add all partial products:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     966 \\\\\n   + 25760 \\\\\n   +193200 \\\\\n   \\hline\n   219926 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\nTo verify, we use the distributive property:\n- Break down both numbers into hundreds, tens, and units:\n  \\[\n  322 = 300 + 20 + 2 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 683 = 600 + 80 + 3\n  \\]\n- Multiply each term and sum the results:\n  \\[\n  \\begin{aligned}\n  300 \\times 600 &= 180000, \\\\\n  300 \\times 80 &= 24000, \\\\\n  300 \\times 3 &= 900, \\\\\n  20 \\times 600 &= 12000, \\\\\n  20 \\times 80 &= 1600, \\\\\n  20 \\times 3 &= 60, \\\\\n  2 \\times 600 &= 1200, \\\\\n  2 \\times 80 &= 160, \\\\\n  2 \\times 3