Now, I need to add up all the partial products:.\n\nFirst partial product: 2276.\n\nSecond partial product: 5690.\n\nThird partial product: 398300.\n\nAdding them together:.\n\nLet me stack them up:.\n\n   2276.\n\n+  5690.\n\n+398300.\n\n----------.\n\nFirst, add 2276 and 5690:.\n\n2276 + 5690:.\n\n2000 + 5000 = 7000.\n\n276 + 690 = 966.\n\nTotal: 7000 + 966 = 7966? Wait, maybe better to do it step by step:.\n\n2276.\n\n+5690.\n\n=?.\n\nAdding units digits: 6 + 0 = 6.\n\nTens: 7 + 9 = 16, write 6, carry 1.\n\nHundreds: 2 + 6 = 8 + 1 (carry) = 9.\n\nThousands: 2 + 5 = 7.\n\nWait, that gives 7966? Wait, but 2276 + 5690:.\n\n2276 + 5000 = 7276.\n\n7276 + 690 = 7276 + 600 = 7876, then +90 = 7966. Yeah, that's correct.\n\nThen adding that to 398300:.\n\n7966 + 398300.\n\nHmm, 398300 + 7000 = 405,300. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
