orithm and verify the result using different methods.\n\nFirst, we break down the multiplication step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 739 by 9 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   739 \\times 9 = 6651\n   \\]\n   - \\(9 \\times 9 = 81\\) (write down 1, carry over 8)\n   - \\(9 \\times 3 = 27 + 8 = 35\\) (write down 5, carry over 3)\n   - \\(9 \\times 7 = 63 + 3 = 66\\)\n\n2. **Multiply 739 by 80 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   739 \\times 80 = 59120\n   \\]\n   - \\(8 \\times 9 = 72\\) (write down 2, carry over 7)\n   - \\(8 \\times 3 = 24 + 7 = 31\\) (write down 1, carry over 3)\n   - \\(8 \\times 7 = 56 + 3 = 59\\)\n   - Shift one position to the left (equivalent to multiplying by 10).\n\n3. **Multiply 739 by 200 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   739 \\times 200 = 147800\n   \\]\n   - \\(2 \\times 9 = 18\\) (write down 8, carry over 1)\n   - \\(2 \\times 3 = 6 + 1 = 7\\)\n   - \\(2 \\times 7 = 14\\)\n   - Shift two positions to the left (equivalent to multiplying by 100).\n\nNext, we sum the partial products:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n6651 \\\\\n+ 59120 \\\\\n+ 147800 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nAdding these together step-by-step:\n1. \\(6651 + 59120 = 65771\\)\n2. \\(65771 + 147800 = 213571\\)\n\nTo verify, we use another method by expressing 289 as \\(300 - 11\\):\n\\[\n739 \\times 289 = 739 \\times (300 - 11) = 739 \\times 300 - 739 \\times 11\n\\]\n\\[\n739 \\times 300 = 221700\n\\]\n\\[\n739 \\times 11 = 8129\n\\]\n\\[\n221700 - 8129 = 213571\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the result. Therefore, the product of 739 and 289 is \\(\\boxed{213571}\\).",
