nFirst, multiply 590 by 0 (units digit) \u2192 0  \nThen multiply 590 by 3 (tens digit, so actually 30) \u2192 590\u00d73=1,770, written as 17,700 (since it's the tens place)  \nThen multiply 590 by 3 (hundreds digit, so actually 300) \u2192 590\u00d73=1,770, written as 177,000 (shifted two places).  \n\nThen add them together: 0 + 17,700 + 177,000 = 194,700. Okay, so that matches the previous result. So that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another method like the difference of squares or something else? Let me see if there's another way. \n\nAlternatively, note that 590 \u00d7 330 = (600 - 10) \u00d7 (300 + 30). Maybe expanding that way?\n\nLet's try that: (600 - 10)(300 + 30) = 600\u00d7300 + 600\u00d730 -10\u00d7300 -10\u00d730.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n600\u00d7300 = 180,000\n\n600\u00d730 = 18,000\n\n-10\u00d7300 = -3,000\n\n-10\u00d730 = -300\n\nAdding those together: 180,000 + 18,000 = 198,000; then subtract 3,000 gives 195,000; subtract another 300 gives 194,700. So that also gives the same answer. \n\nHmm, so that seems consistent. Maybe another way is to use the fact that 590 \u00d7 330 = 59 \u00d7 10 \u00d7 33 \u00d7 10 = (59 \u00d733) \u00d7 100. So first compute 59\u00d733, then multiply by 100. \n\nCalculating 59\u00d733. Let's see, 59\u00d730 is 1,770 and 59\u00d73 is 177. Adding those together: 1,770 + 177 = 1,947. Then multiply by 100 gives 194,700. \n\nAh, that's a much simpler way. So that's the same answer again. \n\nTherefore, all methods are giving me 194,700, so I think that's the correct product. \n\nWait, let me just confirm once more with a calculator-like approach. Let me do 590 \u00d7 330. Let's think of 590 \u00d7 300 = 177,000 and 590 \u00d7 30 = 17,700. Adding those together gives 177,000 +17,700 = 194,700. Yep, exactly. \n\nOkay, so all methods converge to 194,700. Therefore, I think that's the right answer. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, so I'm confident that's correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product 