y, let's compute 763 \u00d7 828 as (700 + 63) \u00d7 (800 + 28) and expand:\n\n= 700\u00d7800 + 700\u00d728 + 63\u00d7800 + 63\u00d728\n\nCompute each term:\n\n700\u00d7800 = 560,000.\n\n700\u00d728: 700\u00d720 = 14,000; 700\u00d78=5,600 \u2192 14,000 + 5,600 = 19,600.\n\n63\u00d7800: 60\u00d7800=48,000; 3\u00d7800=2,400 \u2192 48,000 + 2,400 = 50,400.\n\n63\u00d728: Let's compute 60\u00d728 + 3\u00d728.\n\n60\u00d728 = 1,680; 3\u00d728=84 \u2192 1,680 +84 = 1,764.\n\nNow add all four terms:\n\n560,000 +19,600 = 579,600.\n\n579,600 +50,400 = 630,000.\n\n630,000 +1,764 = 631,764. Exactly the same result again.\n\nAlright, so through multiple methods\u2014standard multiplication, breaking into hundreds/tens/units, and expanding using distributive property\u2014each time the result is 631,764. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 763 and 828 is indeed 631,764.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 763 and 828 is \\boxed{631764}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 763 and 828, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify the result through multiple methods:\n\n1. **Standard Multiplication**:\n   - Multiply 763 by 8 (units place):\n     \\[\n     763 \\times 8 = 6104\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 763 by 2 (tens place, shifted one position left):\n     \\[\n     763 \\times 2 = 1526 \\quad \\text{(shifted left: 15260)}\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 763 by 8 (hundreds place, shifted two positions left):\n     \\[\n     763 \\times 8 = 6104 \\quad \\text{(shifted left twice: 610400)}\n     \\]\n   - Add the partial products:\n     \\[\n     6104 + 15260 + 610400 = 631764\n     \\]\n\n2. **Distributive Property**:\n   - Break down the numbers and expand:\n     \\[\n     763 \\times 828 = 763 \\times (800 + 28) = 763 \\times 800 + 763 \\times 28\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each part:\n     \\[\n     763 \\times 800 = 610400\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     763 \\times 28 = 15260 + 6104 = 21364\n     \\]\n   - Sum the results:\n     \\[\n     610400 + 21364 = 631764\n     \\]\n\n3. **Alternative Expansion**:\n   - Expand both numbers using distributive property:\n     \\[\n     (700 + 63) \\times (800 + 28)\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each term:\n     \\[\n     700 \\times 800 = 560000\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     700 \\times 28 = 19600\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     63 \\times 800 = 50400\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     63 \\times 28 = 1764\n     \\]\n   - Sum all terms:\n     \\[\n     560000 + 19600 + 50400 + 1764 = 631764\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 763 and 828 is \\(\\boxed{631764}\\).",
