re, I think the answer is definitely 145,512.\n\nWait, but let me just go through the original multiplication step once again, just to make sure I didn't make any arithmetic errors the first time.\n\nOriginal problem: 172 \u00d7846.\n\nFirst partial product (units digit 6):\n\n172 \u00d76: 100\u00d76=600, 70\u00d76=420, 2\u00d76=12. 600+420=1020 +12=1032. Correct.\n\nSecond partial product (tens digit 4, so 40):\n\n172 \u00d740: 172\u00d74=688, then \u00d710=6,880. Correct.\n\nThird partial product (hundreds digit 8, so 800):\n\n172\u00d7800: 172\u00d78=1,376; \u00d7100=137,600. Correct.\n\nAdding them:\n\n1,032 +6,880 = 7,912. Then 7,912 +137,600.\n\nAdding 7,000 to 137,600 gives 144,600. Then add the remaining 912 to get 145,512. Yep, that's right.\n\nAlright, so after multiple methods and checks, I can confidently say that the product of 172 and 846 is 145,512.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 172 and 846 is \\boxed{145512}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 172 and 846, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 172 by the units digit of 846 (6):**\n   \\[\n   172 \\times 6 = 1032\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 172 by the tens digit of 846 (40):**\n   \\[\n   172 \\times 40 = 6880\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 172 by the hundreds digit of 846 (800):**\n   \\[\n   172 \\times 800 = 137600\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   1032 + 6880 = 7912\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   7912 + 137600 = 145512\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 172 and 846 is \\(\\boxed{145512}\\).",
