hundreds place so 200):\n\n435 \u00d7200 = 435 \u00d72 \u00d7100 = 870 \u00d7100 = 87,000.\n\nNow add them all together:\n\n435 (from the units)\n\n+ 39,150 (from the tens)\n\n+87,000 (from the hundreds)\n\nAdding them step by step:\n\nFirst, 435 + 39,150 = 39,585\n\nThen, 39,585 + 87,000 = 126,585.\n\nSo that's 126,585. So that matches my previous total. So that must be correct.\n\nWait, so in my first method, when I was adding all the components, I ended up with the same answer. Let me check again the first method's addition to see where I might have messed up.\n\nFirst components:\n\n80,000\n\n+ 36,000 = 116,000\n\n+ 400 = 116,400\n\n+ 6,000 = 122,400\n\n+ 2,700 = 125,100\n\n+30 = 125,130\n\n+1,000 = 126,130\n\n+450 = 126,580\n\n+5 = 126,585.\n\nAh, okay, so in my first calculation, when I thought I had 126,580, then adding 5 gives 126,585. So that's correct. I just needed to add the final 5. So that's the same as the second method. So both methods give me 126,585. So that must be the right answer.\n\nAlternatively, to confirm once more, maybe using another method like the distributive property:\n\n435 \u00d7 291 = (400 + 35) \u00d7 (200 + 91)\n\nBut that might complicate more. Alternatively, maybe using the difference of squares or something else. Hmm, not sure. Alternatively, approximating to check.\n\n435 \u00d7 291. Let's approximate to check if 126,585 is reasonable.\n\n400 \u00d7 300 = 120,000. Since 435 is a bit more than 400, and 291 is a bit less than 300. The difference would be 35 more on the first number and 9 less on the second. So, the approximate would be 120,000 + (35\u00d7300) - (9\u00d7400) + (35\u00d79). Let me see:\n\nWait, actually, expanding (400 + 35)(300 - 9) = 400\u00d7300 + 400\u00d7(-9) + 35\u00d7300 + 35\u00d7(-9)\n\n= 120,000 - 3,600 + 10,500 - 315\n\n= 120,000 - 3,600 is 116,400; 116,400 + 10,500 is 126,900; 126,900 - 315 is 126,585. So exactly the same. So that confirms it again. So I can be confident that 126,585 is the correct product.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 126,585.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 435 and 291 is \\boxed{126585}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 435 and 291, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 435 by 1 (the units place of 291):\n   \\[\n   435 \\times 1 = 435\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 435 by 90 (the tens place of 291):\n   \\[\n   435 \\times 90 = 435 \\times 9 \\times 10 = 3915 \\times 10 = 39150\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 435 by 200 (the hundreds place of 291):\n   \\[\n   435 \\times 200 = 435 \\times 2 \\times 100 = 870 \\times 100 = 87000\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the results of the three multiplications together:\n   \\[\n   435 + 39150 + 87000\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add 435 and 39150:\n     \\[\n     435 + 39150 = 39585\n     \\]\n   - Then, add the result to 87000:\n     \\[\n     39585 + 87000 = 126585\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 435 and 291 is \\(\\boxed{126585}\\).",
