      "text": "668,800 + 62,700 equals?\n\nLet me add the thousands first. 668,800 is 668.8 thousands, and 62,700 is 62.7 thousands. Adding those together: 668.8 + 62.7 = 731.5 thousands, so 731,500. Wait, but let me do it step by step to make sure.\n\n668,800 + 62,700:\n\nStart with the units place, but since both numbers end with 00, it's easier. 668,800 + 60,000 = 728,800. Then add 2,700 more: 728,800 + 2,700 = 731,500. Yes, that's correct. So the final product is 731,500. \n\nWait, but let me verify this using another method just to be sure. Maybe using the standard multiplication algorithm.\n\nMultiplying 836 by 875. Let's write it out as:\n\n      836\n    x875\n    -------\n\nStarting with multiplying 836 by 5 (units place):\n\n836 * 5 = 4,180. \n\nThen multiplying 836 by 70 (tens place, so 7*10). So 836*7=5,852, then shifted one position to the left (because of the 10) becomes 58,520. \n\nNext, multiplying 836 by 800 (hundreds place, so 8*100). 836*8=6,688, shifted two positions to the left becomes 668,800. \n\nAdding all three results: 4,180 + 58,520 + 668,800. Let's do this step by step. \n\nFirst, 4,180 + 58,520 = 62,700. Then adding that to 668,800 gives 731,500. So that's the same as before. \n\nAlternatively, perhaps another way: using the fact that 875 is 1000 - 125. Wait, that might complicate but let me see.\n\nAlternatively, 875 is 7/8 of 1000. Hmm, not sure if that helps here. Alternatively, maybe 836 * 875 = 836 * (800 + 75) which is what I already did. \n\nAlternatively, perhaps using the distributive property in another way. Maybe 836 can be broken down? Let's see, 800 + 30 +6, but that might not help. \n\nAlternatively, use the standard multiplication steps again. Let me try that. \n\nMultiplying 836 by 875:\n\nFirst, write 875 as 5 * 175, but perhaps not helpful. Alternatively, perhaps write 836*875 as 836*(800 + 75) as before. \n\nAlternatively, let me try cross-multiplying. Let me set it up vertically:\n\n        836\n      x875\n      -------\n        4180   (836 x 5)\n       58520   (836 x 70, shifted one position)\n      668800   (836 x 800, shifted two positions)\n      ---------\n      731500\n\nYes, that's the same as before. \n\nAlternatively, perhaps I made an error in the initial breakdown. Let me verify with a calculator method. \n\nWait, since I can't use a calculator, but maybe approximate to check. \n\n836 is approximately 800, and 875 is approximately 900. 800*900 = 720,000. Our result is 731,500 which is a bit higher, but given that 836 is 36 more than 800, and 875 is 25 less than 900, so the approximation makes sense. \n\nAlternatively, 836 * 875. Let me think of 836*800 = 668,800. Then 836*75. Since 75 is 3/4 of 100, so 836*75 is 3/4 of 836*100, which is 83,600. 3/4 of that is 62,700. Adding them gives 668,800 + 62,700 = 731,500. \n\nHmm, all methods are leading me to the same answer. I think that's correct. \n\nWait, just to make sure, let me try another angle. Let me compute 836 * 875 as (800 + 36)*(800 + 75). Wait, actually, no, that would be expanding (a + b)(c + d), but perhaps that complicates. Alternatively, perhaps use some other identity? Not sure. \n\nAlternatively, perhaps compute 836 * 875 as 836 * (700 + 175). Wait, 700 +175 is 875, but perhaps that's more steps. Let me see:\n\n836*700 = 585,200 (since 836*7=5,852; times 100 is 585,200). \n\n836*175: Hmm, 175 is 100 +75, so 836*100=83,600 and 836*75=62,700 as before. Adding those gives 83,600 +62,700 = 146,300. Then total is 585,200 +146,300 = 731,500. Same answer again. \n\nOkay, so all different methods are confirming that the product is 731,500. I think that's solid. \n\nJust to recap the steps one more time:\n\nFirst method: Break down 875 into 800 +75. Multiply 836 by each and add.\n\n836*800 = 668,800\n\n836*75 = 62,700\n\nTotal: 668,800 +62,700 = 731,500.\n\nSecond method: Break down 875 into 5, 70, 800 and use standard multiplication steps, which also gives 731,500.\n\nThird method: Using approximation to check that it's in the ballpark, and it is.\n\nFourth method: Breaking down 875 into 700 + 175 and still getting the same result.\n\nTherefore, I'm confident that the product of 836 and 875 is 731,500.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 836 and 875 is \\boxed{731500}.\n</think>\n\nTo solve the product of 836 and 875, we can use the distributive property by breaking down 875 into 800 and 75:\n\n\\[\n836 \\times 875 = 836 \\times (800 + 75)\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(836 \\times 800\\):\n\n\\[\n836 \\times 800 = 836 \\times 8 \\times 100\n\\]\n\\[\n836 \\times 8 = 6688 \\quad \\text{(since } 800 \\times 8 = 6400, \\, 30 \\times 8 = 240, \\, 6 \\times 8 = 48 \\text{ and } 6400 + 240 + 48 = 6688\\text{)}\n\\]\n\\[\n6688 \\times 100 = 668800\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(836 \\times 75\\). Break down 75 into 70 and 5:\n\n\\[\n836 \\times 75 = 836 \\times (70 + 5)\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(836 \\times 70\\):\n\n\\[\n836 \\times 70 = 836 \\times 7 \\times 10\n\\]\n\\[\n836 \\times 7 = 5852 \\quad \\text{(since } 800 \\times 7 = 5600, \\, 30 \\times 7 = 210, \\, 6 \\times 7 = 42 \\text{ and } 5600 + 210 + 42 = 5852\\text{)}\n\\]\n\\[\n5852 \\times 10 = 58520\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(836 \\times 5\\):\n\n\\[\n836 \\times 5 = 4180 \\quad \\text{(since } 800 \\times 5 = 4000, \\, 30 \\times 5 = 150, \\, 6 \\times 5 = 30 \\text{ and } 4000 + 150 + 30 = 4180\\text{)}\n\\]\n\nAdd the results of \\(836 \\times 70\\) and \\(836 \\times 5\\):\n\n\\[\n58520 + 4180 = 62700\n\\]\n\nFinally, add the results of \\(836 \\times 800\\) and \\(836 \\times 75\\):\n\n\\[\n668800 + 62700 = 731500\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 836 and 875 is \\(\\boxed{731500}\\).",
