0 +2,291=69,991.\n\nThen total would be 210,000 +69,991=279,991? Wait, no, hold on, actually, that's not the right way. Wait, the expansion is (300 +29)(600 +79)=300\u00d7600 +300\u00d779 +29\u00d7600 +29\u00d779. So indeed 180,000 +23,700 +17,400 +2,291= 180,000 +23,700 is 203,700; plus17,400 is 221,100; plus2,291 is 223,391. Oh! That's exactly the result I had before. So that's a good check. So this method gives the same answer. Therefore, that confirms that 223,391 is correct.\n\nAlternatively, let me compute 329 \u00d7 679 using another approach, perhaps the lattice method or another multiplication technique.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps compute 329 \u00d7 680 - 329.\n\nSince 679 is 680 -1. So 329\u00d7679 =329\u00d7(680 -1)=329\u00d7680 -329.\n\nCompute 329\u00d7680 first.\n\n329\u00d7680. Since 680 is 68 \u00d710. So 329\u00d768 \u00d710.\n\nFirst compute 329\u00d768. Let's do that.\n\n329\u00d768:\n\nBreakdown:\n\n329\u00d760 +329\u00d78.\n\n329\u00d760: 329\u00d76\u00d710. 329\u00d76=1,974. \u00d710 is 19,740.\n\n329\u00d78: 329\u00d78. 8\u00d79=72, write 2, carryover7.\n\n8\u00d72=16 +7=23. Write 3, carryover2.\n\n8\u00d73=24 +2=26. So 2,632.\n\nAdding them together:19,740 +2,632 =22,372. Then \u00d710 would be 223,720? Wait, no, wait. Wait, 329\u00d768 is 22,372, then \u00d710 gives 223,720? Wait, no. Wait, 329\u00d7680 is 329\u00d768\u00d710. Wait, 329\u00d768 is 22,372, so \u00d710 is 223,720. Then subtract 329: 223,720 -329 =223,391. Which matches the previous result. So that's another verification.\n\nTherefore, I can be confident that the product is 223,391.\n\nAlternatively, let me do the multiplication step-by-step again without breaking into partial products, just to be thorough.\n\nMultiplying 329 by 679:\n\nStart with 329 \u00d79 =2,961.\n\nThen 329 \u00d770 =23,030.\n\nThen 329 \u00d7600=197,400.\n\nAdding them up gives the same as before. So, yes.\n\nWait, another way to check could be to use a calculator, but since I don't have one here, but since multiple methods have given me the same result, I think it's safe.\n\nAlternatively, let me compute 679 \u00d7329 and see if I get the same result.\n\n679 \u00d7329.\n\nUsing the same method:\n\nFirst, 679 \u00d79:\n\n9\u00d79=81, write 1 carryover8.\n\n9\u00d77=63 +8=71. Write 1 carryover7.\n\n9\u00d76=54 +7=61. So that gives 6,111? Wait, let's do it step by step.\n\nMultiplying 679 \u00d79:\n\nUnits place:9\u00d79=81, write 1, carryover8.\n\nTens place:9\u00d77=63 +8=71, write 1, carryover7.\n\nHundreds place:9\u00d76=54 +7=61. So writing 61. So the first partial product is 6,111.\n\nWait, so that's 6,111? Wait, but 679\u00d79 is 6,111. Let me confirm:\n\n600\u00d79=5,400.\n\n70\u00d79=630, so 5,400+630=6,030.\n\n9\u00d79=81. 6,030+81=6,111. Correct.\n\nNext, multiplying by the tens digit, which is 2 (from 329, the second digit is 2 in the tens place). So 679 \u00d720.\n\n679\u00d72=1,358. Then \u00d710 gives 13,580.\n\nThird partial product: multiplying by the hundreds digit, which is 3 (from 329's hundreds place). So 679\u00d7300.\n\n679\u00d73=2,037. \u00d7100 gives 203,700.\n\nAdding all partial products:\n\nFirst:6,111\n\nSecond:13,580\n\nThird:203,700\n\nTotal: 6,111 +13,580 =19,691. Then +203,700 =223,391. Same result. So that's another confirmation.\n\nTherefore, I can be sure that the product is indeed 223,391.\n\nWait, but just to ensure I didn't make any arithmetic errors in these steps, let me recheck one of the partial products again.\n\nTake 329 \u00d7 600 = 197,400.\n\nYes, 329 \u00d76=1,974, so \u00d7100 is 197,400. Correct.\n\n329\u00d770=23,030. 329\u00d77=2,303, so \u00d710 is 23,030. Correct.\n\n329\u00d79=2,961. Correct.\n\nAdding them together: 2,961 +23,030 =25,991; 25,991+197,400=223,391.\n\nAll steps check out. I think this is solid.\n\nAnother way to check is digit-by-digit multiplication with a different method, like the Russian peasant algorithm, but that might take longer. Alternatively, check if the product is divisible by certain numbers to see if it makes sense.\n\nFor instance, 329 is 329, and 679 is 679. Let me see if either has factors that could simplify.\n\n329 divided by 7? 7\u00d747=329? 7\u00d740=280, 7\u00d747=329. Yes, 7\u00d747=329. Wait, 7\u00d747 is 329? Let me compute 47\u00d77: 40\u00d77=280, 7\u00d77=49, so 280+49=329. Yes, so 329=7\u00d747.\n\nSimilarly, 679 divided by 7? 7\u00d797=679? 7\u00d790=630, 7\u00d77=49, so 630+49=679. Yes, so 679=7\u00d797.\n\nTherefore, 329\u00d7679 = (7\u00d747)\u00d7(7\u00d797) =7\u00b2\u00d747\u00d797.\n\nCompute 7\u00d77=49, so 49\u00d747\u00d797.\n\nFirst compute 47\u00d797. Let's compute that: 47\u00d797.\n\n47\u00d7100=4,700 minus 47\u00d73=141. So 4,700 -141=4,559.\n\nTherefore, 49\u00d74,559.\n\nHmm, 49\u00d74,559. Let's compute that:\n\n49\u00d74,559 = (50 -1)\u00d74,559 =50\u00d74,559 -1\u00d74,559.\n\n50\u00d74,559 =227,950.\n\nSubtract 4,559: 227,950 -4,559 =223,391. Exactly the same result. Wow, that's another confirmation. So breaking down into prime factors and multiplying also gives the same answer. Therefore, this method also leads to 223,391. This gives me even more confidence that the result is correct.\n\nTherefore, after multiple methods and checks, I can confidently say the product of 329 and 679 is 223,391.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 329 and 679 is \\boxed{223391}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 329 and 679, we use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 329 by 9 (the ones place of 679):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     329 \\\\\n   \\times \\  9 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     2961 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   Calculation:\n   \\[\n   9 \\times 9 = 81 \\quad (\\text{write } 1, \\text{ carry } 8) \\\\\n   9 \\times 2 = 18 + 8 = 26 \\quad (\\text{write } 6, \\text{ carry } 2) \\\\\n   9 \\times 3 = 27 + 2 = 29 \\quad (\\text{write } 29)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 329 by 70 (the tens place of 679):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     329 \\\\\n   \\times \\ 70 \\\\\n   \\hline\n    23030 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   Calculation:\n   \\[\n   7 \\times 9 = 63 \\quad (\\text{write } 3, \\text{ carry } 6) \\\\\n   7 \\times 2 = 14 + 6 = 20 \\quad (\\text{write } 0, \\text{ carry } 2) \\\\\n   7 \\times 3 = 21 + 2 = 23 \\quad (\\text{write } 23) \\\\\n   \\text{Result shifted left by 1 digit: } 23030\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 329 by 600 (the hundreds place of 679):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     329 \\\\\n   \\times \\ 600 \\\\\n   \\hline\n    197400 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   Calculation:\n   \\[\n   6 \\times 9 = 54 \\quad (\\text{write } 4, \\text{ carry } 5) \\\\\n   6 \\times 2 = 12 + 5 = 17 \\quad (\\text{write } 7, \\text{ carry } 1) \\\\\n   6 \\times 3 = 18 + 1 = 19 \\quad (\\text{write } 19) \\\\\n   \\text{Result shifted left by 2 digits: } 197400\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     2961 \\\\\n   + 23030 \\\\\n   +197400 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     223391 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\n   Adding step-by-step:\n   \\[\n   2961 + 23030 = 25991 \\\\\n   25991 + 197400 = 223391\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 329 and 679 is \\(\\boxed{223391}\\).",
