Then +324 is 246,564. Yep.\n\nTherefore, seems like 246,564 is the correct answer.\n\nWait but let me check my initial partial products again:\n\nFirst partial product: 761\u00d74 = 3,044. Correct.\n\nSecond: 761\u00d720=15,220. Correct.\n\nThird: 761\u00d7300=228,300. Correct.\n\nAdding them:\n\n3,044 +15,220 = 18,264.\n\n18,264 +228,300: 18,264 + 200,000 = 218,264; 218,264 +28,300 = 246,564. Correct.\n\nHmm, so I think that's the right answer. But just to be thorough, maybe do the multiplication vertically again step by step.\n\nLet me write it out again:\n\n       7 6 1.\n\n     \u00d7 3 2 4.\n\n     -----------\n\nFirst, multiply 761 by 4:\n\n4\u00d71 =4, 4\u00d76=24 (carry 2), 4\u00d77=28 +2=30. So 3044.\n\nSecond, multiply 761 by 2 (tens place):\n\n2\u00d71=2 (tens place, so it's actually 20\u00d71, but in the partial product, we write it shifted one to the left).\n\nWait, let's do it properly:\n\nSecond line: multiplying by the 2 (tens digit), so each digit is multiplied by 2, and shifted one place left.\n\n2\u00d71 =2 (tens place, so it's actually in the tens column, so write 2 in the tens place, i.e., the second digit from the right).\n\nWait, maybe writing the partial products:\n\nFirst partial product (\u00d74):\n\n    761.\n\n  \u00d7  324.\n\n  ---------.\n\n    3044   (this is \u00d74).\n\nSecond partial product (\u00d720):\n\n       761.\n\n  \u00d7  324.\n\n  ---------.\n\n    3044.\n\n   15220   (\u00d72, shifted one position left).\n\nThird partial product (\u00d7300):\n\n       761.\n\n  \u00d7  324.\n\n  ---------.\n\n    3044.\n\n   15220.\n\n+228300   (\u00d73 shifted two positions left).\n\n---------.\n\nNow adding them:\n\nLet me write all the partial products aligned properly:\n\n      3044.\n\n     15220.\n\n    228300.\n\nAdding these:\n\nStart with the first two:\n\n3044 + 15220:\n\n3044.\n\n+15220.\n\n= 18264.\n\nThen 18264 + 228300:\n\n18264 + 228300.\n\nAdding 18,264 + 228,300:\n\n228,300 + 10,000 = 238,300.\n\n238,300 + 8,264 = 246,564. Correct.\n\nTherefore, the final product is 246,564.\n\nWait, but to make sure, perhaps I can do a different verification method. For instance, estimate the product to see if it's in the ballpark.\n\n761 is approximately 760, and 324 is approximately 320.\n\n760 \u00d7 320 = ?\n\n760 \u00d7 300 = 228,000.\n\n760 \u00d720 = 15,200.\n\nTotal is 228,000 +15,200 = 243,200.\n\nThe actual answer is 246,564, which is a bit higher, which makes sense because we rounded down both numbers. 761 is 1 more than 760, and 324 is 4 more than 320. So the difference would be 1\u00d7324 + 760\u00d74 +1\u00d74. Wait, actually the exact difference:\n\n(760 +1)(320 +4) = 760\u00d7320 +760\u00d74 +1\u00d7320 +1\u00d74.\n\nSo the extra over 760\u00d7320 is 760\u00d74 +320 +4 = 3,040 +320 +4=3,364. So 243,200 +3,364 =246,564. Which matches. Therefore, that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, using another estimation: 700\u00d7300=210,000, 700\u00d724=16,800, 61\u00d7300=18,300, 61\u00d724=1,464. Adding all together: 210,000 +16,800 =226,800; 226,800 +18,300 =245,100; 245,100 +1,464=246,564. Same result.\n\nTherefore, I'm confident the answer is 246,564.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 761 and 324 is \\boxed{246564}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 761 and 324, we use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 761 by 4 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   761 \\times 4 = 3044\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 761 by 20 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   761 \\times 2 = 1522 \\quad \\text{(then shift one position to the left)} \\quad \\Rightarrow 15220\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 761 by 300 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   761 \\times 3 = 2283 \\quad \\text{(then shift two positions to the left)} \\quad \\Rightarrow 228300\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     3044 \\\\\n   +15220 \\\\\n  +228300 \\\\\n  \\hline\n   246564 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add \\(3044 + 15220\\):\n     \\[\n     3044 + 15220 = 18264\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to \\(228300\\):\n     \\[\n     18264 + 228300 = 246564\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 761 and 324 is \\(\\boxed{246564}\\).",
