he hundreds place, this 9 represents 900. So, we need to multiply 856 by 900. Alternatively, 856 × 9 and then add two zeros at the end (because it's the hundreds place).\n\nCalculating 856 × 9:.\n\nWait, we already did 856 × 9 earlier, which was 7704. So adding two zeros would make it 770,400. That's the third partial product.\n\nNow, we need to add all these partial products together:.\n\nFirst partial product: 7,704.\n\nSecond partial product: 34,240.\n\nThird partial product: 770,400.\n\nLet me write them down aligned properly for addition:.\n\n```.\n   7,704.\n+ 34,240.\n+770,400.\n----------.\n```.\n\nStarting with adding the first two: 7,704 + 34,240.\n\n7,704 + 34,240:.\n\n7,000 + 34,000 = 41,000.\n\n704 + 240 = 944.\n\nSo total is 41,000 + 944 = 41,944.\n\nThen add that to 770,400:.\n\n41,944 + 770,400.\n\nLet me break that down:.\n\n40,000 + 770,000 = 810,000.\n\n1,944 + 400 = 2,344.\n\nWait, that might not be the right way. Maybe better to add step by step:.\n\n770,400 + 40,000 = 810,400.\n\nThen add the remaining 1,944:. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
