f 856 and 949, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy.\n\n### Method 1: Standard Multiplication Algorithm\n1. **Multiply 856 by 9 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   856 \\times 9 = 7704\n   \\]\n2. **Multiply 856 by 40 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   856 \\times 4 = 3424 \\quad \\text{(then add a zero)} \\quad 34240\n   \\]\n3. **Multiply 856 by 900 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   856 \\times 9 = 7704 \\quad \\text{(then add two zeros)} \\quad 770400\n   \\]\n4. **Add the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   7704 + 34240 + 770400 = 812344\n   \\]\n\n### Method 2: Distributive Property (Difference of Squares)\n1. **Express 949 as \\(1000 - 51\\):**\n   \\[\n   856 \\times 949 = 856 \\times (1000 - 51)\n   \\]\n2. **Calculate each part:**\n   \\[\n   856 \\times 1000 = 856000\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   856 \\times 51 = 43656\n   \\]\n3. **Subtract the results:**\n   \\[\n   856000 - 43656 = 812344\n   \\]\n\n### Method 3: Breaking into Smaller Components\n1. **Break down the numbers:**\n   \\[\n   856 = 800 + 56 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 949 = 900 + 49\n   \\]\n2. **Use the distributive property:**\n   \\[\n   (800 + 56)(900 + 49) = 800 \\times 900 + 800 \\times 49 + 56 \\times 900 + 56 \\times 49\n   \\]\n3. **Calculate each term:**\n   \\[\n   800 \\times 900 = 720000\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   800 \\times 49 = 39200\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   56 \\times 900 = 50400\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   56 \\times 49 = 2744\n   \\]\n4. **Sum all terms:**\n   \\[\n   720000 + 39200 + 50400 + 2744 = 812344\n   \\]\n\n### Method 4: Average and Difference of Squares\n1. **Find the average and difference:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Average} = \\frac{856 + 949}{2} = 902.5 \\quad \\text{Difference} = 46.5\n   \\]\n2. **Apply the identity:**\n   \\[\n   (902.5 - 46.5)(902.5 + 46.5) = 902.5^2 - 46.5^2\n   \\]\n3. **Calculate each square:**\n   \\[\n   902.5^2 = 814506.25 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 46.5^2 = 2162.25\n   \\]\n4. **Subtract the squares:**\n   \\[\n   814506.25 - 2162.25 = 812344\n   \\]\n\nAll methods confirm the 