800+40=2840. So first partial product: 2840.\n\nNext, multiply by 9 (tens place). Since it's the tens place, the result is shifted one to the left (equivalent to multiplying by 10).\n\n9\u00d7710: 9\u00d7700=6300; 9\u00d710=90 \u2192 6300+90=6390. Shifted left by one digit gives 63,900.\n\nThen multiply by 1 (hundreds place), shifted two places left (equivalent to \u00d7100).\n\n1\u00d7710=710; shifted two places becomes 71,000.\n\nNow add them up:\n\n2840  .\n63900  .\n71000  .\nTotal: Let's align them properly.\n\n\u2003\u00a02,840  .\n+63,900  .\n+71,000  .\n----------.\nAdding the first two: 2,840 +63,900 = 66,740.\n\nThen 66,740 +71,000 = 137,740.\n\nSame answer again. So that seems consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another method, like breaking down both numbers into smaller components.\n\n710 can be written as 700 +10.\n\n194 can be written as 200 -6.\n\nTherefore, using the distributive property:\n\n(700 +10) \u00d7 (200 -6) = 700\u00d7200 +700\u00d7(-6) +10\u00d7200 +10\u00d7(-6).\n\nCompute each term:\n\n700\u00d7200 = 140,000.\n\n700\u00d7(-6) = -4,200.\n\n10\u00d7200 =2,000.\n\n10\u00d7(-6)= -60.\n\nNow add them up: 140,000 -4,200 +2,000 -60.\n\nFirst 140,000 -4,200 = 135,800.\n\n135,800 +2,000 =137,800.\n\n137,800 -60 =137,740.\n\nSame result again. Hmm, so that's three different methods and all give me 137,740. Seems solid. Maybe I should check with a calculator, but since I can't use one, I'll verify through another method.\n\nAlternatively, let's do the multiplication step by step digit by digit:\n\nMultiplying 710 \u00d7194.\n\nStarting with 4\u00d7710:\n\n4\u00d70 =0, 4\u00d71=4, 4\u00d77=28. So writing down 2840.\n\nThen 9\u00d7710 (tens place, so shifted left one):\n\n9\u00d70=0, 9\u00d71=9, 9\u00d77=63. So that would be 6390, shifted left becomes 63900.\n\nThen 1\u00d7710 (hundreds place, shifted left two):\n\n1\u00d70=0, 1\u00d71=1, 1\u00d77=7. So 710 shifted two becomes 71000.\n\nAdding them up again gets 2840 +63900 +71000 =137,740.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do the multiplication vertically in a different way. Let me try:\n\nMultiply 710 by 194:\n\nFirst, write 710 on top, 194 below. So,\n\n\u2003\u2003710  .\n\u00d7\u00a0194  .\n----------.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n4\u00d7710: 4\u00d70=0, 4\u00d71=4, 4\u00d77=28. So write 2840.\n\nNext line, multiply by 9 (tens place), so we have to shift one:\n\n9\u00d70=0, 9\u00d71=9, 9\u00d77=63. So writing 6390, but shifted one to the left: so it's 63900.\n\nThird line, multiply by 1 (hundreds place), shifted two:\n\n1\u00d70=0, 1\u00d71=1, 1\u00d77=7. So 710 shifted two is 71000.\n\nAdding all three lines:\n\n2840  \n63900  \n71000  \nTotal: 137,740. Yep.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps check with another approach like the lattice method? Though that might be more time-consuming, but let me try a small part.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do 710 \u00d7200 =142,000, then subtract 710\u00d76=4,260. So 142,000 -4,260 =137,740. Yep, same answer again.\n\nAlternatively, use estimation to check if the answer is reasonable. 700\u00d7200 is 140,000. Since 710 is a bit more than 700, and 194 is a bit less than 200. So the actual product should be a bit more than 140,000 minus some amount. Since 710\u00d7200 is 142,000, and then subtract 710\u00d76=4,260, so 142,000 -4,260 is 137,740. That seems reasonable.\n\nAlternatively, let me compute 700\u00d7194 first, then add 10\u00d7194.\n\n700\u00d7194: 700\u00d7200=140,000 minus 700\u00d76=4,200, so 140,000 -4,200=135,800.\n\nThen 10\u00d7194=1,940.\n\nAdding those together:135,800 +1,940=137,740. Again the same answer.\n\nHmm, so all methods lead to 137,740. Therefore, I think that's the correct product. I don't see any errors in my calculations, and cross-verifying through multiple methods gives the same result. Therefore, I can be confident that the answer is 137,740.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 710 and 194 is \\boxed{137740}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 710 and 194, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify through multiple methods:\n\n1. **Standard Multiplication Algorithm:**\n   - Multiply 710 by 4 (units place):\n     \\[\n     710 \\times 4 = 2840\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 710 by 9 (tens place, shifted one position left):\n     \\[\n     710 \\times 9 = 6390 \\quad \\text{(shifted left gives 63900)}\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 710 by 1 (hundreds place, shifted two positions left):\n     \\[\n     710 \\times 1 = 710 \\quad \\text{(shifted left gives 71000)}\n     \\]\n   - Add the partial products:\n     \\[\n     2840 + 63900 + 71000 = 137740\n     \\]\n\n2. **Distributive Property:**\n   - Break down 194 into \\(200 - 6\\):\n     \\[\n     710 \\times 194 = 710 \\times (200 - 6)\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each term:\n     \\[\n     710 \\times 200 = 142000 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 710 \\times 6 = 4260\n     \\]\n   - Subtract the second term from the first:\n     \\[\n     142000 - 4260 = 137740\n     \\]\n\n3. **Alternative Breakdown:**\n   - Break down both numbers:\n     \\[\n     (700 + 10) \\times (200 - 6)\n     \\]\n   - Expand and calculate each term:\n     \\[\n     700 \\times 200 = 140000, \\quad 700 \\times (-6) = -4200, \\quad 10 \\times 200 = 2000, \\quad 10 \\times (-6) = -60\n     \\]\n   - Sum the results:\n     \\[\n     140000 - 4200 + 2000 - 60 = 137740\n     \\]\n\nAll methods consistently result in the product of 710 and 194 being \\(\\boxed{137740}\\).",
