      "text": "54,720 + 200 = 54,920, then +28 is 54,948. Wait, hold on, let me check that again.\n\nWait, 54,720 plus 228. Let's break it down: 54,720 + 200 is 54,920, and then add the remaining 28: 54,920 + 28 = 54,948. Okay, that seems right.\n\nBut let me verify using another method to be sure. Maybe using the standard multiplication algorithm.\n\nMultiplying 228 by 241:\n\nLet me write it vertically:\n\n\u2003\u2003228  \n\u00d7241  \n--------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit of the lower number (241):\n\nFirst, multiply 228 by 1 (the units place of 241):\n\n228 \u00d7 1 = 228.\n\nNext, multiply 228 by 4 (the tens place of 241). But since it's the tens place, it's actually 40. So, 228 \u00d7 4 = 912, but shifted one position to the left, so 9,120.\n\nThen multiply 228 by 2 (the hundreds place of 241), which is actually 200. So 228 \u00d7 2 = 456, shifted two positions left, making it 45,600.\n\nNow add all those together:\n\n228  \n9120  \n45600  \n-------  \nAdding them up:\n\nStart with 228 + 9,120 = 9,348. Then 9,348 + 45,600. Let's see, 9,348 + 45,600. Hmm, 9,000 + 45,000 is 54,000. Then 348 + 600 is 948. So total is 54,000 + 948 = 54,948. Okay, same result. Good, that matches my first method.\n\nAlternatively, maybe there's another way to cross-verify. Let me try using another method, perhaps the difference of squares or some other algebraic trick. Wait, 228 and 241, do these numbers relate in a way that can be simplified?\n\nHmm, 228 and 241. Let me see, 241 - 228 = 13. Not sure if that helps. Alternatively, maybe express 241 as 250 - 9? Let's see.\n\nWait, 250 - 9 is 241, but maybe that complicates things. Let's try:\n\n228 \u00d7 241 = 228 \u00d7 (250 - 9) = 228\u00d7250 - 228\u00d79.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n228\u00d7250. Since 250 is a quarter of 1000, so 228\u00d7250 = 228\u00d7(1000/4) = (228/4)*1000. 228 divided by 4 is 57. So 57\u00d71000 = 57,000.\n\nThen, 228\u00d79. Let's compute that: 200\u00d79=1,800 and 28\u00d79=252, so total is 1,800 + 252 = 2,052.\n\nSo subtracting: 57,000 - 2,052 = ?\n\n57,000 - 2,000 is 55,000, then subtract 52 more: 55,000 - 52 = 54,948. Same answer again! Okay, so that's a third method giving me the same result. That's reassuring.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard algorithm again but in a different order. Let me try 241 \u00d7 228 instead, just to see if commutative property holds.\n\n241 \u00d7 228. Let's do this vertically:\n\n\u2003\u2003241  \n\u00d7228  \n--------\n\nMultiply 241 by 8 (units place): 241\u00d78.\n\n200\u00d78=1,600; 40\u00d78=320; 1\u00d78=8. So 1,600 + 320 = 1,920 +8 = 1,928.\n\nThen multiply 241 by 2 (tens place, which is actually 20). So 241\u00d72=482, shifted one to the left: 4,820.\n\nThen multiply 241 by 2 (hundreds place, which is actually 200). Wait, no, the hundreds place in 228 is the first digit, which is 2, so 200. Wait, actually, 228 is 2 hundreds, 2 tens, 8 units. Wait, no, 228's digits are 2 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 8 (units). So when multiplying 241 \u00d7 228, the third step is multiplying by the hundreds place (the first 2 in 228), which is 200. So 241 \u00d7 200 = 48,200.\n\nNow add all three:\n\n1,928 (from units)  \n4,820 (from tens)  \n48,200 (from hundreds)  \nTotal: 1,928 + 4,820 = 6,748; then 6,748 + 48,200 = 54,948. Same result again. Perfect.\n\nHmm, so all methods are pointing to 54,948. Let me check if I might have made a mistake in any step. Wait, in the first method, when I broke down 241 into 200+40+1, and multiplied each by 228, then added, got 54,948. Second method vertical multiplication also same. Third method using 228*(250-9) gave same. Fourth method reversing the multiplication also same. So seems solid.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use calculator? But since I don't have one, but perhaps approximate to check reasonableness. 228 is approximately 230, 241 is approximately 240. 230*240 is 230*240. 200*240 = 48,000; 30*240=7,200. So total 55,200. The actual answer is 54,948, which is a bit less, which makes sense because we rounded both numbers up. The difference between 230*240 and 228*241 is 2 less in the first number and 1 more in the second. The net effect would be roughly (228*241) = (230 -2)*(240+1) = 230*240 +230*1 -2*240 -2*1. Which is 55,200 +230 -480 -2 = 55,200 - 252 = 54,948. Exactly. So that also confirms.\n\nTherefore, I'm confident that the product of 228 and 241 is 54,948.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 228 and 241 is \\boxed{54948}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 228 and 241, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into smaller parts:\n\n\\[\n228 \\times 241 = 228 \\times (200 + 40 + 1)\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term separately:\n\n1. \\(228 \\times 200 = 228 \\times 2 \\times 100 = 456 \\times 100 = 45600\\)\n2. \\(228 \\times 40 = 228 \\times 4 \\times 10 = 912 \\times 10 = 9120\\)\n3. \\(228 \\times 1 = 228\\)\n\nAdding these results together:\n\n\\[\n45600 + 9120 + 228 = 45600 + 9120 = 54720\n\\]\n\\[\n54720 + 228 = 54948\n\\]\n\nVerification using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   \\quad 228 \\\\\n\\times 241 \\\\\n\\hline\n   \\quad 228 \\quad (\\text{228 \u00d7 1}) \\\\\n  9120 \\quad \\ (\\text{228 \u00d7 40, shifted one position left}) \\\\\n+45600 \\quad (\\text{228 \u00d7 200, shifted two positions left}) \\\\\n\\hline\n   54948 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nAnother method using the difference of squares:\n\n\\[\n228 \\times 241 = 228 \\times (250 - 9) = 228 \\times 250 - 228 \\times 9\n\\]\n\\[\n228 \\times 250 = 57000 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 228 \\times 9 = 2052\n\\]\n\\[\n57000 - 2052 = 54948\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 228 and 241 is \\(\\boxed{54948}\\).",
