      "text": "446,000 + 5,472 = 451,472? Wait, no. Wait, 406,000 + 45,472.\n\nLet me add digit by digit:\n\n406,000\n\n+\u00a0 45,472\n\n= ?\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n0 +2 =2\n\n0+7=7\n\n0+4=4\n\n6 +5 =11, write 1, carryover 1.\n\n0 (from 406,000's thousands place) plus 4 (from 45,472's ten thousands place) plus the 1 carried over is 5.\n\nThen the 4 from the hundred thousands place.\n\nWait, perhaps better written as:\n\n406,000\n\n+\u00a0 45,472\n\n------------\n\nAdding units: 0+2=2\n\nTens:0+7=7\n\nHundreds:0+4=4\n\nThousands:6 +5=11, so write 1, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands: 0 (from 406,000) +4 (from 45,472) +1 (carryover) =5.\n\nHundred-thousands:4 (from 406,000) + 0 =4.\n\nSo the total is 451,472.\n\nWait, hold on, let's see:\n\n406,000\n\n+\u00a0 45,472\n\n= (400,000 + 6,000) + (40,000 + 5,000 + 472)\n\nSo 400,000 +40,000 =440,000\n\n6,000 +5,000 =11,000\n\nTotal so far:451,000, plus 472 is 451,472. Yes, that's right.\n\nSo the total product is 451,472.\n\nWait, but let me double-check my partial products to make sure I didn't make a mistake there.\n\nFirst partial product: 812 \u00d76 = 4,872. That's correct.\n\nSecond partial product: 812 \u00d750 =4,060 \u00d710? Wait, no, 812\u00d750 is 812\u00d75\u00d710. 812\u00d75=4,060, so 4,060 \u00d710 is 40,600. That's correct.\n\nThird partial product: 812\u00d7500. 812\u00d75=4,060, so times 100 is 406,000. Correct.\n\nAdding them: 4,872 +40,600 =45,472, then +406,000 gives 451,472. So that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can verify using another method, like the distributive property.\n\n812 \u00d7556 = 812\u00d7(500 +50 +6) = 812\u00d7500 +812\u00d750 +812\u00d76, which is exactly what I did. So that's the same as above.\n\nAlternatively, maybe another way: 800\u00d7556 + 12\u00d7556.\n\nLet me try that.\n\nFirst, 800\u00d7556.\n\n800\u00d7500 =400,000.\n\n800\u00d750=40,000.\n\n800\u00d76=4,800.\n\nAdding those together:400,000 +40,000=440,000 +4,800=444,800.\n\nThen 12\u00d7556.\n\n12\u00d750