ave made a mistake, but now with this method, it's 706,260. \n\nWait, but let me check with another method just to be sure. Maybe using another breakdown.\n\nAlternatively, 894 * 790 can be considered as (900 - 6) * (800 - 10). Wait, that might complicate, but let's try expanding it.\n\nUsing the formula (a - b)(c - d) = ac - ad - bc + bd.\n\nSo, (900 - 6)(800 - 10) = 900*800 - 900*10 - 6*800 + 6*10.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n900*800 = 720,000\n\n900*10 = 9,000\n\n6*800 = 4,800\n\n6*10 = 60\n\nNow putting them all together:\n\n720,000 - 9,000 - 4,800 + 60\n\nFirst subtract 9,000 from 720,000: 711,000\n\nThen subtract 4,800: 711,000 - 4,800 = 706,200\n\nThen add 60: 706,200 + 60 = 706,260\n\nSame result again. Hmm, so that's three different methods all leading to 706,260. So maybe I was right the first time, and my confusion was unfounded. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do straight multiplication:\n\n   894  \nx790  \n--------\nFirst, multiply 894 by 0: 0\n\nThen multiply 894 by 9 (tens place, but since it's the 9 in 790 is actually 90), so we have to shift one position.\n\nWait, actually, let's do it step by step:\n\nMultiplying 894 by 790:\n\nFirst, write it as:\n\n      894  \n    x790  \n    --------\n      000  (894 x 0)\n     8046   (894 x 9, shifted one position to the left because it's the tens place)\n   6258     (894 x 7, but since the 7 is in the hundreds place, shifted two positions)\n   --------\n   ?\n\nWait, actually, 790 is 7 hundreds, 9 tens, and 0 ones. So:\n\nFirst, multiply 894 by 0 (units place): 0\n\nThen multiply 894 by 9 (tens place, so actually 90), so 894*9=8046, then shift one position to the left: 80460\n\nThen multiply 894 by 7 (hundreds place, so 700), so 894*7=6258, then shift two positions to the left: 625800\n\nNow add the two results: 80,460 + 625,800 = ?\n\nAdding 80,460 + 625,800:\n\n625,800 + 80,000 = 705,800\n\nThen add 460: 705,800 + 460 = 706,260. \n\nSame answer again. Okay, so that confirms it again. \n\nTherefore, the product of 894 and 790 is 706,260. \n\nWait, but just to be thorough, maybe I should use another method. Let's try using the standard algorithm step by step.\n\nMultiplying 894 by 790:\n\nSince 790 has three digits, but the last digit is 0, so actually, it's 7 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 0 (units). \n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\nFirst, multiply by 0: 894 x 0 = 0. Write that down.\n\nNext, multiply by 9 (tens place). So 894 x 9 = 8,046. Since it's the tens place, we shift one position to the left, so it's 80,460.\n\nThen multiply by 7 (hundreds place). 894 x 7 = 6,258. Since it's the hundreds place, shift two positions to the left, making it 625,800.\n\nAdd those two results: 80,460 + 625,800 = 706,260. Yep, same as before.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do it all in one line:\n\n894 \u00d7 790\n\n= 894 \u00d7 (800 - 10)\n\n= 894\u00d7800 - 894\u00d710\n\n= 715,200 - 8,940\n\n= 715,200 - 8,000 - 940\n\n= 707,200 - 940\n\n= 706,260.\n\nSame result. Alright, so after going through multiple methods: breaking down using distributive property, using the standard multiplication algorithm, and verifying with another distributive approach, all lead to the same answer. I think that's solid. \n\nTherefore, I can confidently say the product of 894 and 790 is 706,260. \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 894 and 790 is \\boxed{706260}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 894 and 790, we can use the distributive property by breaking down 790 into 800 - 10:\n\n\\[\n894 \\times 790 = 894 \\times (800 - 10)\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(894 \\times 800\\):\n\n\\[\n894 \\times 800 = 894 \\times 8 \\times 100\n\\]\n\nBreaking down \\(894 \\times 8\\):\n\n\\[\n894 \\times 8 = (800 \\times 8) + (90 \\times 8) + (4 \\times 8) = 6400 + 720 + 32 = 7152\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\n894 \\times 800 = 7152 \\times 100 = 715200\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(894 \\times 10\\):\n\n\\[\n894 \\times 10 = 8940\n\\]\n\nSubtract the two results:\n\n\\[\n715200 - 8940 = 715200 - 8000 - 940 = 707200 - 940 = 706260\n\\]\n\nVerification using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n    894 \\\\\n  \\times 790 \\\\\n  \\hline\n    000 \\quad (\\text{894} \\times 0) \\\\\n   80460 \\quad (\\text{894} \\times 9 \\text{ shifted one position left}) \\\\\n 625800 \\quad (\\text{894} \\times 7 \\text{ shifted two positions left}) \\\\\n  \\hline\n  706260 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the result. Therefore, the product of 894 and 790 is \\(\\boxed{706260}\\).",
