      "text": "71219? Wait, let me check the addition again step by step.\n\nWait, 2519 + 68700. Let me think in terms of place value. 2519 is 2 thousands, 5 hundreds, 1 ten, 9 ones. 68700 is 6 ten thousands, 8 thousands, 7 hundreds, 0 tens, 0 ones.\n\nAdding them together:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\nOnes place: 9 + 0 = 9.\n\nTens place: 1 + 0 = 1.\n\nHundreds place: 5 + 7 = 12. So write down 2, carry over 1.\n\nThousands place: 2 (from 2519) + 8 (from 68700) + 1 (carryover) = 11. So write down 1, carry over 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 0 (since 2519 has no ten thousands) + 6 (from 68700) + 1 (carryover) = 7.\n\nSo putting it all together: 7 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 9 (ones). So 71219. Wait, but let me verify with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another approach to cross-verify. Let me try using the distributive property: 229 \u00d7 311. Let me break down 311 into 300 + 10 + 1. So, 229*(300 +10 +1) = 229\u00d7300 + 229\u00d710 + 229\u00d71.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n229\u00d7300 = 229\u00d73\u00d7100 = 687\u00d7100 = 68,700.\n\n229\u00d710 = 2,290.\n\n229\u00d71 = 229.\n\nAdding them together: 68,700 + 2,290 = 70,990; then 70,990 + 229 = 71,219. So same result. Hmm, that seems consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method like the lattice method or some shortcut? Let me see.\n\nAlternatively, if I notice that 229 and 311 are both primes? Wait, actually, I don't know if they are primes. Let me check quickly. 229: it's a well-known prime? Let's see, 15 squared is 225, so primes up to 15. 229 divided by 2? No. 3? 2+2+9=13, not divisible by 3. 5? Ends with 9. 7? 7*32=224, 224+7=231, so 229-224=5, so not divisible by 7. 11? 2-2+9=9, not divisible by 11. 13? 13*17=221, 221+13=234, so 229 is prime. 311 similarly: 17 squared is 289, 18 squared is 324. So check primes up to 17. 311 divided by 2? No. 3? 3+1+1=5, not divisible by 3. 5? Ends with 1. 7? 7*44=308, 308+7=315, so 311-308=3, not divisible by 7. 11? 3-1+1=3, not divisible by 11. 13? 13*23=299, 299+13=312, so 311-299=12, not divisible by 13. 17? 17*18=306, 306+17=323, so 311-306=5. Not divisible. So 311 is also a prime. Therefore, their product is just 229\u00d7311, which is 71,219 as we calculated. But maybe there's another way to compute this?\n\nAlternatively, maybe using (200+29)(300+11). Let me try expanding that:\n\n(200 + 29)(300 +11) = 200\u00d7300 + 200\u00d711 + 29\u00d7300 + 29\u00d711.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n200\u00d7300 = 60,000.\n\n200\u00d711 = 2,200.\n\n29\u00d7300 = 8,700.\n\n29\u00d711 = 319.\n\nNow add them all together:\n\n60,000 + 2,200 = 62,200.\n\n62,200 + 8,700 = 70,900.\n\n70,900 + 319 = 71,219. Same result again. Okay, that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the difference of squares or some other algebraic identity? Hmm, let's see.\n\nWait, 229 and 311, maybe express them as numbers around 270 or something? Let me think.\n\nAlternatively, 229 \u00d7 311. Let me see if they are equidistant from a common number. Let me see the average of 229 and 311. (229 + 311)/2 = (540)/2 = 270. So they are both 41 away from 270? 270 - 229 = 41, and 311 - 270 = 41. Oh! So they are symmetric around 270. So that means 229 = 270 - 41 and 311 = 270 + 41. Therefore, their product is (270 -41)(270 +41) = 270\u00b2 - (41)\u00b2. That might be easier to compute.\n\nLet's try that.\n\nFirst compute 270 squared: 270 \u00d7 270. 27 squared is 729, so 270 squared is 72,900.\n\nThen compute 41 squared: 41 \u00d7 41 = 1,681.\n\nSubtracting: 72,900 - 1,681 = ?\n\nLet me compute that. 72,900 - 1,600 = 71,300. Then subtract 81 more: 71,300 - 81 = 71,219. Yep, same answer! That's a much quicker way. So that's clever.\n\nTherefore, the product is 71,219. Let me just confirm once more with another method to be absolutely sure.\n\nAlternatively, I can use a calculator, but since I don't have one, perhaps do the multiplication step by step again.\n\nLet me write it out again:\n\nMultiplying 229 \u00d7 311.\n\nBreakdown:\n\nFirst, 229 \u00d7 1 (units place) = 229.\n\nThen 229 \u00d7 1 (tens place) shifted one to the left: 2290.\n\nThen 229 \u00d7 3 (hundreds place) shifted two to the left: 229 \u00d7 3 = 687, so 68700.\n\nAdding those three: 229 + 2290 = 2519; 2519 + 68700 = 71,219.\n\nAlternatively, if I do the multiplication vertically:\n\n\u2003\u2003229\n\u00d7\u00a0311\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u2003\u2003229 (229 \u00d7 1)\n\u20032290 (229 \u00d7 10)\n+68700 (229 \u00d7 300)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u200371219.\n\nYes, that's the same as before. So all methods converge to 71,219. I think that's solid. Therefore, the product of 229 and 311 is 71,219.\n\nBut wait, just to make sure, let me check with another algebraic identity. Let me write 311 as 300 +11, so:\n\n229 \u00d7 311 = 229 \u00d7 (300 +11) = 229\u00d7300 + 229\u00d711.\n\nWe know 229\u00d7300 is 68,700.\n\n229\u00d711: 229\u00d710 + 229\u00d71 = 2,290 + 229 = 2,519.\n\nSo adding 68,700 + 2,519 = 71,219 again. Yep.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use 229\u00d7300 = (200 +29)\u00d7300 = 200\u00d7300 +29\u00d7300 = 60,000 +8,700 = 68,700, same as before. So everything checks out.\n\nAlternatively, if I consider that 229 \u00d7 311 = 311 \u00d7 229 (commutative property), maybe compute 311 \u00d7 200 + 311 \u00d729.\n\n311\u00d7200 = 62,200.\n\n311\u00d729: Let's compute that. 300\u00d729 = 8,700 and 11\u00d729 = 319, so 8,700 + 319 = 9,019? Wait, no, wait: 311\u00d729. Wait, 311\u00d730 is 9,330, minus 311 gives 9,330 - 311 = 9,019. So 62,200 + 9,019 = 71,219 again. Perfect.\n\nAlright, so after multiple methods\u2014direct multiplication, breaking into components, using the difference of squares, verifying with distributive property\u2014all leading to the same result, I can be confident that the product is 71,219.\n\nJust to recap:\n\n- Standard algorithm gave 71,219.\n\n- Breaking into (270 -41)(270 +41)=270\u00b2 -41\u00b2=71,219.\n\n- Distributing over hundreds, tens, ones: same result.\n\n- Other breakdowns with different groupings also confirmed it.\n\nTherefore, unless I made the same mistake in all methods\u2014which is possible but unlikely\u2014the answer should be correct.\n\nWait a second, just a sanity check: 200\u00d7300 is 60,000. 229 is a bit more than 200, 311 is a bit more than 300, so the product should be a bit more than 60,000. 71,219 is indeed a bit more, so that makes sense. If it were, say, 7,000 or 700,000, that would be off, but 71k is reasonable.\n\nAlternatively, approximate: 230 \u00d7 300 = 69,000. Since 229 is 1 less than 230, and 311 is 11 more than 300. So the difference would be (230\u00d7300) - (1\u00d7300) + (229\u00d711). Wait, maybe overcomplicating, but approximately, 230\u00d7310 = 230\u00d7300 +230\u00d710 = 69,000 +2,300 =71,300. So 229\u00d7311 would be 230\u00d7311 -1\u00d7311 = 71,300 + (230\u00d71) -311 = Hmm, maybe better to think 230\u00d7311 = 230*(300+11)=230\u00d7300 +230\u00d711=69,000 +2,530=71,530. Then subtract 1\u00d7311 (since 229 is 230-1), so 71,530 -311=71,219. Exactly. So that also works. So that approximation method gives the exact answer, which reinforces that it's correct.\n\nTherefore, after all these cross-verifications, I can confidently say the product is 71,219.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 229 and 311 is \\boxed{71219}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 229 and 311, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy:\n\n1. **Standard Multiplication Algorithm:**\n   - Multiply 229 by 1 (units place): \\(229 \\times 1 = 229\\)\n   - Multiply 229 by 10 (tens place): \\(229 \\times 10 = 2290\\)\n   - Multiply 229 by 300 (hundreds place): \\(229 \\times 300 = 68700\\)\n   - Add the partial products:\n     \\[\n     \\begin{array}{r}\n      229 \\\\\n     +2290 \\\\\n     +68700 \\\\\n     \\hline\n      71219 \\\\\n     \\end{array}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Difference of Squares:**\n   - Recognize that 229 and 311 are symmetric around 270:\n     \\[\n     229 = 270 - 41 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 311 = 270 + 41\n     \\]\n   - Use the identity \\((a - b)(a + b) = a^2 - b^2\\):\n     \\[\n     (270 - 41)(270 + 41) = 270^2 - 41^2\n     \\]\n   - Calculate:\n     \\[\n     270^2 = 72900 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 41^2 = 1681\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     72900 - 1681 = 71219\n     \\]\n\n3. **Distributive Property:**\n   - Break down 311 into 300 + 10 + 1:\n     \\[\n     229 \\times (300 + 10 + 1) = 229 \\times 300 + 229 \\times 10 + 229 \\times 1\n     \\]\n   - Calculate each term:\n     \\[\n     229 \\times 300 = 68700, \\quad 229 \\times 10 = 2290, \\quad 229 \\times 1 = 229\n     \\]\n   - Sum the results:\n     \\[\n     68700 + 2290 + 229 = 71219\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 229 and 311 is \\(\\boxed{71219}\\).",
