      "text": "291,000 + 1,588 = 292,588? Wait, no, 291,000 + 1,588 would be 292,588? Wait, 291,000 + 1,000 is 292,000, plus 588 is 292,588. Hmm, but let me check again.\n\nWait, actually, 60,988 + 231,600:\n\nBreakdown:\n\n231,600 + 60,000 = 291,600  .\n\nThen add the remaining 988: 291,600 + 988 = 292,588. Yes, that's correct.\n\nWait, but let me verify with another method to be sure. Maybe I made a mistake in partial products.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can compute 772 \u00d7 379 using another approach, like the standard algorithm again.\n\nStarting over:\n\n772 \u00d7 379.\n\nLet me write it as:\n\n\u2003\u2003772  .\n\u00d7\u00a0379  .\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014.\n\nFirst step: multiply by 9 (units place):\n\n772 \u00d7 9: 2\u00d79=18, write down 8, carryover 1.\n\nThen 7\u00d79=63 +1=64, write down 4, carryover 6.\n\nThen 7\u00d79=63 +6=69. So first line is 6948.\n\nSecond step: multiply by 7 (tens place, so shift one position left):\n\n772 \u00d7 7: same as before, 2\u00d77=14, write 4, carryover 1.\n\n7\u00d77=49 +1=50, write 0, carryover 5.\n\n7\u00d77=49 +5=54. So that gives 5404. Since it's the tens place, shift one left: 54040.\n\nThird step: multiply by 3 (hundreds place, so shift two positions left):\n\n772 \u00d73: 2\u00d73=6, 7\u00d73=21, carryover 2, 7\u00d73=21 +2=23. So 2316, then shift two left: 231600.\n\nAdding all three: 6948 + 54040 = 60,988; 60,988 + 231,600 = 292,588. So that seems correct.\n\nWait, but just to be thorough, maybe I can check with another method, like the distributive property.\n\nLet me break down 379 into 300 + 70 +9 and 772 as 700 +70 +2.\n\nThen (700 +70 +2) \u00d7 (300 +70 +9).\n\nHmm, that might be tedious but let's try.\n\nMultiply each term:\n\nFirst, 700\u00d7300 = 210,000.\n\n700\u00d770 = 49,000.\n\n700\u00d79 = 6,300.\n\nThen 70\u00d7300 = 21,000.\n\n70\u00d770 = 4,900.\n\n70\u00d79 = 630.\n\nThen 2\u00d7300 = 600.\n\n2\u00d770 = 140.\n\n2\u00d79 = 18.\n\nNow add all these up:\n\n210,000 +49,000 = 259,000.\n\n259,000 +6,300 = 265,300.\n\n265,300 +21,000 = 286,300.\n\n286,300 +4,900 = 291,200.\n\n291,200 +630 = 291,830.\n\n291,830 +600 = 292,430.\n\n292,430 +140 = 292,570.\n\n292,570 +18 = 292,588.\n\nOkay, so that matches the previous result. So that gives me confidence that the answer is 292,588.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another method: 772 \u00d7 379.\n\nAlternatively, notice that 772 \u00d7 379 = 772 \u00d7 (400 - 21).\n\nWait, 400 -21 is 379. Let me see if that's easier.\n\nCompute 772\u00d7400 - 772\u00d721.\n\n772\u00d7400: 772 \u00d74 \u00d7100 = 3,088 \u00d7100 = 308,800.\n\n772\u00d721: Let's compute 772\u00d720 +772\u00d71 = 15,440 +772 = 16,212.\n\nSo subtract: 308,800 -16,212.\n\nLet me compute that: 308,800 - 16,000 = 292,800. Then subtract 212 more: 292,800 -212 = 292,588. Same answer again.\n\nHmm, so that method also gives the same result. So I think it's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard algorithm again but check the addition step once more.\n\nAdding 6948, 54040, and 231600.\n\nLet me add 6948 + 54040 first:\n\n6948 + 54040:\n\n54040 + 6000 = 60040, then + 948 = 60988. Then adding 231600:\n\n231600 + 60,988.\n\n231,600 + 60,000 = 291,600; 291,600 + 988 = 292,588. Yep.\n\nAlternatively, using calculator-like approach: 772 \u00d7 379.\n\nWait, maybe multiply step by step:\n\nFirst, 700\u00d7300 = 210,000.\n\n700\u00d770 = 49,000.\n\n700\u00d79 = 6,300.\n\n70\u00d7300 = 21,000.\n\n70\u00d770 = 4,900.\n\n70\u00d79 = 630.\n\n2\u00d7300=600.\n\n2\u00d770=140.\n\n2\u00d79=18.\n\nAdding all these up gives the same as before.\n\nAlternatively, another way: 772 \u00d7 379 = (700 + 72) \u00d7 379.\n\nCompute 700\u00d7379 + 72\u00d7379.\n\n700\u00d7379: 700\u00d7300=210,000; 700\u00d779=55,300. So total 210,000 +55,300=265,300.\n\nWait, actually, 700\u00d7379 is 700\u00d7(300+79)=700\u00d7300 +700\u00d779.\n\nBut 700\u00d779: 700\u00d770=49,000 and 700\u00d79=6,300. So total 49,000+6,300=55,300. So 210,000 +55,300=265,300.\n\nThen 72\u00d7379. Let's compute that.\n\n72\u00d7300=21,600.\n\n72\u00d770=5,040.\n\n72\u00d79=648.\n\nAdding those: 21,600 +5,040 =26,640 +648=27,288.\n\nSo total is 265,300 +27,288=292,588. Same result again.\n\nOkay, so all methods are converging to 292,588. I think that's solid. Therefore, the product of 772 and 379 is 292,588.\n\nWait, but just to be extra sure, maybe do a quick estimation to see if it's in the ballpark. 772 is approximately 800, and 379 is approximately 400. 800\u00d7400 is 320,000. Our answer is 292,588, which is a bit less, which makes sense because we rounded both numbers up. So it seems plausible.\n\nAlternatively, 772 is 28 less than 800, and 379 is 21 less than 400. The difference would be (800\u00d7400) - (28\u00d7400 + 21\u00d7800 - 28\u00d721). Wait, that's getting complicated, but roughly, the adjustment would be subtracting (28\u00d7400 +21\u00d7800). Let's see:\n\n28\u00d7400=11,200 and 21\u00d7800=16,800. Total to subtract is 11,200 +16,800=28,000. So 320,000 -28,000=292,000. Which is close to our exact answer of 292,588. The difference is because of the overlapping subtraction term (28\u00d721). Since we subtracted that twice, we need to add it back once. 28\u00d721=588. So 292,000 +588=292,588. Exactly! So that matches perfectly. So that confirms the answer is correct.\n\nAlright, so after multiple methods and checks, I'm confident that 772 multiplied by 379 is 292,588.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 772 and 379 is \\boxed{292588}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 772 and 379, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify the result through multiple methods.\n\nFirst, we set up the multiplication vertically:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   772 \\\\\n\\times 379 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n**Step 1: Multiply 772 by 9 (units place):**\n\n\\[\n772 \\times 9 = 6948\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Multiply 772 by 70 (tens place):**\n\n\\[\n772 \\times 7 = 5404 \\quad \\text{(then add a zero)} \\quad \\rightarrow 54040\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Multiply 772 by 300 (hundreds place):**\n\n\\[\n772 \\times 3 = 2316 \\quad \\text{(then add two zeros)} \\quad \\rightarrow 231600\n\\]\n\n**Step 4: Add all partial products:**\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n    6948 \\\\\n  +54040 \\\\\n+231600 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nAdding step-by-step:\n\n1. \\(6948 + 54040 = 60988\\)\n2. \\(60988 + 231600 = 292588\\)\n\n**Verification using the distributive property:**\n\nBreak down the numbers:\n\n\\[\n(700 + 70 + 2) \\times (300 + 70 + 9)\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term and sum them up:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&700 \\times 300 = 210000, \\\\\n&700 \\times 70 = 49000, \\\\\n&700 \\times 9 = 6300, \\\\\n&70 \\times 300 = 21000, \\\\\n&70 \\times 70 = 4900, \\\\\n&70 \\times 9 = 630, \\\\\n&2 \\times 300 = 600, \\\\\n&2 \\times 70 = 140, \\\\\n&2 \\times 9 = 18.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nSumming these results:\n\n\\[\n210000 + 49000 + 6300 + 21000 + 4900 + 630 + 600 + 140 + 18 = 292588\n\\]\n\n**Verification using another method:**\n\n\\[\n772 \\times 379 = 772 \\times (400 - 21) = 772 \\times 400 - 772 \\times 21\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n772 \\times 400 &= 308800, \\\\\n772 \\times 21 &= 16212.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nSubtract:\n\n\\[\n308800 - 16212 = 292588\n\\]\n\nAll methods confirm the result is \\(\\boxed{292588}\\).",
