hat also gives 190,816. So that confirms the result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using calculator math, but since this is a thought process, I should stick to manual calculations.\n\nAlternatively, another way is to use the standard algorithm again but more carefully.\n\nWait, let me try multiplying 356 \u00d7 536 using the standard vertical method step by step again.\n\nFirst, writing 356 \u00d7 536.\n\nMultiply 356 by 6 (units): 2136.\n\nMultiply 356 by 30 (tens): 10,680.\n\nMultiply 356 by 500 (hundreds): 178,000.\n\nAdd them together:\n\n2136 + 10,680 = 12,816.\n\n12,816 + 178,000 = 190,816. Same result.\n\nHmm, so that's consistent. Maybe I can also check with another method, like estimating?\n\n356 is approximately 350, and 536 is approximately 540. 350\u00d7540 = 350\u00d7500 + 350\u00d740 = 175,000 + 14,000 = 189,000. The actual answer is 190,816, which is a bit higher, which makes sense because I rounded down both numbers. So that seems reasonable.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps breaking into (300+56)(500+36). Let me see:\n\n(300 + 56)(500 + 36) = 300\u00d7500 + 300\u00d736 + 56\u00d7500 + 56\u00d736.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n300\u00d7500 = 150,000.\n\n300\u00d736 = 10,800.\n\n56\u00d7500 = 28,000.\n\n56\u00d736 = let's compute that: 50\u00d736=1,800, 6\u00d736=216; total 1,800+216=2,016.\n\nAdding them all together:\n\n150,000 + 10,800 = 160,800.\n\n160,800 + 28,000 = 188,800.\n\n188,800 + 2,016 = 190,816. Same result again.\n\nOkay, so all methods are giving me 190,816, so I think that's the correct product. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, so I'm confident that's the right answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 356 and 536 is \\boxed{190816}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 356 and 536, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm by breaking down the multiplication into partial products and then summing them up.\n\nFirst, we multiply 356 by each digit of 536, starting from the rightmost digit:\n\n1. **Multiply 356 by 6 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   356 \\times 6 = 2136\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 356 by 30 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   356 \\times 30 = 10680\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 356 by 500 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   356 \\times 500 = 178000\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the partial products:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n    2136 \\\\\n  + 10680 \\\\\n+ 178000 \\\\\n\\hline\n  190816 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBreaking down the addition step-by-step:\n- Adding 2136 and 10680:\n  \\[\n  2136 + 10680 = 12816\n  \\]\n- Adding the result to 178000:\n  \\[\n  12816 + 178000 = 190816\n  \\]\n\nThus, the product of 356 and 536 is \\(\\boxed{190816}\\).",
