 +28,800 -3,000 -216 = 400,000 +25,584 = 425,584. Exactly the same. So that's a good check.\n\nTherefore, I can be confident that 794 multiplied by 536 is indeed 425,584.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 794 and 536 is \\boxed{425584}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 794 and 536, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 794 by 6 (the units place of 536):**\n   \\[\n   794 \\times 6 = 4764\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 794 by 30 (the tens place of 536, which is 3 \u00d7 10):**\n   \\[\n   794 \\times 3 = 2382 \\quad \\text{(then add a zero)} \\quad 23820\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 794 by 500 (the hundreds place of 536, which is 5 \u00d7 100):**\n   \\[\n   794 \\times 5 = 3970 \\quad \\text{(then add two zeros)} \\quad 397000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   4764 + 23820 + 397000\n   \\]\n\n   - Adding the first two partial products:\n     \\[\n     4764 + 23820 = 28584\n     \\]\n   - Adding the result to the third partial product:\n     \\[\n     28584 + 397000 = 425584\n     \\]\n\n5. **Verification using the distributive property:**\n   \\[\n   (800 - 6) \\times 536 = 800 \\times 536 - 6 \\times 536\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   800 \\times 536 = 428800 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 6 \\times 536 = 3216\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   428800 - 3216 = 425584\n   \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 794 and 536 is \\(\\boxed{425584}\\).",
