rtial product:   9820.\n\nThird partial product: 441,900.\n\nAdding them together. Let me line them up properly:.\n\n        491.\n\n      + 9820.\n\n    +441900.\n\n------------.\n\nStarting with the first two: 491 + 9820. Let's see: 491 + 9820. 491 + 9000 is 9491, then +820? Wait, no. Wait, 9820 is 9 thousands, 8 hundreds, 2 tens. 491 is 4 hundreds, 9 tens, 1 one. Adding 491 + 9820:.\n\nUnits place: 1 + 0 = 1.\n\nTens place: 9 + 2 = 11, write down 1 and carry over 1.\n\nHundreds place: 4 + 8 + 1 (carry) = 13, write down 3 and carry over 1.\n\nThousands place: 0 + 9 + 1 (carry) = 10, so write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 0 + 0 + 1 (carry) = 1.\n\nWait, that gives 10,311? Wait, let me check again. Wait, 491 + 9820:.\n\n491.\n\n+9820.\n\n= ?.\n\nLet me do it step by step:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 1 + 0 = 1.\n\nTens: 9 + 2 = 11, write 1, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds: 4 + 8 = 12, plus the carried 1 is 13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nThousands: 0 (from 491) + 9 (from 9820) = 9, plus the carried 1 is 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands: 0 + 0 + carried 1 = 1.\n\nSo the total is 10,311. Wait, but 491 + 9820 is 10,311? Let me check with another method. 9820 + 491: 9820 + 400 is 10,220, plus 91 is 10,311. Yes, that's correct.\n\nNow add that to the third partial product, which is 441,900.\n\nSo 10,311 + 441,900.\n\nAdding those together:.\n\n10,311.\n\n+441,900.\n\n= ?.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 1 + 0 = 1.\n\nTens: 1 + 0 = 1.\n\nHundreds: 3 + 9 = 12, write 2, carryover 1.\n\nThousands: 0 + 1 + 1 (carryover) = 2.\n\nTen-thousands: 1 (from 10,311) + 4 (from 441,900) = 5.\n\nHundred-thousands: 4 from the 441,900.\n\nWait, maybe better to write it out:.\n\n441,900.\n\n+  10,311. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
