{(then add a zero)} \\quad 16240\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 406 by 500 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   406 \\times 5 = 2030 \\quad \\text{(then add two zeros)} \\quad 203000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     1218 \\\\\n   + 16240 \\\\\n   + 203000 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     220458 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\nTo verify, we use the distributive property:\n\\[\n(400 + 6)(500 + 40 + 3) = 400 \\cdot 500 + 400 \\cdot 40 + 400 \\cdot 3 + 6 \\cdot 500 + 6 \\cdot 40 + 6 \\cdot 3\n\\]\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n400 \\cdot 500 &= 200000, \\\\\n400 \\cdot 40 &= 16000, \\\\\n400 \\cdot 3 &= 1200, \\\\\n6 \\cdot 500 &= 3000, \\\\\n6 \\cdot 40 &= 240, \\\\\n6 \\cdot 3 &= 18.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nAdding these together:\n\\[\n200000 + 16000 + 1200 + 3000 + 240 + 18 = 220458\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 406 and 543 is \\boxed{220458}.",
