ther way to check.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps using calculator approximation? Since I can't use a calculator, but maybe do an approximate check.\n\nIf I round 372 to 370 and 838 to 840, then 370*840 = ?\n\n370*800 = 296,000.\n\n370*40=14,800.\n\nTotal is 296,000 +14,800 =310,800. The actual answer is 311,736 which is about 936 more, which is reasonable because we rounded 372 up to 370 (which is actually lower, so maybe my rounding was off). Wait, 372 is 370 +2, and 838 is 840 -2. So the approximate would be (370)(840) = 310,800. The actual is (370+2)(840-2) =370*840 -370*2 +2*840 -2*2 =310,800 -740 +1,680 -4= 310,800 +940 -4= 311,736. Exactly. So that's a perfect check. So that method gives exactly the same answer. So that must be correct.\n\nTherefore, I can be confident that the product of 372 and 838 is 311,736.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 372 and 838 is \\boxed{311736}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 372 and 838, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 372 by 8 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     372 \\\\\n   \\times \\ 8 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     2976 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   Calculation:\n   - \\(2 \\times 8 = 16\\) (write 6, carry over 1)\n   - \\(7 \\times 8 + 1 = 57\\) (write 7, carry over 5)\n   - \\(3 \\times 8 + 5 = 29\\) (write 29)\n   Result: 2976\n\n2. **Multiply 372 by 3 (tens place, so shift one position left):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     372 \\\\\n   \\times \\ 30 \\\\\n   \\hline\n    11160 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   Calculation:\n   - \\(2 \\times 3 = 6\\)\n   - \\(7 \\times 3 = 21\\) (write 1, carry over 2)\n   - \\(3 \\times 3 + 2 = 11\\) (write 11)\n   Result: 1116 (shifted to 11160)\n\n3. **Multiply 372 by 8 (hundreds place, so shift two positions left):**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     372 \\\\\n   \\times \\ 800 \\\\\n   \\hline\n   297600 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   Calculation:\n   - \\(372 \\times 8 = 2976\\) (shifted to 297600)\n\n4. **Add all partial products:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     2976 \\\\\n   + 11160 \\\\\n   +297600 \\\\\n   \\hline\n    311736 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   - First, add 2976 and 11160:\n     \\[\n     2976 + 11160 = 14136\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to 297600:\n     \\[\n     14136 + 297600 = 311736\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 372 and 838 is \\(\\boxed{311736}\\).",
