ng those together: 20.32 + 1.016 = 21.336.\n\nTherefore, 21.336 \u00d710^4 = 213,360. Exactly the same result. So that's another method, converting to scientific notation and multiplying the coefficients, then adjusting the exponent. That also gives the same answer.\n\nHmm, so all these different methods are confirming that the product is 213,360. That gives me more confidence that this is the correct answer.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check using a calculator? Wait, but since I don't have a calculator here, but I can do a rough estimate to see if it makes sense.\n\nEstimate: 400 \u00d7 500 = 200,000.\n\nBut since 420 is 20 more than 400, and 508 is 8 more than 500, the actual product should be a bit more than 200,000. Our answer is 213,360, which is 13,360 more. Let's see:\n\nThe difference from 400\u00d7500 to 420\u00d7508 is the extra from both numbers. The approximate increase can be calculated as (420-400)*500 + 400*(508-500) + (20)*(8). That is, adding the extra from each term plus the cross term.\n\nSo, 20\u00d7500 = 10,000,\n\n400\u00d78 = 3,200,\n\nand 20\u00d78= 160. Adding those together: 10,000 +3,200=13,200 +160=13,360. So total added to the original 200,000 is 13,360, which gives 213,360. Exactly the same.\n\nTherefore, the estimation method also confirms that.\n\nHmm, so all these cross-checks are making me feel confident that 213,360 is indeed the correct product of 420 and 508. I think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, and all methods converge to the same number. So I can be pretty sure that's the right answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 420 and 508 is \\boxed{213360}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 420 and 508, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into smaller parts:\n\n1. Break down the numbers:\n   - \\( 420 = 400 + 20 \\)\n   - \\( 508 = 500 + 8 \\)\n\n2. Apply the distributive property:\n   \\[\n   (400 + 20) \\times (500 + 8)\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply each part separately:\n  