 = 248,136. Yep.\n\nI think that's thorough enough. All methods are converging to the same result. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. So the product of 588 and 422 is 248,136.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 588 and 422 is \\boxed{248136}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 588 and 422, we can break down the multiplication using the distributive property:\n\n1. **Break down 422 into its components**:\n   - 422 = 400 + 20 + 2\n\n2. **Multiply 588 by each component**:\n   - \\(588 \\times 2 = 1,176\\)\n   - \\(588 \\times 20 = 11,760\\)\n   - \\(588 \\times 400 = 235,200\\)\n\n3. **Add the results together**:\n   - First, add \\(1,176 + 11,760\\):\n     \\[\n     1,176 + 11,760 = 12,936\n     \\]\n   - Then, add the result to \\(235,200\\):\n     \\[\n     12,936 + 235,200 = 248,136\n     \\]\n\n4. **Verification using different methods**:\n   - **Distributive property expansion**:\n     \\[\n     (500 + 80 + 8)(400 + 20 + 2)\n     \\]\n     Calculating each term and summing them gives the same result, 248,136.\n   - **Division check**:\n     \\[\n     248,136 \\div 588 = 422\n     \\]\n     Confirms the multiplication is correct.\n\nThus, the product of 588 and 422 is \\(\\boxed{248136}\\).",
