messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 850 and 130?', '<think>:.\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 850 and 130. Hmm, let me think about how to approach this. Multiplying large numbers can sometimes be tricky, but maybe breaking it down into smaller parts will help. Let me start by writing down the numbers: 850 and 130. .\n\nFirst, I remember that multiplying by 100 is straightforward, so maybe I can use that to simplify. Let me see, 130 is the same as 100 + 30. So, if I break it down like that, I can use the distributive property. That would mean 850 times 100 plus 850 times 30. .\n\nCalculating 850 times 100 first. Well, multiplying by 100 just adds two zeros to the end of the number. So 850 with two more zeros would be 85,000. That part seems easy enough.\n\nNow, the next part is 850 times 30. Hmm, 30 is 3 times 10, so maybe I can do 850 times 3 first and then multiply by 10. Let me try that. 850 times 3. Breaking that down further: 800 times 3 is 2,400, and 50 times 3 is 150. Adding those together gives 2,400 + 150 = 2,550. Then, multiplying by 10 gives 25,500. .\n\nSo now I have both parts: 85,000 and 25,500. Adding those together should give the total product. Let me add them step by step. 85,000 plus 25,500. Starting with the thousands: 85,000 + 20,000 is 105,000. Therefore, my final answer is: ']]
