d 36*121 is 4,356. Adding those gives 108,900 +4,356 = 113,256. Exactly! So that's another way to verify. So that's the same answer. So I think that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the distributive property in another way. 936 x 121 = 936 x (120 +1) = 936x120 +936x1, which is exactly what I did first. So that gives the same result again. So I think 113,256 is correct.\n\nWait, just to make sure, let me try multiplying 936 by 121 step by step manually:\n\nStarting with the multiplication:\n\nFirst, write 936  \nMultiply by 1 (units place): 936  \nMultiply by 2 (tens place, so shifted one position to the left): 936 x 2 = 1,872, but since it's the tens place, it's actually 18,720  \nMultiply by 1 (hundreds place, shifted two positions to the left): 936 x 1 = 936, but shifted two places makes it 93,600  \nThen add all three:  \n936  \n+18,720  \n=19,656  \nThen 19,656 +93,600 = 113,256  \n\nYes, that's the same as before. So I think that's correct. I can't see any errors here, so I think the product of 936 and 121 is 113,256.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 936 and 121 is \\boxed{113256}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 936 and 121, we can break down the multiplication into simpler steps using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, we recognize that 121 can be decomposed into 120 + 1. Therefore, we calculate:\n\n\\[\n936 \\times 121 = 936 \\times (120 + 1) = (936 \\times 120) + (936 \\times 1)\n\\]\n\nCalculating \\(936 \\times 120\\):\n\n\\[\n936 \\times 120 = 936 \\times (12 \\times 10) = (936 \\times 12) \\times 10\n\\]\n\nBreaking down \\(936 \\times 12\\):\n\n\\[\n936 \\times 12 = 936 \\times (10 + 2) = (936 \\times 10) + (936 \\times 2) = 9360 + 1872 = 11232\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\n936 \\times 120 = 11232 \\times 10 = 112320\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(936 \\times 1\\):\n\n\\[\n936 \\times 1 = 936\n\\]\n\nAdding the two results together:\n\n\\[\n112320 + 936 = 113256\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can also use the standard multiplication method:\n\n\\[\n\\begi