. **Compute each part**:\n   - \\(543 \\times 500 = 543 \\times 5 \\times 100 = 2715 \\times 100 = 271,\\!500\\)\n   - \\(543 \\times 6 = 3,\\!258\\)\n\n3. **Add the results**:\n   \\[\n   271,\\!500 + 3,\\!258 = 274,\\!758\n   \\]\n\n4. **Verification using standard algorithm**:\n   ```\n     543  \n   \u00d7 506  \n   \u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014  \n     3258  (543 \u00d7 6)  \n    0000   (543 \u00d7 0, shifted left by 1)  \n   271500  (543 \u00d7 5, shifted left by 2)  \n   \u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014  \n   274,758\n   ```\n\n5. **Prime factorization cross-check**:\n   - \\(543 = 3 \\times 181\\)\n   - \\(506 = 2 \\times 11 \\times 23\\)\n   - Combined: \\(3 \\times 181 \\times 2 \\times 11 \\times 23 = 274,\\!758\\)\n\n**Final Answer**:  \nThe product of 543 and 506 is \\boxed{274758}.",
