y 6 (units place of 896):**\n   \\[\n   613 \\times 6 = 3678\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 613 by 9 (tens place of 896, shifted one position to the left):**\n   \\[\n   613 \\times 9 = 5517 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by one digit gives 55170)}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 613 by 8 (hundreds place of 896, shifted two positions to the left):**\n   \\[\n   613 \\times 8 = 4904 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by two digits gives 490400)}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   3678 + 55170 + 490400\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add \\(3678 + 55170\\):\n     \\[\n     3678 + 55170 = 58848\n     \\]\n\n   - Then add the result to \\(490400\\):\n     \\[\n     58848 + 490400 = 549248\n     \\]\n\nTo verify, we can use the distributive property:\n\\[\n613 \\times 896 = 613 \\times (900 - 4) = 613 \\times 900 - 613 \\times 4\n\\]\n\\[\n613 \\times 900 = 551700 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 613 \\times 4 = 2452\n\\]\n\\[\n551700 - 2452 = 549248\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the product is \\(\\boxed{549248}\\).",
